INSERT INTO _s459 VALUES
(4258,62,1,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). The Father seats the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge. *They shall call his name Immanuel, which being interpreted is, Elohim (God) with us* (Matthew 1:23) — the enthroned one is the one who came in flesh.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(4259,69,26,69,26,$n$*And there was great joy amongst them, And they blessed and glorified and extolled Because the name of that Son of Adam had been revealed unto them.* (1 Enoch 69:26). *Thou shalt call his name Yahusha (Jesus): for he shall save his people from their sins* (Matthew 1:21). The name revealed to the holy ones in heaven, to their joy, is the name given on earth to the child. The name is the gospel.$n$,$n$And there was great joy amongst them, And they blessed and glorified and extolled Because the name of that Son of Adam had been revealed unto them.$n$),
(4274,90,20,90,37,$n$*And I saw that a white bull was born, with large horns, and all the beasts of the field and all the birds of the air feared him and made petition to him all the time.* (1 Enoch 90:37). The Animal Apocalypse ends where the Magi's watch ends: a white bull born at the close of the vision, large-horned, feared and petitioned by every beast and bird — the seed of Adam restored in one figure. *Where is he that is born King of the Yahudim (Jews)? for we have seen his star in the east* (Matthew 2:2). The men who read the heavens were looking for the one this vision had already shown.$n$,$n$And I saw that a white bull was born, with large horns, and all the beasts of the field and all the birds of the air feared him and made petition to him all the time.$n$),
(4275,90,21,90,38,$n$*And I saw till all their generations were transformed, and they all became white bulls; and the first among them became a lamb, and that lamb became a great animal and had great black horns on its head; and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced over it and over all the oxen.* (1 Enoch 90:38). The lamb that becomes the great horned one — the Lamb who is also the King. The star of Matthew 2:2 announced a child; the vision had already shown what the child would be: the lamb grown into the one the Lord of the sheep rejoices over.$n$,$n$And I saw till all their generations were transformed, and they all became white bulls; and the first among them became a lamb, and that lamb became a great animal and had great black horns on its head; and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced over it and over all the oxen.$n$),
(4292,14,15,14,18,$n$*And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* (1 Enoch 14:18). This is the room the open heaven of Matthew 3:16 gives onto — the lofty throne, the cherubim, the fire streaming from beneath it (1 Enoch 14:18–22). The heavens do not open onto emptiness; they open onto the throne of the Great Glory, and from that throne the voice of the next verse speaks.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(4293,71,1,71,1,$n$*And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* (1 Enoch 71:1). The ascent that ends in the Head of Days naming the Son of Adam (1 Enoch 71:14) begins here, with the heavens opened to Enoch. At the Yarden (Jordan) the same heavens open and the same Father speaks over the same Son.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$),
(4298,39,5,40,5,$n$*And the second voice I heard blessing the Elect One and the elect ones who hang upon Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 40:5). *And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son* (Matthew 3:17). Enoch heard two voices in the throne room: the first blessing Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits (1 Enoch 40:4), the second blessing the Elect One. The Father's voice at the river and the heaven's blessing of the Elect One speak of the same Son.$n$,$n$And the second voice I heard blessing the Elect One and the elect ones who hang upon Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(4299,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased* (Matthew 3:17). Enoch had already heard the Father name him: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* The voice at the river is the voice from the throne; the Son it names is the one righteousness never leaves.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(4323,5,7,1,8,$n$*But with the righteous He will make peace. And will protect the elect, And mercy shall be upon them. And they shall all belong to Elohim (God), And they shall be prospered, And they shall all be blessed. And He will help them all, And light shall appear unto them, And He will make peace with them.* (1 Enoch 1:8). *Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 5:3). The blessing is not an entry fee; it is the Father's own word over those who are already his. Enoch heard the same word before the Beatitudes were spoken: peace, protection, mercy, belonging — pronounced over the elect, not offered to applicants.$n$,$n$But with the righteous He will make peace. And will protect the elect, And mercy shall be upon them. And they shall all belong to Elohim (God), And they shall be prospered, And they shall all be blessed. And He will help them all, And light shall appear unto them, And He will make peace with them.$n$),
(4328,58,3,58,3,$n$*And the righteous shall be in the light of the sun, And the elect in the light of eternal life: The days of their life shall be unending, And the days of the holy without number.* (1 Enoch 58:3). *Ye are the light of the world* (Matthew 5:14) — not *become*; *are.* Enoch says why: the righteous are set in the light of the sun and the elect in the light of eternal life. The light the disciples carry is the light they were placed in.$n$,$n$And the righteous shall be in the light of the sun, And the elect in the light of eternal life: The days of their life shall be unending, And the days of the holy without number.$n$),
(4329,38,4,38,4,$n$*From that time those that possess the earth shall no longer be powerful and exalted: And they shall not be able to behold the face of the holy, For Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits has caused His light to appear On the face of the holy, righteous, and elect.* (1 Enoch 38:4). *A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid* (Matthew 5:14). Enoch saw the day the light appears on the face of the holy, righteous and elect, and the powerful can no longer behold it. The disciples on the mountain are the first sight of that city; the light that makes it visible is the Lord of Spirits' own.$n$,$n$From that time those that possess the earth shall no longer be powerful and exalted: And they shall not be able to behold the face of the holy, For Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits has caused His light to appear On the face of the holy, righteous, and elect.$n$),
(4330,38,2,38,2,$n$*And when the Righteous One shall appear before the eyes of the righteous, Whose elect works hang upon Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And light shall appear to the righteous and the elect who dwell on the earth, Where then will be the dwelling of the sinners, And where the resting-place of those who have denied Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits? It had been good for them if they had not been born.* (1 Enoch 38:2). *Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 5:16). Enoch saw the day the light appears on the righteous and the elect who dwell on the earth — and the question that day asks of the sinners. The shining is the Father's doing; the glory goes to him.$n$,$n$And when the Righteous One shall appear before the eyes of the righteous, Whose elect works hang upon Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And light shall appear to the righteous and the elect who dwell on the earth, Where then will be the dwelling of the sinners, And where the resting-place of those who have denied Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits? It had been good for them if they had not been born.$n$),
(4334,82,13,104,9,$n$*Be not godless in your hearts, and lie not and alter not the words of uprightness, nor charge with lying the words of the Holy Great One, nor take account of your idols; for all your lying and all your godlessness issue not in righteousness but in great sin.* (1 Enoch 104:9). Enoch's charge to his children is the charge Matthew 5:19 makes to every teacher: do not alter the words of uprightness. *Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so, he shall be called the least in the kingdom of heaven.* To alter the words and to teach men so are one act; both are named here before the gospel names them.$n$,$n$Be not godless in your hearts, and lie not and alter not the words of uprightness, nor charge with lying the words of the Holy Great One, nor take account of your idols; for all your lying and all your godlessness issue not in righteousness but in great sin.$n$),
(4335,95,2,104,10,$n$*And now I know this mystery, that sinners will alter and pervert the words of righteousness in many ways, and will speak wicked words, and lie, and practise great deceits, and write books concerning their words.* (1 Enoch 104:10). Enoch knew the mystery before the pulpit practised it: sinners will alter and pervert the words of righteousness, and write books about it. *Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so* (Matthew 5:19) — the teaching is the perverting; the books are the sermons. The kingdom-status of such teachers was fixed long before the sermon was preached.$n$,$n$And now I know this mystery, that sinners will alter and pervert the words of righteousness in many ways, and will speak wicked words, and lie, and practise great deceits, and write books concerning their words.$n$),
(4365,9,4,9,4,$n$*And they said to Yahuah (Lord) of the ages: ‘Lord of lords, Elohim (God) of gods, King of kings, and Elohim (God) of the ages, the throne of Thy glory (standeth) unto all the generations of the ages, and Thy name holy and glorious and blessed unto all the ages!* (1 Enoch 9:4). Enoch's angels pray what the disciples are taught to pray: the holy and blessed name, the throne of glory that stands to all generations, the King of kings. *Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom come* (Matthew 6:9–10) is the same prayer in the mouth of the children.$n$,$n$And they said to Yahuah (Lord) of the ages: ‘Lord of lords, Elohim (God) of gods, King of kings, and Elohim (God) of the ages, the throne of Thy glory (standeth) unto all the generations of the ages, and Thy name holy and glorious and blessed unto all the ages!$n$),
(4366,84,2,84,2,$n$*‘Blessed be Thou, O Yahuah (Lord), King, Great and mighty in Thy greatness, Yahuah (Lord) of the whole creation of the heaven, King of kings and Elohim (God) of the whole world. And Thy power and kingship and greatness abide for ever and ever, And throughout all generations Thy dominion; And all the heavens are Thy throne for ever, And the whole earth Thy footstool for ever and ever.* (1 Enoch 84:2). *Hallowed be thy name* (Matthew 6:9). Enoch's own prayer blesses the King whose dominion is through all generations and whose throne is the heavens. The disciples are taught to pray what the patriarch prayed.$n$,$n$‘Blessed be Thou, O Yahuah (Lord), King, Great and mighty in Thy greatness, Yahuah (Lord) of the whole creation of the heaven, King of kings and Elohim (God) of the whole world. And Thy power and kingship and greatness abide for ever and ever, And throughout all generations Thy dominion; And all the heavens are Thy throne for ever, And the whole earth Thy footstool for ever and ever.$n$),
(4367,84,3,9,5,$n$*Thou hast made all things, and power over all things hast Thou: and all things are naked and open in Thy sight, and Thou seest all things, and nothing can hide itself from Thee.* (1 Enoch 9:5). The One whose kingdom the disciples pray to come is the One who made all things and holds power over all things, from whom nothing hides. *Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven* (Matthew 6:10) asks nothing new; it asks that what is already true in heaven be seen on earth.$n$,$n$Thou hast made all things, and power over all things hast Thou: and all things are naked and open in Thy sight, and Thou seest all things, and nothing can hide itself from Thee.$n$),
(4377,94,1,94,1,$n$*And now I say unto you, my sons, love righteousness and walk therein; For the paths of righteousness are worthy of acceptation, But the paths of unrighteousness shall suddenly be destroyed and vanish.* (1 Enoch 94:1). Two ways, and only two. Enoch sets them before his sons — the paths of righteousness worthy of acceptance, the paths of unrighteousness that vanish — long before Matthew 7:13's *wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction.* The choice at Deuteronomy 30:19 was already old when Enoch taught it.$n$,$n$And now I say unto you, my sons, love righteousness and walk therein; For the paths of righteousness are worthy of acceptation, But the paths of unrighteousness shall suddenly be destroyed and vanish.$n$),
(4378,94,2,94,2,$n$*And to certain men of a generation shall the paths of violence and of death be revealed, And they shall hold themselves afar from them, And shall not follow them.* (1 Enoch 94:2). Enoch sees it from the other side: the paths of violence and death are shown to certain men of a generation, and they keep far from them. *Strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it* (Matthew 7:14). The few who hold themselves afar are the few who find.$n$,$n$And to certain men of a generation shall the paths of violence and of death be revealed, And they shall hold themselves afar from them, And shall not follow them.$n$),
(4386,90,18,90,33,$n$*And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.* (1 Enoch 90:33). *Many shall come from the east and west, and shall sit down with Avraham (Abraham), and Yitschaq (Isaac), and Ya'aqov (Jacob), in the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 8:11). Enoch saw the sitting-down: all that had been destroyed and dispersed assembled in the house, and the Lord of the sheep rejoicing because they had returned. The many from east and west are the dispersed of the house coming home — the scattered sheep, not a new flock.$n$,$n$And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.$n$),
(4391,46,2,46,2,$n$*And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?* (1 Enoch 46:2). Enoch asks who *that Son of Adam* is — a figure named by title, standing beside the Head of Days. When Yahusha (Jesus) says *the Son of Adam hath not where to lay his head* (Matthew 8:20) he takes that title for himself: the named one of the Parables, now with no bed on the earth he came to.$n$,$n$And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?$n$),
(4395,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). The spirits that met him among the tombs are named here by origin and by work: the spirits of the giants, afflicting and destroying, hungering and thirsting without food. The two possessed men of Matthew 8:28, *exceeding fierce, so that no man might pass by that way,* were under exactly this.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(4411,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *The Son of Adam hath power on earth to forgive sins* (Matthew 9:6). The Parables had already named him the one born unto righteousness, over whom righteousness abides; the forgiveness he speaks on earth is that abiding righteousness exercised in flesh.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(4424,90,16,90,25,$n$*And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.* (1 Enoch 90:25). The shepherds who were set over the sheep and destroyed more than they were bidden end here, judged and cast into the fiery abyss. When Yahusha (Jesus) saw the multitudes *as sheep having no shepherd* (Matthew 9:36), he was looking at the flock those shepherds had left; the vision had already recorded their sentence.$n$,$n$And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.$n$),
(4425,90,17,90,29,$n$*And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.* (1 Enoch 90:29). The shepherdless sheep of Matthew 9:36 are not left shepherdless. Enoch saw the Lord of the sheep bring a new house, greater and loftier than the first, with all the sheep within it. The compassion that moved him at the sight of the scattered flock is the compassion that builds the house.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.$n$),
(4426,90,18,90,33,$n$*And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.* (1 Enoch 90:33). *When he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad* (Matthew 9:36). Enoch saw where the scattering ends: all that had been destroyed and dispersed assembled in the house, and the Lord of the sheep rejoicing because they had returned.$n$,$n$And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.$n$),
(4453,103,3,104,1,$n$*I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.* (1 Enoch 104:1). *Whosoever therefore shall confess me before men, him will I confess also before my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 10:32). Enoch swears to the righteous that their names are already written before the glory of the Great One. The Son confesses before the Father the ones whose names were written before they ever confessed.$n$,$n$I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.$n$),
(4454,103,8,103,4,$n$*And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.* (1 Enoch 103:4). *But whosoever shall deny me before men, him will I also deny before my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 10:33). Enoch's word to the righteous who die in righteousness is that their memorial does not perish before the Great One. The warning of Matthew 10:33 is the other side of that promise: a memorial can be kept, and a name can be blotted out (1 Enoch 108:3). The denier is not a tare who never had a name; he is wheat that did not endure.$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$),
(4461,5,7,1,8,$n$*But with the righteous He will make peace. And will protect the elect, And mercy shall be upon them. And they shall all belong to Elohim (God), And they shall be prospered, And they shall all be blessed. And He will help them all, And light shall appear unto them, And He will make peace with them.* (1 Enoch 1:8). The answer sent to Yochanan (John) — *the blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, and the dead are raised up, and the poor have the gospel preached to them* (Matthew 11:5) — is the peace, protection, mercy, and light Enoch saw promised to the righteous, now arriving in flesh.$n$,$n$But with the righteous He will make peace. And will protect the elect, And mercy shall be upon them. And they shall all belong to Elohim (God), And they shall be prospered, And they shall all be blessed. And He will help them all, And light shall appear unto them, And He will make peace with them.$n$),
(4462,10,17,10,17,$n$*And then shall all the righteous escape, And shall live till they beget thousands of children, And all the days of their youth and their old age Shall they complete in peace.* (1 Enoch 10:17). Enoch saw the days when the righteous escape and complete their years in peace, the earth tilled in righteousness and cleansed of oppression (1 Enoch 10:17–22). The works Yahusha (Jesus) lists for Yochanan (John) at Matthew 11:5 are the first fruits of those days — the age Enoch saw, beginning.$n$,$n$And then shall all the righteous escape, And shall live till they beget thousands of children, And all the days of their youth and their old age Shall they complete in peace.$n$),
(4501,95,7,95,7,$n$*Woe to you, sinners, for ye persecute the righteous; For ye shall be delivered up and persecuted because of injustice, And heavy shall its yoke be upon you.* (1 Enoch 95:7). *Then the Pharisees went out, and held a council against him, how they might destroy him* (Matthew 12:14). Enoch's woe already names them: sinners who persecute the righteous, and the heavy yoke that waits for them. The council against the Righteous One is the act the woe was written for.$n$,$n$Woe to you, sinners, for ye persecute the righteous; For ye shall be delivered up and persecuted because of injustice, And heavy shall its yoke be upon you.$n$),
(4504,62,2,62,2,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.* (1 Enoch 62:2). *Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him, and he shall shew judgment to the Gentiles* (Matthew 12:18). Enoch saw the same: the spirit of righteousness poured out on the Elect One seated on the throne, and the word of his mouth bringing judgment. The servant of Isaiah and the Elect One of the Parables are one figure, and the Spirit upon him is the same Spirit.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.$n$),
(4512,65,11,65,11,$n$*And these—they have no place of repentance for ever, because they have shown them what was hidden, and they are the damned: but as for thee, my son, Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits knows that thou art pure, and guiltless of this reproach concerning the secrets.* (1 Enoch 65:11). *But the blasphemy against the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Ghost) shall not be forgiven unto men* (Matthew 12:32). Enoch heard the sentence on those who showed what was hidden and became the damned: no place of repentance for ever. There is a sin that closes the door from the inside; the Pharisees who called the Spirit's work the work of Beelzebub stood at that door.$n$,$n$And these—they have no place of repentance for ever, because they have shown them what was hidden, and they are the damned: but as for thee, my son, Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits knows that thou art pure, and guiltless of this reproach concerning the secrets.$n$),
(4526,48,7,48,7,$n$*And the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath revealed him to the holy and righteous; For he hath preserved the lot of the righteous, Because they have hated and despised this world of unrighteousness, And have hated all its works and ways in the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits: For in his name they are saved, And according to his good pleasure hath it been in regard to their life.* (1 Enoch 48:7). *Because it is given unto you to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to them it is not given* (Matthew 13:11). Enoch says who the *you* are: the holy and righteous to whom the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits reveals him, who have hated this world of unrighteousness. The revealing follows the belonging; it does not create it.$n$,$n$And the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath revealed him to the holy and righteous; For he hath preserved the lot of the righteous, Because they have hated and despised this world of unrighteousness, And have hated all its works and ways in the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits: For in his name they are saved, And according to his good pleasure hath it been in regard to their life.$n$),
(4531,19,1,19,1,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). *Then cometh the wicked one, and catcheth away that which was sown in his heart* (Matthew 13:19). Enoch names the spirits of the Watchers assuming many forms, leading mankind astray — the actor behind the catching-away. He is not a figure of speech; the restored library records his origin and his end.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$),
(4536,10,9,10,9,$n$*And to Gabriel said Yahuah (Lord): ‘Proceed against the bastards and the reprobates, and against the children of fornication: and destroy [the children of fornication and] the children of the Watchers from amongst men [and cause them to go forth]: send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle: for length of days shall they not have.* (1 Enoch 10:9). *The tares are the children of the wicked one* (Matthew 13:38). Enoch names them before the parable does: the children of the Watchers, a seed with a father of its own, distinguished from the line of Adam and marked for destruction. The tares are not bad wheat; they are another seed.$n$,$n$And to Gabriel said Yahuah (Lord): ‘Proceed against the bastards and the reprobates, and against the children of fornication: and destroy [the children of fornication and] the children of the Watchers from amongst men [and cause them to go forth]: send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle: for length of days shall they not have.$n$),
(4540,10,13,10,13,$n$*In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.* (1 Enoch 10:13). *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth* (Matthew 13:42). Enoch saw the abyss of fire and the prison appointed for the Watchers — the furnace the parable names, already mapped.$n$,$n$In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.$n$),
(4541,54,6,54,6,$n$*And Michael, and Gabriel, and Raphael, and Phanuel shall take hold of them on that great day, and cast them on that day into the burning furnace, that Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits may take vengeance on them for their unrighteousness in becoming subject to Satan and leading astray those who dwell on the earth.’* (1 Enoch 54:6). *The reapers are the angels* (Matthew 13:39), and here they are by name: Michael, Gabriel, Raphael and Phanuel, casting the hosts of Azazel into the burning furnace on the great day. The furnace of Matthew 13:42 has its angels, its day, and its reason — vengeance for leading astray those who dwell on the earth.$n$,$n$And Michael, and Gabriel, and Raphael, and Phanuel shall take hold of them on that great day, and cast them on that day into the burning furnace, that Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits may take vengeance on them for their unrighteousness in becoming subject to Satan and leading astray those who dwell on the earth.’$n$),
(4545,46,3,46,3,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *All these things spake Yahusha (Jesus) unto the multitude in parables* (Matthew 13:34). Enoch had named the Son of Adam as the one who reveals all the treasures of that which is hidden. The parables are that revealing — hidden things opened, by the one chosen to open them.$n$,$n$And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.$n$),
(4557,22,7,22,7,$n$*And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’* (1 Enoch 22:7). *The good seed are the children of the kingdom; but the tares are the children of the wicked one* (Matthew 13:38). The seed war is older than the parable. Enoch is shown the spirit of Hevel (Abel), the first righteous blood, making its suit against the seed of Qayin (Cain) until that seed is gone from among the seed of men. Two seeds, from Genesis 4 to the harvest.$n$,$n$And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’$n$),
(4597,46,2,46,2,$n$*And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?* (1 Enoch 46:2). *Whom do men say that I the Son of Adam am?* (Matthew 16:13). The question uses the title Enoch asked about — *that Son of Adam,* the one who went with the Head of Days. The King asks whether men have recognized the figure the Parables named.$n$,$n$And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?$n$),
(4598,46,3,46,3,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *Thou art the Messiah (Christ), the Son of the living Elohim (God)* (Matthew 16:16). Kefa (Peter) confesses what Enoch was told: the Son of Adam who has righteousness, whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits has chosen, whose lot has the pre-eminence for ever. The confession at Caesarea Philippi is the angel's answer at 1 Enoch 46:3, spoken on earth.$n$,$n$And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.$n$),
(4602,49,2,49,2,$n$*For he is mighty in all the secrets of righteousness, And unrighteousness shall disappear as a shadow, And have no continuance; Because the Elect One standeth before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his glory is for ever and ever, And his might unto all generations.* (1 Enoch 49:2). *I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 16:19). The secrets of righteousness belong to the Elect One who stands before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits; the keys Kefa (Peter) receives are stewardship of what is his. The one who holds the secrets delegates their opening.$n$,$n$For he is mighty in all the secrets of righteousness, And unrighteousness shall disappear as a shadow, And have no continuance; Because the Elect One standeth before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his glory is for ever and ever, And his might unto all generations.$n$),
(4603,51,3,51,3,$n$*And the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne, And his mouth shall pour forth all the secrets of wisdom and counsel: For Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath given (them) to him and hath glorified him.* (1 Enoch 51:3). *I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 16:19). Enoch saw the Elect One seated on the Father's throne, his mouth pouring out the secrets of wisdom and counsel. The keys are given by the one who sits on that throne; the house of David's key (Isaiah 22:22) is on his shoulder before it is in Kefa's (Peter's) hand.$n$,$n$And the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne, And his mouth shall pour forth all the secrets of wisdom and counsel: For Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath given (them) to him and hath glorified him.$n$),
(4604,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *Flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 16:17). The Father's naming of the Son of Adam at 1 Enoch 71:14 is the same revealing — the Head of Days declaring who he is. Kefa (Peter) receives on earth what Enoch heard in heaven, and the keys follow the revealing.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(4605,69,27,69,27,$n$*And he sat on the throne of his glory, And the sum of judgement was given unto the Son of Adam, And he caused the sinners to pass away and be destroyed from off the face of the earth, And those who have led the world astray.* (1 Enoch 69:27). *Whatsoever thou shalt bind on earth shall be bound in heaven* (Matthew 16:19). The sum of judgement was given to the Son of Adam on the throne of his glory; what the apostles bind and loose is bound and loosed under that judgement, not beside it.$n$,$n$And he sat on the throne of his glory, And the sum of judgement was given unto the Son of Adam, And he caused the sinners to pass away and be destroyed from off the face of the earth, And those who have led the world astray.$n$),
(4677,8,1,8,1,$n$*And Azâzêl taught men to make swords, and knives, and shields, and breastplates, and made known to them the metals of the earth and the art of working them, and bracelets, and ornaments, and the use of antimony, and the beautifying of the eyelids, and all kinds of costly stones, and all colouring tinctures.* (1 Enoch 8:1). *Whoso shall offend one of these little ones which believe in me, it were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck* (Matthew 18:6). The stumbling-blocks laid across the way of the little ones have a history: Azazel taught men the arts that became the snares. The millstone is the King's answer to the teacher of the snare.$n$,$n$And Azâzêl taught men to make swords, and knives, and shields, and breastplates, and made known to them the metals of the earth and the art of working them, and bracelets, and ornaments, and the use of antimony, and the beautifying of the eyelids, and all kinds of costly stones, and all colouring tinctures.$n$),
(4680,22,11,22,11,$n$*Here their spirits shall be set apart in this great pain till the great day of judgement and punishment and torment of those who curse for ever and retribution for their spirits. There He shall bind them for ever.* (1 Enoch 22:11). *It were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and that he were drowned in the depth of the sea* (Matthew 18:6). Better than what? Than the place Enoch was shown — spirits set apart in great pain until the great day of judgement, and bound there. The sea is the lesser end.$n$,$n$Here their spirits shall be set apart in this great pain till the great day of judgement and punishment and torment of those who curse for ever and retribution for their spirits. There He shall bind them for ever.$n$),
(4682,89,42,90,18,$n$*And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep came unto them and took in His hand the staff of His wrath, and smote the earth, and the earth clave asunder, and all the beasts and all the birds of the heaven fell from among those sheep, and were swallowed up in the earth and it covered them.* (1 Enoch 90:18). *For the Son of Adam is come to save that which was lost* (Matthew 18:11). The Lord of the sheep comes to the flock in person, staff in hand, and the beasts and birds that devoured them are swallowed by the earth. The saving of the lost is the Lord of the sheep arriving.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep came unto them and took in His hand the staff of His wrath, and smote the earth, and the earth clave asunder, and all the beasts and all the birds of the heaven fell from among those sheep, and were swallowed up in the earth and it covered them.$n$),
(4683,89,54,89,54,$n$*And after that I saw that when they forsook the house of Yahuah (Lord) and His tower they fell away entirely, and their eyes were blinded; and I saw Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep how He wrought much slaughter amongst them in their herds until those sheep invited that slaughter and betrayed His place.* (1 Enoch 89:54). *If a man have an hundred sheep, and one of them be gone astray, doth he not leave the ninety and nine, and goeth into the mountains, and seeketh that which is gone astray?* (Matthew 18:12). Enoch's vision names the owner of the flock: Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep, whose house and tower the sheep forsook. The shepherd of the parable is not a hired man; he is the Lord of the sheep seeking his own.$n$,$n$And after that I saw that when they forsook the house of Yahuah (Lord) and His tower they fell away entirely, and their eyes were blinded; and I saw Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep how He wrought much slaughter amongst them in their herds until those sheep invited that slaughter and betrayed His place.$n$),
(4685,90,18,90,33,$n$*And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.* (1 Enoch 90:33). *He rejoiceth more of that sheep, than of the ninety and nine which went not astray* (Matthew 18:13). Enoch saw that joy at the end: the Lord of the sheep rejoicing with great joy because all that had been dispersed had returned to his house. The parable's one sheep is the vision's whole flock.$n$,$n$And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.$n$),
(4686,40,9,40,9,$n$*And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’* (1 Enoch 40:9). *In heaven their angels do always behold the face of my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 18:10). Enoch is given the names of the four who stand before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits — mercy, healing, power, and repentance unto hope. The little ones are watched over from the throne itself.$n$,$n$And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’$n$),
(4711,94,3,94,8,$n$*Woe to you, ye rich, for ye have trusted in your riches, And from your riches shall ye depart, Because ye have not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of your riches.* (1 Enoch 94:8). *A rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 19:23). Enoch's woe says why: those who trust in riches depart from them, having not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of their wealth. The difficulty is not the money; it is the trust.$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye rich, for ye have trusted in your riches, And from your riches shall ye depart, Because ye have not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of your riches.$n$),
(4712,97,7,97,7,$n$*Woe to you, ye sinners, who live on the mid ocean and on the dry land, Whose remembrance is evil against you.* (1 Enoch 97:7). *A rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 19:23). The young ruler's confidence — *all these things have I kept from my youth up* — is the sinner's confidence Enoch names: a remembrance that is evil against him, however secure the holdings look.$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye sinners, who live on the mid ocean and on the dry land, Whose remembrance is evil against you.$n$),
(4713,94,8,97,9,$n$*And now let us do what we purposed: For we have gathered silver, And many are the husbandmen in our houses.’ And our granaries are (brim) full as with water,* (1 Enoch 97:9). *It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of Elohim (God)* (Matthew 19:24). Enoch gives the rich man's own speech — silver gathered, granaries full, *let us do what we purposed.* That speech is the needle's eye closing.$n$,$n$And now let us do what we purposed: For we have gathered silver, And many are the husbandmen in our houses.’ And our granaries are (brim) full as with water,$n$),
(4715,100,6,100,6,$n$*And (then) the children of the earth shall see the wise in security, And shall understand all the words of this book, And recognize that their riches shall not be able to save them In the overthrow of their sins.* (1 Enoch 100:6). *With men this is impossible; but with Elohim (God) all things are possible* (Matthew 19:26). Enoch saw the day the children of the earth understand that riches cannot save them. What riches cannot do, Elohim (God) does — that is the whole of the disciples' hope, and the whole of the rich man's.$n$,$n$And (then) the children of the earth shall see the wise in security, And shall understand all the words of this book, And recognize that their riches shall not be able to save them In the overthrow of their sins.$n$),
(4726,39,1,62,8,$n$*And the congregation of the elect and holy shall be sown. And all the elect shall stand before him on that day.* (1 Enoch 62:8). *So the last shall be first, and the first last: for many be called, but few chosen* (Matthew 20:16). Enoch saw the chosen gathered: the congregation of the elect and holy sown, and all the elect standing before him on that day. The few are not fewer because they tried harder; they are the elect, and the elect are revealed by their standing.$n$,$n$And the congregation of the elect and holy shall be sown. And all the elect shall stand before him on that day.$n$),
(4736,62,9,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). *The Son of Adam came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many* (Matthew 20:28). The same Son of Adam, Enoch saw, raises the kings and the mighty from their seats and breaks the teeth of the sinners. The one who serves is the one who judges; the ransom and the reckoning belong to the same hands.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(4753,89,35,89,58,$n$*But He remained unmoved, though He saw it, and rejoiced that they were devoured and swallowed and robbed, and left them to be devoured in the hand of all the beasts.* (1 Enoch 89:58). *Let no fruit grow on thee henceforward for ever. And presently the fig tree withered away* (Matthew 21:19). Enoch saw the Lord of the sheep do the same to a flock that had abandoned him: unmoved, leaving them to be devoured. The withered tree is the leadership that bore no fruit, left to its own harvest.$n$,$n$But He remained unmoved, though He saw it, and rejoiced that they were devoured and swallowed and robbed, and left them to be devoured in the hand of all the beasts.$n$),
(4761,89,45,90,25,$n$*And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.* (1 Enoch 90:25). *He will miserably destroy those wicked men, and will let out his vineyard unto other husbandmen* (Matthew 21:41). The husbandmen answer their own parable; Enoch's vision records the sentence they pronounced — the seventy shepherds judged, found guilty, and cast into the fiery abyss.$n$,$n$And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.$n$),
(4782,51,3,51,3,$n$*And the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne, And his mouth shall pour forth all the secrets of wisdom and counsel: For Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath given (them) to him and hath glorified him.* (1 Enoch 51:3). *Yahuah (The LORD) said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand* (Matthew 22:44; Psalm 110:1). Enoch heard the same seating spoken by the Father: *the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne.* The Pharisees could not say how David's son is David's Lord; the Parables had already seated him.$n$,$n$And the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne, And his mouth shall pour forth all the secrets of wisdom and counsel: For Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath given (them) to him and hath glorified him.$n$),
(4783,61,8,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool* (Matthew 22:44). The Head of Days placing the Elect One on the throne of glory is Psalm 110:1 seen from the throne room — the Father seating the Son, the Son judging. The Formless seats the Formed; the One who is seated is Elohim (God) and has a Father.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(4784,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *If David then call him Lord, how is he his son?* (Matthew 22:45). The Father answers at 1 Enoch 71:14: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* Born — David's son after the flesh; named by the Head of Days — David's Lord. The question the Pharisees could not answer, the Parables had answered.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(4801,22,7,21,10,$n$*And he said unto me: ‘This place is the prison of the angels, and here they will be imprisoned for ever.’* (1 Enoch 21:10). *Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of Gehinnom (hell)?* (Matthew 23:33). Enoch was shown the prison of the angels and told it holds them for ever. The judgment the serpents cannot escape is the judgment their fathers, the Watchers, are already held for; the seed goes where the seed came from.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘This place is the prison of the angels, and here they will be imprisoned for ever.’$n$),
(4802,22,14,22,7,$n$*And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’* (1 Enoch 22:7). *That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Hevel (Abel)* (Matthew 23:35). Enoch saw the spirit of Hevel (Abel) making its suit against the seed of Qayin (Cain) until that seed is destroyed. The blood that cries from the ground (Genesis 4:10) is still crying in Enoch's vision, and the King hands the sum of it to the generation standing in front of him.$n$,$n$And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’$n$),
(4807,65,11,65,10,$n$*And He said unto me: “Because of their unrighteousness their judgement has been determined upon and shall not be withheld by Me for ever. Because of the sorceries which they have searched out and learnt, the earth and those who dwell upon it shall be destroyed.”* (1 Enoch 65:10). *As in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noach (Noah) entered into the ark* (Matthew 24:38). Enoch heard the sentence pronounced over those days: judgement determined, not to be withheld, the earth and its dwellers to be destroyed for the sorceries they had learned. The eating and drinking went on under a sentence already passed.$n$,$n$And He said unto me: “Because of their unrighteousness their judgement has been determined upon and shall not be withheld by Me for ever. Because of the sorceries which they have searched out and learnt, the earth and those who dwell upon it shall be destroyed.”$n$),
(4808,67,1,10,13,$n$*In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.* (1 Enoch 10:13). *And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be* (Matthew 24:39). The flood took the wicked away; it did not carry the righteous off. Enoch's word for the Watchers is the same taking: led off to the abyss of fire, to the prison. The ones taken at the coming are the ones taken at the flood — the judged.$n$,$n$In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.$n$),
(4814,90,10,90,10,$n$*And it looked at them [and their eyes opened], and it cried to the sheep, and the rams saw it and all ran to it.* (1 Enoch 90:10). *And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds* (Matthew 24:31). Enoch saw the gathering as a flock: the great horn cried to the sheep, their eyes opened, and the rams all ran to it. The gathering is the sheep running to the horn that called them.$n$,$n$And it looked at them [and their eyes opened], and it cried to the sheep, and the rams saw it and all ran to it.$n$),
(4845,62,5,62,5,$n$*And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.* (1 Enoch 62:5). *When the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory* (Matthew 25:31). Enoch saw that seat and the faces of those who see it — terror, pain, downcast countenance, when they see that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory. The sheep-and-goats judgment opens on the throne the Parables had already set.$n$,$n$And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.$n$),
(4846,62,3,61,10,$n$*And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.* (1 Enoch 61:10). *And all the holy angels with him* (Matthew 25:31). Enoch gives the roll: the host of the heavens, the holy ones above, Cherubim, Seraphim and Ophannim, the angels of power and of principalities — and the Elect One among them. The company of the coming was mustered in the Parables before the gospel named it.$n$,$n$And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.$n$),
(4847,62,9,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). *And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another* (Matthew 25:32). The Son of Adam who separates is the Son of Adam Enoch saw raise the kings and the mighty from their seats and break the teeth of the sinners. The separation is a reversal; the mighty do not keep their seats at it.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(4848,62,11,46,6,$n$*And he shall put down the countenance of the strong, And shall fill them with shame. And darkness shall be their dwelling, And worms shall be their bed, And they shall have no hope of rising from their beds, Because they do not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 46:6). *Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels* (Matthew 25:41). Enoch saw what that departure is for the strong: countenance put down, shame, darkness for a dwelling, worms for a bed, no hope of rising — because they did not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,$n$And he shall put down the countenance of the strong, And shall fill them with shame. And darkness shall be their dwelling, And worms shall be their bed, And they shall have no hope of rising from their beds, Because they do not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(4849,63,7,63,8,$n$*And in the day of our suffering and tribulation He saves us not, And we find no respite for confession That our Lord is true in all His works, and in His judgements and His justice, And His judgements have no respect of persons.* (1 Enoch 63:8). *Depart from me, ye cursed* (Matthew 25:41) is answered in Enoch by the mouths of the kings and the mighty themselves: in the day of their tribulation he saves them not, and their confession comes too late to be anything but true. *Lord, when saw we thee an hungred?* (Matthew 25:44) is the same late confession.$n$,$n$And in the day of our suffering and tribulation He saves us not, And we find no respite for confession That our Lord is true in all His works, and in His judgements and His justice, And His judgements have no respect of persons.$n$),
(4850,46,2,46,2,$n$*And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?* (1 Enoch 46:2). *Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Matthew 26:64). The bound man before the council names himself with Enoch's title — *that Son of Adam* who went with the Head of Days. The council thought it was judging him; he was telling them who would judge.$n$,$n$And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?$n$),
(4854,63,3,62,9,$n$*And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.* (1 Enoch 62:9). *Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power* (Matthew 26:64). Enoch saw what the council will see: all the kings and the mighty falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, petitioning him for mercy. The men who condemned him will kneel to him.$n$,$n$And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.$n$),
(4877,63,1,62,3,$n$*And there shall stand up in that day all the kings and the mighty, And the exalted and those who hold the earth, And they shall see and recognize How he sits on the throne of his glory, And righteousness is judged before him, And no lying word is spoken before him.* (1 Enoch 62:3). *When the morning was come, all the chief priests and elders of the people took counsel against Yahusha (Jesus) to put him to death* (Matthew 27:1). Enoch saw the other morning: all the kings and the mighty standing up in that day to see and recognize how he sits on the throne of his glory, where no lying word is spoken. The council that condemned him stands at his bar.$n$,$n$And there shall stand up in that day all the kings and the mighty, And the exalted and those who hold the earth, And they shall see and recognize How he sits on the throne of his glory, And righteousness is judged before him, And no lying word is spoken before him.$n$),
(4878,62,3,61,10,$n$*And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.* (1 Enoch 61:10). *If he be the King of Yashar'el (Israel), let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him* (Matthew 27:42). The mockers set the wrong test. Enoch saw the King's credential: the whole host of heaven summoned, and the Elect One among them. He did not come down from the cross; he is the one for whom the heavens are mustered.$n$,$n$And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.$n$),
(4879,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *He trusted in Elohim (God); let him deliver him now, if he will have him* (Matthew 27:43). The Head of Days had already said it: *the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.* The cross was not the Father's forsaking of the Son; it was the Son of Adam, born unto righteousness, doing what righteousness does.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(4880,63,3,62,9,$n$*And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.* (1 Enoch 62:9). *Let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him* (Matthew 27:42). Enoch saw the mockers' end: the kings and the mighty and those who rule the earth falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, worshipping and petitioning. *Every knee should bow* (Philippians 2:10) — the mockers included.$n$,$n$And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.$n$),
(4900,62,6,62,2,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.* (1 Enoch 62:2). *All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch saw the giving: the Elect One seated on the throne of glory, the spirit of righteousness poured out on him, the word of his mouth slaying the sinners. The power was given by the Father; the Son wields it.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.$n$),
(4901,62,9,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). *All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch's Son of Adam raises the kings and the mighty from their seats and breaks the teeth of the sinners. That is what all power looks like when it is used.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(4902,61,8,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch saw the placing — Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits setting the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge and to weigh deeds in the balance. The Father is the giver; the Son is seated; the power is the power to judge.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(7843,19,1,19,1,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). 1 Enoch 19:1 names the watcher-spirits and their appointed standing-place of judgement. At Mark 3:11 the unclean spirits *fell down before him, and cried, saying, Thou art the Son of Elohim (God)* — the watcher-administration recognizing the Judge before whom it must one day stand, falling down before the Formed one whose great-judgement-day is named in the Enochic library.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$),
(7844,16,1,16,4,$n$*Say to them therefore: “You have no peace.”’* (1 Enoch 16:4). *Let us alone; what have we to do with thee, thou Yahusha (Jesus) of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us?* (Mark 1:24). The spirits that cry out have been told their sentence: no peace. The Holy One's coming is the disturbance of a peace they were never granted.$n$,$n$Say to them therefore: “You have no peace.”’$n$),
(7845,15,11,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). 1 Enoch 16:1 names the unclean spirit's origin and its appointed end: the spirits gone forth from the giants destroy until the day of the great judgement. The demon's own question at Mark 1:24 — *art thou come to destroy us?* — names that it knows its judgement-day is fixed; the watchers' offspring recognize that the Holy One of Elohim is the one who holds the day of their consummation.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(7846,15,6,15,8,$n$*And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling.* (1 Enoch 15:8). (1 Enoch 15:8-7 reads: *Evil spirits have proceeded from their bodies; because they are born from men and from the holy Watchers is their beginning and primal origin... And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth.*) The unclean spirit that cries in the synagogue — *I know thee who thou art, the Holy One of Elohim (God)* — is one of these: an evil spirit gone forth from the slain giants' flesh, the watchers' offspring under restraint. It recognizes the Formed one before the watching crowd can name him because it was there at the rebellion. The recognition is not the sheep's hearing; the demons know and tremble, and the King silences them.$n$,$n$And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling.$n$),
(7852,19,1,19,1,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). *And see him that was possessed with the devil, and had the legion, sitting, and clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid* (Mark 5:15). The man restored is the reversal, in one life, of what Enoch says these spirits do — defile mankind and lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods. Their day of judgement is fixed; the Gadarene was given his back early.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$),
(7855,16,1,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). *For he said unto him, Come out of the man, thou unclean spirit.* 1 Enoch 16:1 names the spirits the command addresses by their origin in the slain giants:  The unclean spirit is not a faceless force; the Hebrew library had recorded its lineage and its sentence — *Say to them therefore: "You have no peace."* (1 Enoch 16:4) — long before the King commanded it out of the man.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(7856,15,11,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). *And the unclean spirits went out, and entered into the swine: and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the sea* (Mark 5:13). The spirits of the giants afflict and destroy, Enoch says, and they do not eat yet hunger. The sea was not their judgement; that waits for the day of the consummation. It was the King displacing them.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(7857,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). *My name is Legion: for we are many* (Mark 5:9). Enoch names what a legion does to a man among the tombs: the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, and cause offences. The man crying and cutting himself night and day was under exactly that.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(7858,15,8,15,10,$n$*[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]* (1 Enoch 15:10). *My name is Legion: for we are many* (Mark 5:9). Many, because they are the earth-born spirits of the giants whose dwelling is on the earth. The gospel's word for them is *Legion*; Enoch's word is their pedigree.$n$,$n$[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]$n$),
(7868,27,2,26,2,$n$*And there I saw a holy mountain, and underneath the mountain to the east there was a stream and it flowed towards the south.* (1 Enoch 26:2). 1 Enoch 27:1-3 places the accursed valley — the Hinnom-shaped place of punishment for the godless — beside the holy mountain, the very Ge-Hinnom topography the gospel's *hell* (Gehenna) draws its name from. The King's *cut it off ... than having two hands to go into hell* (Mark 9:43) walks the same place-of-judgment architecture 1 Enoch maps at the middle of the earth: the accursed valley appointed for the day of judgment.$n$,$n$And there I saw a holy mountain, and underneath the mountain to the east there was a stream and it flowed towards the south.$n$),
(7869,22,11,22,11,$n$*Here their spirits shall be set apart in this great pain till the great day of judgement and punishment and torment of those who curse for ever and retribution for their spirits. There He shall bind them for ever.* (1 Enoch 22:11). *Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched* (Mark 9:48). Enoch was shown where the sinners' spirits are set apart in great pain until the great day of judgement — a holding until the judgement comes, and then the binding for ever. The place Mark warns of is the place Enoch had mapped; the fire that is not quenched is the judgement the holding waits for.$n$,$n$Here their spirits shall be set apart in this great pain till the great day of judgement and punishment and torment of those who curse for ever and retribution for their spirits. There He shall bind them for ever.$n$),
(7874,62,9,62,9,$n$*And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.* (1 Enoch 62:9). *Ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Mark 14:62). Enoch saw the seeing: the kings and the mighty falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, petitioning for mercy. The court that condemned him will see him, exactly as he said.$n$,$n$And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.$n$),
(7875,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). 1 Enoch 71:14 names the Son of Adam born unto righteousness, over whom the righteousness of the Head of Days never fails. Mark 14:62's self-identification — *I am: and ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power* — names the same figure the Parables named: the righteous one whom the Head of Days does not forsake, enthroned at the right hand. The title-naming of the Parables and the direct attribution of the King land on one figure.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(7876,62,1,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Sitting on the right hand of power* (Mark 14:62). Enoch saw the placing: Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits set the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge. The bound man names his seat before the court that thinks it is judging him.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(7877,46,4,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). *Ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Mark 14:62). The one the Sanhedrin condemns is the one Enoch saw raise the kings and the mighty from their seats and break the teeth of the sinners. The reversal was written before the trial.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(7886,40,2,40,2,$n$*And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.* (1 Enoch 40:2). 1 Enoch 40:2 names the four presences who stand on the four sides of Yahuah of Spirits — the angelic standing-before-the-throne architecture. When Gabriel answers Zecharyah (Zacharias) at Luke 1:19 — *I am Gabriel, that stand in the presence of Elohim (God)* — he names the same standing-before-Yahuah office the Hebrew library already named. The Enochic vision had already seen the presences who stand before the throne; Gabriel names himself as one of them.$n$,$n$And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.$n$),
(7887,40,9,40,9,$n$*And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’* (1 Enoch 40:9). 1 Enoch 40:9 names Gabriel by name as the third of the four presences who stand before Yahuah (God) of Spirits. Luke 1:19's *I am Gabriel, that stand in the presence of Elohim (God)* names the same Gabriel in the same standing-before-the-throne office. The Hebrew library carries the named angel of the presence; the gospel sends that same named angel to the priest at the altar of incense. (And the same Phanuel of v.9 is named at the presentation — Anna *the daughter of Phanuel,* Luke 2:36 — the throne-room names threading into the temple-court narrative.)$n$,$n$And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’$n$),
(7892,40,1,40,1,$n$*And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 40:1). *Suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly host praising Elohim (God)* (Luke 2:13). Enoch saw that host where it stands — thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. At the birth of the Son the host that stands before the throne came down to the fields.$n$,$n$And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(7893,39,12,40,3,$n$*And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* (1 Enoch 40:3). 1 Enoch 40:3 names the praises uttered before Yahuah of glory by the presences of the throne-room. Luke 2:14's *Glory to Elohim (God) in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men* is the same heavenly-praise register, now sounded on earth. The glory the host gives in the highest is the glory the Hebrew library heard them give before the throne; the nativity brings the throne-room praise down to the shepherds' field.$n$,$n$And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.$n$),
(7894,39,13,40,4,$n$*The first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever.* (1 Enoch 40:4). 1 Enoch 40:4 names the first voice of the host blessing Yahuah of Spirits for ever and ever. The angelic *Glory to Elohim (God) in the highest* of Luke 2:14 is the same blessing-of-the-Most-High the Hebrew library named in the mouths of the host. The host that blesses Yahuah for ever in the Enochic vision is the host that blesses him over Bethlehem; the praise is one praise, heard first in heaven and now on earth.$n$,$n$The first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever.$n$),
(7899,85,3,85,3,$n$*Before I took thy mother Edna, I saw in a vision on my bed, and behold a bull came forth from the earth, and that bull was white; and after it came forth a heifer, and along with this (latter) came forth two bulls, one of them black and the other red.* (1 Enoch 85:3). 1 Enoch 85:3 opens the Animal Apocalypse with the white bull (Adam) coming forth from the earth, the heifer (Chavah/Eve), and the two young bulls — the black (Cain) and the red (Hevel/Abel). This is the Adamic toledot in vision-form, the same opening of the seed-line Luke 3:38 closes its backward genealogy on: *the son of Adam, which was the son of Elohim (God).* The Hebrew library sees the first man as the white bull from the earth whom Yahuah created; the gospel names the same Adam as the son of Elohim at the head of the seed-line.$n$,$n$Before I took thy mother Edna, I saw in a vision on my bed, and behold a bull came forth from the earth, and that bull was white; and after it came forth a heifer, and along with this (latter) came forth two bulls, one of them black and the other red.$n$),
(7900,85,8,85,9,$n$*And I saw in my sleep that white bull likewise grow and become a great white bull, and from him proceeded many white bulls, and they resembled him. And they began to beget many white bulls, which resembled them, one following the other, (even) many.* (1 Enoch 85:9–10). 1 Enoch 85:9 names the *another white bull* (Shet/Seth) from whom the many white bulls proceed, each resembling the one before — the seed-of-Adam carried forward through the Sethite line, generation following generation. Luke 3:36-38 traces that same white-bull line backward — *Enos... Seth... Adam, which was the son of Elohim (God).* The Hebrew library sees the seed-line as the white bulls one-following-another from Shet; the gospel names the genealogy of the same seed-line back to its Adamic and divine head.$n$,$n$And I saw in my sleep that white bull likewise grow and become a great white bull, and from him proceeded many white bulls, and they resembled him.$n$),
(7901,60,8,60,8,$n$*But the male is named Behemoth, who occupied with his breast a waste wilderness named Dûidâin, on the east of the garden where the elect and righteous dwell, where my grandfather was taken up, the seventh from Adam, the first man whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits created.* (1 Enoch 60:8). 1 Enoch 60:8 names Enoch (Chanok) as *the seventh from Adam* and names Adam as *the first man whom Yahuah of Spirits created.* Luke 3:37-38 runs the genealogy through *Enoch... Jared... Adam, which was the son of Elohim (God)* — Enoch standing seventh in the line from Adam, exactly as the Hebrew library counts him (the same count Jude 1:14 carries). The Hebrew library names Adam as the first-created man and Enoch as the seventh from him; the gospel's backward genealogy lands on the same Adam, the son of the Elohim who created him.$n$,$n$But the male is named Behemoth, who occupied with his breast a waste wilderness named Dûidâin, on the east of the garden where the elect and righteous dwell, where my grandfather was taken up, the seventh from Adam, the first man whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits created.$n$),
(7906,16,1,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). *What have I to do with thee, Yahusha (Jesus), thou Son of Elohim (God) most high? I beseech thee, torment me not* (Luke 8:28). The spirits know the day of the consummation is appointed for them; Enoch records that they destroy only until it. The demoniac's cry is the fear of a sentence already written.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(7907,15,11,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). The Hebrew library names the appointed-consummation the spirits operate under — they destroy until the great judgement, and they fear its premature arrival. Luke 8:31's Legion *besought him that he would not command them to go out into the deep* — the abussos, the place of confinement appointed against the day of consummation. The spirits beg to be spared the very binding 1 Enoch names as appointed; the King's arrival is the appointed authority they dread.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(7908,15,8,15,10,$n$*[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]* (1 Enoch 15:10). The Hebrew library names the demon-origin and earth-dwelling architecture: the unclean spirits are the earthbound spirits born of the giants, the offspring of the Watcher-rebellion of Genesis 6. Luke 8:29's unclean spirit — the one that *oftentimes had caught him* and drove the man *into the wilderness* — is an earth-dwelling spirit of exactly the order 1 Enoch names. The library carried the demon-origin diagnostic for centuries; the King's casting-out at Luke 8 walks the same architecture.$n$,$n$[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]$n$),
(7924,6,6,6,6,$n$*And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* (1 Enoch 6:6). *I beheld Satan as lightning fall from heaven* (Luke 10:18). Enoch records the first fall — two hundred who descended on Hermon in the days of Jared and bound themselves by oath. The seventy returning with the devils subject to them (Luke 10:17) were undoing, territory by territory, what began on that mountain.$n$,$n$And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.$n$),
(7938,90,3,90,10,$n$*And it looked at them [and their eyes opened], and it cried to the sheep, and the rams saw it and all ran to it.* (1 Enoch 90:10). *For the Son of Adam is come to seek and to save that which was lost* (Luke 19:10). Enoch saw the seeking as a horn crying to the sheep, their eyes opening, and all of them running to it. The lost are the house of Yashar'el (Israel) scattered among the nations; the seeking is the call that brings the sheep running home — not a new flock gathered from the nations.$n$,$n$And it looked at them [and their eyes opened], and it cried to the sheep, and the rams saw it and all ran to it.$n$),
(7946,22,11,22,4,$n$*And these places have been made to receive them till the day of their judgement and till their appointed period [till the period appointed], till the great judgement (comes) upon them.’* (1 Enoch 22:4). *Between us and you there is a great gulf fixed* (Luke 16:26). Enoch saw the fixing: the hollow places made to receive the dead until the day of their judgement, divided one from another. Sheol is real and the dead are aware in it — and it is a holding until the appointed period, not the final destination.$n$,$n$And these places have been made to receive them till the day of their judgement and till their appointed period [till the period appointed], till the great judgement (comes) upon them.’$n$),
(7947,22,10,22,10,$n$*And such has been made for sinners when they die and are buried in the earth and judgement has not been executed on them in their lifetime.* (1 Enoch 22:10). The conscious-souls-of-the-dead-assembled register against the inherited soul-sleep misread. Luke 16:23's rich man *in hell (hadēs) lift up his eyes, being in torments, and seeth Avraham (Abraham) afar off, and Lazaros in his bosom* assumes exactly this architecture — the spirits of the dead are gathered, aware, and identifiable, held in the hollow places the Hebrew library named.$n$,$n$And such has been made for sinners when they die and are buried in the earth and judgement has not been executed on them in their lifetime.$n$),
(7948,22,9,22,9,$n$*And he answered me and said unto me: ‘These three have been made that the spirits of the dead might be separated. And such a division has been made for the spirits of the righteous, in which there is the bright spring of water.* (1 Enoch 22:9). Enoch is shown the holding-places of the dead — distinct compartments hewn in the great mountain. Luke 16:22's carrying of Lazaros *by the angels into Avraham's (Abraham's) bosom* while the rich man is *buried* and lifts his eyes in another place walks the same architecture the Hebrew library named: the dead are held in separated compartments pending the judgment, not annihilated into nothing and not dispatched to a final eternal destination.$n$,$n$And he answered me and said unto me: ‘These three have been made that the spirits of the dead might be separated. And such a division has been made for the spirits of the righteous, in which there is the bright spring of water.$n$),
(7955,22,11,22,4,$n$*And these places have been made to receive them till the day of their judgement and till their appointed period [till the period appointed], till the great judgement (comes) upon them.’* (1 Enoch 22:4). *To day shalt thou be with me in paradise* (Luke 23:43). Enoch was shown the places made to receive the dead until the day of their judgement. The paradise promised to the thief that day is the righteous division of those places, held until the great judgement — not the final state, but the keeping until it.$n$,$n$And these places have been made to receive them till the day of their judgement and till their appointed period [till the period appointed], till the great judgement (comes) upon them.’$n$),
(7956,22,9,22,9,$n$*And he answered me and said unto me: ‘These three have been made that the spirits of the dead might be separated. And such a division has been made for the spirits of the righteous, in which there is the bright spring of water.* (1 Enoch 22:9). *To day shalt thou be with me in paradise* (Luke 23:43). Enoch was shown the hollow places where the spirits of the dead are received — deep, wide, divided. The paradise promised to the thief that day is the righteous division of those places, where the bright spring of water is, until the day of judgement.$n$,$n$And he answered me and said unto me: ‘These three have been made that the spirits of the dead might be separated. And such a division has been made for the spirits of the righteous, in which there is the bright spring of water.$n$),
(7957,104,4,104,4,$n$*Be hopeful, and cast not away your hope; for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.* (1 Enoch 104:4). *Neither can they die any more: for they are equal unto the angels* (Luke 20:36). Enoch tells the righteous to hope, *for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.* The equality with angels is joy without end, promised before the Sadducees asked their question.$n$,$n$Be hopeful, and cast not away your hope; for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.$n$),
(7958,39,5,39,5,$n$*Here mine eyes saw their dwellings with His righteous angels, And their resting-places with the holy. And they petitioned and interceded and prayed for the children of men, And righteousness flowed before them as water, And mercy like dew upon the earth: Thus it is amongst them for ever and ever.* (1 Enoch 39:5). *Equal unto the angels; and are the children of Elohim (God), being the children of the resurrection* (Luke 20:36). Enoch saw their dwellings with the righteous angels and their resting-places with the holy. The children of the resurrection dwell where Enoch saw them dwell.$n$,$n$Here mine eyes saw their dwellings with His righteous angels, And their resting-places with the holy. And they petitioned and interceded and prayed for the children of men, And righteousness flowed before them as water, And mercy like dew upon the earth: Thus it is amongst them for ever and ever.$n$),
(7959,39,4,39,4,$n$*And there I saw another vision, the dwelling-places of the holy, And the resting-places of the righteous.* (1 Enoch 39:4). The Hebrew library names the dwellings of the righteous WITH the holy angels — the resting-places of the elect among the holy ones of heaven. *They are equal unto the angels; and are the children of Elohim (God), being the children of the resurrection* (Luke 20:36): the equal-unto-the-angels register the King names against the Sadducees' deny-the-resurrection is the same dwelling-with-the-righteous-angels Enoch saw — the children of the resurrection sharing the resting-places of the holy ones, no longer dying, no longer given in marriage, equal unto the angels.$n$,$n$And there I saw another vision, the dwelling-places of the holy, And the resting-places of the righteous.$n$),
(7969,42,2,42,2,$n$*Wisdom went forth to make her dwelling among the children of men, And found no dwelling-place: Wisdom returned to her place, And took her seat among the angels.* (1 Enoch 42:2). *He came unto his own, and his own received him not* (John 1:11). Enoch saw Wisdom go out to make her dwelling among the children of men and find no place. The Word came to his own and found no room; the rejection was foreseen before the Word was made flesh.$n$,$n$Wisdom went forth to make her dwelling among the children of men, And found no dwelling-place: Wisdom returned to her place, And took her seat among the angels.$n$),
(7997,62,2,61,9,$n$*And when he shall lift up his countenance To judge their secret ways according to the word of the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And their path according to the way of the righteous judgement of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, Then shall they all with one voice speak and bless, And glorify and extol and sanctify the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 61:9). *And hath given him authority to execute judgment also, because he is the Son of Adam* (John 5:27). Enoch saw him lift up his countenance to judge their secret ways, and the whole host bless the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for it. The authority is given by the Father; the judging is the Son's; the praise returns to the Father.$n$,$n$And when he shall lift up his countenance To judge their secret ways according to the word of the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And their path according to the way of the righteous judgement of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, Then shall they all with one voice speak and bless, And glorify and extol and sanctify the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(7998,61,8,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *And hath given him authority to execute judgment also, because he is the Son of Adam* (John 5:27). Enoch saw the giving: the Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge and to weigh deeds in the balance. The authority John names is the seat Enoch saw filled.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(8001,62,2,61,9,$n$*And when he shall lift up his countenance To judge their secret ways according to the word of the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And their path according to the way of the righteous judgement of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, Then shall they all with one voice speak and bless, And glorify and extol and sanctify the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 61:9). *The hour is come, that the Son of Adam should be glorified* (John 12:23). Enoch saw the glorifying: the Son of Adam judging their secret ways, and all the holy blessing and sanctifying the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. *Father, glorify thy name* (John 12:28) is the Son asking for what the Parables already showed.$n$,$n$And when he shall lift up his countenance To judge their secret ways according to the word of the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And their path according to the way of the righteous judgement of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, Then shall they all with one voice speak and bless, And glorify and extol and sanctify the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(8002,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *The hour is come, that the Son of Adam should be glorified* (John 12:23). The Son of Adam is the one the Head of Days named at 1 Enoch 71:14 — born unto righteousness, never forsaken. The hour John names is the hour that naming comes to pass on earth.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(8008,51,1,51,1,$n$*And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* (1 Enoch 51:1). *I am the resurrection, and the life* (John 11:25). Enoch saw the earth and Sheol give back what they hold, and the Elect One arise. The one who says *I am the resurrection* is the one at whose arising the dead are given back.$n$,$n$And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.$n$),
(9875,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). The coming the angels promise at Acts 1:11 — *this same Yahusha (Jesus)... shall so come in like manner* — is the coming Jude quoted from Enoch: he comes with ten thousands of his holy ones to execute judgement. The holy ones with him are the seed of promise, gathered to him and coming with him into the land — not souls come down out of heaven.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(9899,62,1,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Yahuah (The LORD) said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand* (Acts 2:34). Enoch saw the seating: Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placing the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge. The right hand of Psalm 110 is the throne of glory of the Parables.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(9900,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *Elohim (God) hath made that same Yahusha (Jesus), whom ye have crucified, both Lord and Messiah (Christ)* (Acts 2:36). The Father had already named him: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* The one Kefa (Peter) preaches is the one the Head of Days declared.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(10661,8,2,8,2,$n$*And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* (1 Enoch 8:2). The *spirit of divination* (Acts 16:16) is no neutral gift: enchantment and soothsaying are the watcher-taught corruptions, the arts the fallen ones handed to men. Paul commands the spirit out in the name of Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ) (Acts 16:18) — the One above the watchers undoing what they taught.$n$,$n$And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.$n$),
(12616,71,1,71,1,$n$*And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* (1 Enoch 71:1). *By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death... because Elohim (God) had translated him* (Hebrews 11:5). The Torah says only that Elohim (God) took him; Enoch tells the taking from the inside — *my spirit was translated and it ascended into the heavens.* The man who pleased Elohim (God) was brought up among the holy sons of Elohim (God), translated rather than buried.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$),
(12617,71,5,71,5,$n$*And he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens, And I saw there as it were a structure built of crystals, And between those crystals tongues of living fire.* (1 Enoch 71:5). *By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death* (Hebrews 11:5). The word Hebrews uses for Enoch — *translated* — is the word the vision uses: *he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens.* The witness who would not see death is carried into the very dwelling-place of Elohim, among the first fathers and the righteous who dwell there from the beginning of the world.$n$,$n$And he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens, And I saw there as it were a structure built of crystals, And between those crystals tongues of living fire.$n$),
(12820,14,15,14,18,$n$*And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* (1 Enoch 14:18). The throne Enoch saw — crystal, wheels like the sun, cherubim, fire streaming from beneath it (1 Enoch 14:18–22) — is the throne-and-fire presence John is brought into when he sees the Formed One whose *eyes were as a flame of fire* and whose *feet like unto fine brass, as if they burned in a furnace* (Revelation 1:14–15). John falls as dead, as Enoch fell on his face.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(12822,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *I am he that liveth, and was dead; and, behold, I am alive for evermore* (Revelation 1:18). The one who says it is the Son of Adam born unto righteousness, over whom righteousness abides, whom the Head of Days never forsakes — forsaken not even in death.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(12826,25,5,25,5,$n$*Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.* (1 Enoch 25:5). The restored library says plainly what the letter promises: the fruit of the tree *shall be for food to the elect,* and the tree transplanted to the holy place. *To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of Elohim (God)* (Revelation 2:7). The same elect, the same tree, the same gift.$n$,$n$Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.$n$),
(12850,104,1,104,1,$n$*I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.* (1 Enoch 104:1). *I will not blot out his name out of the book of life* (Revelation 3:5). Enoch swears that the names of the righteous are written before the glory of the Great One — and warns that names can be blotted out: *their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books* (1 Enoch 108:3). No name is added later; names written before the foundation of the world are kept by overcoming, or lost.$n$,$n$I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.$n$),
(12851,108,3,108,3,$n$*And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* (1 Enoch 108:3). Enoch names the blotting that falls on the sinners — *their names shall be blotted out of the book of life.* That is the very sentence the overcomer of Sardis is promised exemption from: *I will not blot out his name out of the book of life* (Revelation 3:5). The same book, the same blotting, the same patience-unto-the-end — the Hebrew library and the Apocalypse speak one judgment, and the white-robed who endure are kept written.$n$,$n$And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.$n$),
(12942,14,15,14,18,$n$*And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* (1 Enoch 14:18). *And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone* (Revelation 4:3). Enoch saw the lofty throne of crystal with wheels like the shining sun and the cherubim about it, and the Great Glory seated on it (1 Enoch 14:20). The throne of precious stone was seen before the door in heaven opened to John.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(12952,39,12,40,3,$n$*And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* (1 Enoch 40:3). Enoch too saw four about the throne of glory and heard their unceasing praise — *the four presences which surround the throne of glory, and they praise Yahuah (God) of Spirits* (1 Enoch 39:11), *as they uttered praises before Yahuah (God) of glory.* So the *four beasts... rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy* (Revelation 4:8). The restored library beheld the same fourfold worship before the same throne, the ceaseless praise of the Most High.$n$,$n$And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.$n$),
(12953,39,13,40,4,$n$*The first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever.* (1 Enoch 40:4). The praise Enoch heard rises *for ever and ever* — the very note John's four living creatures sound, who *rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy* (Revelation 4:8). One worship before one throne.$n$,$n$The first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever.$n$),
(12956,40,1,40,1,$n$*And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 40:1). *The four and twenty elders fall down before him that sat on the throne* (Revelation 4:10). Enoch saw the multitude beyond number standing before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The elders who cast their crowns belong to that numberless worship.$n$,$n$And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(12979,40,1,40,1,$n$*And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 40:1). *Ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands* (Revelation 5:11) — John's count is Enoch's count, word for word. Enoch heard that host bless Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits and bless the Elect One beside him (1 Enoch 40:4–5); John hears them cry *Worthy is the Lamb that was slain* (Revelation 5:12). The Father and the Lamb, praised together by the myriads.$n$,$n$And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(12980,14,21,18,16,$n$*And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’* (1 Enoch 18:16). In the same throne-vision where Enoch saw the mountain *like the throne of Yahuah (God)* (1 Enoch 14:15) and the columns of heavenly fire, the measure *ten thousand* sounds — the very scale John reaches for at the throne: *ten thousand times ten thousand* (Revelation 5:11). The myriad-numbered host of heaven and the ten-thousand reckonings of the throne-vision are the world Revelation 5 stands in: the innumerable court gathered before the One who sits, now lifting its voice to the Lamb.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$),
(13160,99,3,99,3,$n$*In those days make ready, ye righteous, to raise your prayers as a memorial, And place them as a testimony before the angels, That they may place the sin of the sinners for a memorial before the El Elyon (Most High).* (1 Enoch 99:3). Enoch bids the righteous *raise your prayers as a memorial... before the angels* — and in Revelation an angel does exactly that, offering the incense *with the prayers of all saints* so that they *ascended up before Elohim (God)* (Revelation 8:4). The prayers are a memorial laid before the Most High, and the same fire-bearing angel who carries them up then casts the fire of the altar to the earth (8:5): the memorial of the righteous becomes the judgment on the sinners.$n$,$n$In those days make ready, ye righteous, to raise your prayers as a memorial, And place them as a testimony before the angels, That they may place the sin of the sinners for a memorial before the El Elyon (Most High).$n$),
(13370,18,12,18,14,$n$*The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.* (1 Enoch 18:14). Enoch is shown the end of heaven and earth, a prison for the stars and the host of heaven. John sees *a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit* (Revelation 9:1). The pit has a history; the stars it holds are named in the next verses (1 Enoch 18:15–16).$n$,$n$The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.$n$),
(13371,18,14,18,16,$n$*And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’* (1 Enoch 18:16). The stars that *transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (God)* were bound till their judgment — and now one such fallen star is loosed to open the pit: *I saw a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit* (Revelation 9:1). The binding Enoch saw and the loosing John sees are the two ends of one story; the pit holds the transgressing stars until the appointed hour, and the trumpet sounds that hour.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$),
(13372,21,8,21,7,$n$*And from thence I went to another place, which was still more horrible than the former, and I saw a horrible thing: a great fire there which burnt and blazed, and the place was cleft as far as the abyss, being full of great descending columns of fire: neither its extent or magnitude could I see, nor could I conjecture.* (1 Enoch 21:7). *There arose a smoke out of the pit, as the smoke of a great furnace* (Revelation 9:2). Enoch had seen the abyss cleft and blazing with columns of fire — the furnace-place. The smoke of Revelation's pit rises from the fire Enoch was shown.$n$,$n$And from thence I went to another place, which was still more horrible than the former, and I saw a horrible thing: a great fire there which burnt and blazed, and the place was cleft as far as the abyss, being full of great descending columns of fire: neither its extent or magnitude could I see, nor could I conjecture.$n$),
(13414,81,1,81,1,$n$*And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’* (1 Enoch 81:1). *The mystery of Elohim (God) should be finished, as he hath declared to his servants the prophets* (Revelation 10:7). Enoch is set before the heavenly tablets and told to read what is written there and mark every fact. The mystery is what stands written in heaven; the prophets read it and declare it, and the seventh trumpet brings it to pass.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’$n$),
(13415,81,2,81,2,$n$*And I observed the heavenly tablets, and read everything which was written (thereon) and understood everything, and read the book of all the deeds of mankind, and of all the children of flesh that shall be upon the earth to the remotest generations.* (1 Enoch 81:2). *The mystery of Elohim (God) should be finished, as he hath declared to his servants the prophets* (Revelation 10:7). Enoch read the heavenly tablets and the book of all the deeds of mankind to the remotest generations. The prophet does not invent the mystery; he reads it where it is already written.$n$,$n$And I observed the heavenly tablets, and read everything which was written (thereon) and understood everything, and read the book of all the deeds of mankind, and of all the children of flesh that shall be upon the earth to the remotest generations.$n$),
(13433,90,17,90,29,$n$*And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.* (1 Enoch 90:29). The restored library saw the end of the measuring — not the old house propped up but *a new house... greater and loftier than the first*, into which the Lord of the sheep gathers all his flock. So the angel's reed to *measure the temple of Elohim (God), and the altar, and them that worship therein* (Revelation 11:1) marks off the house being built for the regathered: the worshippers numbered now are the sheep brought home into the greater house, the restoration of all Yashar'el (Israel).$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.$n$),
(13770,20,5,20,5,$n$*Michael, one of the holy angels, to wit, he that is set over the best part of mankind and over chaos.* (1 Enoch 20:5). The library names Michael's very charge: *set over the best part of mankind* — over the people of the promise — *and over chaos.* That is exactly his work in the vision: *Michael and his angels fought against the dragon* (Revelation 12:7), the guardian of the covenant people warring against the chaos-serpent who would devour the woman's child.$n$,$n$Michael, one of the holy angels, to wit, he that is set over the best part of mankind and over chaos.$n$),
(13799,90,12,90,20,$n$*And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.* (1 Enoch 90:20). *Whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world* (Revelation 13:8). Enoch saw the books opened before the Lord of the sheep on his throne, and elsewhere *the books of the living were opened before Him* (1 Enoch 47:3). The worshippers of the beast are not in that book; the names in it were written before the beast rose.$n$,$n$And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.$n$),
(13805,90,14,90,18,$n$*And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep came unto them and took in His hand the staff of His wrath, and smote the earth, and the earth clave asunder, and all the beasts and all the birds of the heaven fell from among those sheep, and were swallowed up in the earth and it covered them.* (1 Enoch 90:18). *As many as would not worship the image of the beast should be killed* (Revelation 13:15). Enoch saw the end of every beast and bird that devoured the sheep: the Lord of the sheep came with the staff of his wrath and the earth swallowed them. The beast and the false prophet go into the fire (Revelation 19:20); the beasts of the vision go into the earth. The fire the false prophet calls down is not the fire that has the last word.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep came unto them and took in His hand the staff of His wrath, and smote the earth, and the earth clave asunder, and all the beasts and all the birds of the heaven fell from among those sheep, and were swallowed up in the earth and it covered them.$n$),
(13836,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *One sat like unto the Son of Adam* (Revelation 14:14) — the comparative preserved: one *like* the Son of Adam, and the Standard he is like is the one Enoch heard named: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* The crowned cloud-rider is that Son of Adam, who took flesh and remains the Formed.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(14898,90,12,90,20,$n$*And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.* (1 Enoch 90:20). *The books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life* (Revelation 20:12). Enoch saw the sealed books taken and opened before the Lord of the sheep on his throne, and in the Parables *the books of the living were opened before Him* (1 Enoch 47:3). The books of deeds and the book of the living, opened together for judgment, are the books of the great white throne.$n$,$n$And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.$n$),
(14941,25,5,25,5,$n$*Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.* (1 Enoch 25:5). Enoch was shown the tree of life transplanted to the holy place, its fruit for food to the elect. John sees the transplanting done — the tree *in the midst of the street* of the city, *and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations* (Revelation 22:2). The fruit reserved for the elect is theirs; the leaves reach the nations through them.$n$,$n$Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.$n$),
(15001,60,1,60,1,$n$*In the year 500, in the seventh month, on the fourteenth day of the month in the life of Enoch. In that Parable I saw how a mighty quaking made the heaven of heavens to quake, and the host of the El Elyon (Most High), and the angels, a thousand thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, were disquieted with a great disquiet.* (1 Enoch 60:1). The Hebrew library numbered the throne-host exactly as John does: *a thousand thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand,* the angels of the Most High; and *the Head of Days sat on the throne of His glory, and the angels and the righteous stood around Him* (1 Enoch 60:2) — the very picture of the elders and myriads who fall down and worship before the throne (Revelation 4:10).$n$,$n$In the year 500, in the seventh month, on the fourteenth day of the month in the life of Enoch. In that Parable I saw how a mighty quaking made the heaven of heavens to quake, and the host of the El Elyon (Most High), and the angels, a thousand thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, were disquieted with a great disquiet.$n$),
(15003,39,11,40,2,$n$*And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.* (1 Enoch 40:2). Enoch saw the four John sees: four presences on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, whose praises he heard (1 Enoch 40:3). John's *four beasts* who *rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy* (Revelation 4:8) are the same four about the same throne.$n$,$n$And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.$n$),
(15004,71,5,71,5,$n$*And he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens, And I saw there as it were a structure built of crystals, And between those crystals tongues of living fire.* (1 Enoch 71:5). Enoch saw the throne-room floored and walled with crystal — *a structure built of crystals* — the same clear, shining expanse John names *a sea of glass like unto crystal* (Revelation 4:6). The crystal pavement of the throne-house the seers of Yashar'el (Israel) beheld is the crystal sea before the throne, the clear floor of the heavenly sanctuary.$n$,$n$And he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens, And I saw there as it were a structure built of crystals, And between those crystals tongues of living fire.$n$),
(15005,71,8,71,8,$n$*And I saw angels who could not be counted, A thousand thousands, and ten thousand times ten thousand, Encircling that house. And Michael, and Raphael, and Gabriel, and Phanuel, And the holy angels who are above the heavens, Go in and out of that house.* (1 Enoch 71:8). *Him that liveth for ever and ever* (Revelation 4:9) sits in a house Enoch saw: a structure built of crystals with tongues of living fire between them (1 Enoch 71:5), encircled by angels beyond counting. It is the throne-room John enters.$n$,$n$And I saw angels who could not be counted, A thousand thousands, and ten thousand times ten thousand, Encircling that house. And Michael, and Raphael, and Gabriel, and Phanuel, And the holy angels who are above the heavens, Go in and out of that house.$n$),
(15006,14,18,18,12,$n$*And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.* (1 Enoch 18:12). In the same vision where Enoch reached the throne of Yahuah (God), he passed the lofty throne-room John is now caught up into — *a door was opened in heaven* (Revelation 4:1), the throne *set in heaven* (Revelation 4:2). The seers of Yashar'el (Israel) ascended to behold what John beholds: the throne of the living Elohim (God) above the firmament.$n$,$n$And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.$n$),
(15014,62,9,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). In Enoch the Elect One is set *on the throne of His glory* (1 Enoch 62:6) and before him the kings and mighty fall — the same enthroned, worshipped Son of Adam John beholds receiving *blessing, and honour, and glory, and power* with him that sits on the throne (Revelation 5:13). The Formed Son seated and worshipped, distinct from Yahuah (God) of Spirits who seated him, is the frame the library and the seer share.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(15015,62,6,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing* (Revelation 5:12). The dignity the Lamb receives is the seat Enoch saw given: the Elect One placed on the throne of glory by Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, to judge. The Lamb receives; the Father gives.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(15033,18,11,18,12,$n$*And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.* (1 Enoch 18:12). The bottomless pit the seer sees unlocked (Revelation 9:1) is the waste place at the end of heaven and earth that Enoch was shown — neither firmament above nor earth beneath, the very abyss the fallen star is given the key to open.$n$,$n$And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.$n$),
(15034,18,13,18,15,$n$*And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* (1 Enoch 18:15). The star fallen from heaven (Revelation 9:1) is one of these transgressing stars Enoch named — the host that broke the commandment and was bound in the prison-pit; the fall the seer watches is the fall the older library had already charted.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$),
(15035,18,15,18,11,$n$*And I saw a deep abyss, with columns of heavenly fire, and among them I saw columns of fire fall, which were beyond measure alike towards the height and towards the depth.* (1 Enoch 18:11). *There arose a smoke out of the pit, as the smoke of a great furnace* (Revelation 9:2). Enoch saw the abyss with its columns of heavenly fire beyond measure. The smoke rises from a fire that was seen before the pit was opened.$n$,$n$And I saw a deep abyss, with columns of heavenly fire, and among them I saw columns of fire fall, which were beyond measure alike towards the height and towards the depth.$n$),
(15036,21,5,21,6,$n$*These are of the number of the stars of heaven, which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord), and are bound here till ten thousand years, the time entailed by their sins, are consummated.’* (1 Enoch 21:6). *I saw a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit* (Revelation 9:1). Enoch was told who is bound in that place: stars of heaven that transgressed the commandment, bound till their ten thousand years are consummated. The pit has prisoners before it has a key.$n$,$n$These are of the number of the stars of heaven, which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord), and are bound here till ten thousand years, the time entailed by their sins, are consummated.’$n$),
(15057,99,7,99,7,$n$*And they who worship stones, and grave images of gold and silver and wood and stone and clay, and those who worship impure spirits and demons, and all kinds of idols not according to knowledge, shall get no manner of help from them.* (1 Enoch 99:7). The restored library binds the two charges into one, just as the seer does: those who *worship... grave images of gold and silver and wood* and *worship impure spirits and demons* — idol-worship and devil-worship together, exactly *the works of their hands, that they should not worship devils, and idols of gold, and silver* (Revelation 9:20). And, as Enoch warns, the idols *shall get no manner of help from them*: the plagues fall and the breathless gods cannot save.$n$,$n$And they who worship stones, and grave images of gold and silver and wood and stone and clay, and those who worship impure spirits and demons, and all kinds of idols not according to knowledge, shall get no manner of help from them.$n$),
(15091,108,3,108,3,$n$*And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* (1 Enoch 108:3). *Whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb* (Revelation 13:8). Enoch knows the book and the blotting: *their names shall be blotted out of the book of life.* The names were written before the foundation of the world; the beast's worshippers are not among them, and the wheat that falls away is blotted out. No name is added after.$n$,$n$And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.$n$),
(15167,18,14,18,16,$n$*And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’* (1 Enoch 18:16). *That he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled* (Revelation 20:3). Enoch saw the rebels bound *till the time when their guilt should be consummated* — a fixed term, after which comes the final fire. The binding of the dragon has the same shape: a term, then the end.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$),
(16012,1,9,1,9,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* Enoch frames his prophecy with this advent twice over, and it is 1:9 that Jude quotes by name.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(16298,14,1,14,1,$n$1 Enoch 14:1 — *The book of the words of righteousness, and of the reprimand of the eternal Watchers in accordance with the command of the Holy Great One in that vision.* The heading of the very document Enoch writes out and reads before Elohim (God) in 13:6 and 13:10 — a book of reprimand, not of pardon.$n$,$n$The book of the words of righteousness, and of the reprimand of the eternal Watchers in accordance with the command of the Holy Great One in that vision.$n$),
(16669,21,7,18,16,$n$1 Enoch 18:16 — *And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’* Enoch revisits the same prison of the stars later in the journey, repeating the binding-till-judgement of 1 Enoch 18:16 word for word.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$),
(16701,16,3,16,3,$n$1 Enoch 16:3 — *“You have been in heaven, but all the mysteries had not yet been revealed to you, and you knew worthless ones, and these in the hardness of your hearts you have made known to the women, and through these mysteries women and men work much evil on earth."* Enoch's own word explains why the women of 19:2 become agents of destruction: the Watchers taught them the forbidden mysteries.$n$,$n$“You have been in heaven, but all the mysteries had not yet been revealed to you, and you knew worthless ones, and these in the hardness of your hearts you have made known to the women, and through these mysteries women and men work much evil on earth."$n$),
(16705,15,10,15,12,$n$1 Enoch 15:12 — *And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.* This is the defiling and leading-astray of mankind that Uriel shows Enoch in 19:1, the same spirits at work.$n$,$n$And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.$n$),
(16706,15,8,15,10,$n$1 Enoch 15:10 — *[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]* Enoch's own earlier vision identifies the form-shifting spirits of 19:1 as the earth-bound evil spirits sprung from the dead giants.$n$,$n$[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]$n$),
(16715,21,6,18,15,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* The luminaries Raguel takes vengeance on in 1 Enoch 20:4 are these stars that broke their appointed order.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$),
(16716,21,5,18,14,$n$1 Enoch 18:14 — *The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.* Raguel's vengeance on the world of the luminaries in 1 Enoch 20:4 is the binding of the transgressing stars Enoch sees imprisoned one chapter later.$n$,$n$The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.$n$),
(16721,40,9,40,9,$n$1 Enoch 40:9 — *And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’* Enoch names Michael first again among the archangels, the same honoured prince of 1 Enoch 20:5.$n$,$n$And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’$n$),
(16731,19,1,19,1,$n$1 Enoch 19:1 — *And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* The same Uriel who guides Enoch names the term of this prison: the fallen angels stand here till the great judgement.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$),
(16739,18,12,18,13,$n$1 Enoch 18:13–14 — *I saw there seven stars like great burning mountains, and to me, when I inquired regarding them, The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.* Enoch's earlier journey shows the very same seven bound stars and the same prison-of-the-host that he revisits in 21:4-5.$n$,$n$I saw there seven stars like great burning mountains, and to me, when I inquired regarding them,$n$),
(16751,21,5,18,14,$n$1 Enoch 18:14 — *The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.* The chapter-21 cell Enoch toured is the same prison of the angels named in Enoch 22:7.$n$,$n$The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.$n$),
(16775,18,8,18,8,$n$1 Enoch 18:8 — *But the middle one reached to heaven like the throne of Elohim (God), of alabaster, and the summit of the throne was of sapphire.* Enoch had already seen this central throne-mountain among the seven on his earlier journey, the same height-excelling middle peak resembling the seat of a throne (24:3).$n$,$n$But the middle one reached to heaven like the throne of Elohim (God), of alabaster, and the summit of the throne was of sapphire.$n$),
(17136,15,7,15,7,$n$1 Enoch 15:7 — *And therefore I have not appointed wives for you; for as for the spiritual ones of the heaven, in heaven is their dwelling.* Chapter 25 in this parse is a verbatim duplicate of chapter 15; the same word on the origin of evil spirits stands in both places.$n$,$n$And therefore I have not appointed wives for you; for as for the spiritual ones of the heaven, in heaven is their dwelling.$n$),
(17235,72,3,72,3,$n$1 Enoch 72:3 — *And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.* The Astronomical Book opens by repeating this very vision, confirming the twelve portals Enoch first glimpses here in chapter 33.$n$,$n$And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.$n$),
(17245,76,1,76,1,$n$1 Enoch 76:1 — *And at the ends of the earth I saw twelve portals open to all the quarters (of the heaven), from which the winds go forth and blow over the earth.* Enoch's own Luminaries section widens chapter 34's three-per-quarter gates into the twelve portals of the winds.$n$,$n$And at the ends of the earth I saw twelve portals open to all the quarters (of the heaven), from which the winds go forth and blow over the earth.$n$),
(17258,34,2,34,2,$n$1 Enoch 34:2 — *And here I saw three portals of heaven open in the heaven: through each of them proceed north winds: when they blow there is cold, hail, frost, snow, dew, and rain.* The journey of chapter 34 already met the west portals; chapter 35:1 returns to describe them, marking them small such as he had seen in the east.$n$,$n$And here I saw three portals of heaven open in the heaven: through each of them proceed north winds: when they blow there is cold, hail, frost, snow, dew, and rain.$n$),
(17270,77,1,77,1,$n$1 Enoch 77:1 — *And the first quarter is called the east, because it is the first: and the second, the south, because the El Elyon (Most High) will descend there, yea, there in quite a special sense will He who is blessed for ever descend.* Enoch's own Luminaries book names the same four quarters he surveys here, confirming one consistent cosmology across the books.$n$,$n$And the first quarter is called the east, because it is the first: and the second, the south, because the El Elyon (Most High) will descend there, yea, there in quite a special sense will He who is blessed for ever descend.$n$),
(17356,22,14,22,7,$n$*And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’* (1 Enoch 22:7). The voice that *crieth unto me from the ground* (Genesis 4:10) is given a seed-war shape in the restored apocalyptic: the spirit of Abel makes ceaseless suit against Cain *till his seed is destroyed* — the cry for justice running until the wicked seed is cut off from among *the seed of men*.$n$,$n$And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’$n$),
(17390,15,8,15,10,$n$*[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]* (1 Enoch 15:10). The *mighty men which were of old, men of renown* (Genesis 6:4) leave a residue after the flesh perishes: the witness teaches that the spirits of these giants remain on the earth — the corruption of the Watcher-mixing outlasting its bodies, the unclean spirits loosed in the world.$n$,$n$[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]$n$),
(17391,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). The *men of renown* of Genesis 6:4 become, in their spirits, the afflicting powers — the demonic legacy of the Nephilim, the seed-war's cosmic front continuing to *work destruction on the earth* long after the giants' flesh has fallen.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(17913,1,9,1,9,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* Enoch's first parable already declared the 'judgement upon all' that chapter 37 reopens (1 Enoch 1:7).$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(17929,62,9,46,4,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* Enoch's parables name the Son of Adam as the One who unseats the kings and mighty that 38:6 sees cast down from their thrones.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(17936,45,3,45,3,$n$1 Enoch 45:3 — *On that day Mine Elect One shall sit on the throne of glory And shall try their works, And their places of rest shall be innumerable. And their souls shall grow strong within them when they see Mine elect ones, And those who have called upon My glorious name:* Enoch's own parables name the same enthronement, the Elect One on the throne of glory trying works, that 38:10 declares.$n$,$n$On that day Mine Elect One shall sit on the throne of glory And shall try their works, And their places of rest shall be innumerable. And their souls shall grow strong within them when they see Mine elect ones, And those who have called upon My glorious name:$n$),
(17953,45,3,45,3,$n$1 Enoch 45:3 — *On that day Mine Elect One shall sit on the throne of glory And shall try their works, And their places of rest shall be innumerable. And their souls shall grow strong within them when they see Mine elect ones, And those who have called upon My glorious name:* The same Elect One on the same throne of glory; what He speaks from it in 1 Enoch 39:5 He executes here as judgement of works.$n$,$n$On that day Mine Elect One shall sit on the throne of glory And shall try their works, And their places of rest shall be innumerable. And their souls shall grow strong within them when they see Mine elect ones, And those who have called upon My glorious name:$n$),
(17995,60,11,60,11,$n$1 Enoch 60:11 — *And the other angel who went with me and showed me what was hidden told me what is first and last in the heaven in the height, and beneath the earth in the depth, and at the ends of the heaven, and on the foundation of the heaven.* Enoch's own Parables expand the balance of 41:1, showing the weighing reckoned spirit by spirit beside the chambers of the winds.$n$,$n$And the other angel who went with me and showed me what was hidden told me what is first and last in the heaven in the height, and beneath the earth in the depth, and at the ends of the heaven, and on the foundation of the heaven.$n$),
(18047,72,1,72,1,$n$1 Enoch 72:1 — *The book of the courses of the luminaries of the heaven, the relations of each, according to their classes, their dominion and their seasons, according to their names and places of origin, and according to their months, which Uriel, the holy angel, who was with me, who is their guide, showed me; and he showed me all their laws exactly as they are, and how it is with regard to all the years of the world and unto eternity, till the new creation is accomplished which dureth till eternity.* — the Luminaries book unfolds in detail the chambers Enoch only glimpses in 44:1.$n$,$n$The book of the courses of the luminaries of the heaven, the relations of each, according to their classes, their dominion and their seasons, according to their names and places of origin, and according to their months, which Uriel, the holy angel, who was with me, who is their guide, showed me; and he showed me all their laws exactly as they are, and how it is with regard to all the years of the world and unto eternity, till the new creation is accomplished which dureth till eternity.$n$),
(18922,62,1,61,8,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* The Father places the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge and weigh deeds — the same throne-of-glory judgement 45:3 announces.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(18955,62,7,71,14,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — *And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* Parables restates 46:3 — the same Son of Adam over whom righteousness abides, never forsaken by the Head of Days.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(18995,62,1,61,8,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* The Son of Adam named in 48:2 is the Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(19003,51,1,51,1,$n$1 Enoch 51:1 — *And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* Enoch's own ch51 makes the Elect One the agent of resurrection — the rising of the righteous who fell asleep in Him.$n$,$n$And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.$n$),
(19007,62,1,61,8,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* The office of judging the secret things named in 49:4 is the throne-of-glory judgement given here.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(19019,51,1,51,1,$n$1 Enoch 51:1 — *And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* Enoch's own next chapter sets the righteous judgement of 50:4 after the resurrection, when the Elect One arises to judge.$n$,$n$And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.$n$),
(19023,108,3,108,3,$n$1 Enoch 108:3 — *And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* Enoch's own books show the inverse of 50:4's verdict: the unrepentant blotted out, while the elect's names stand.$n$,$n$And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.$n$),
(19054,61,8,61,8,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* Enoch's own parallel: the Father places the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge, the same enthronement as 51:3.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(19847,53,1,53,1,$n$1 Enoch 53:1 — *There mine eyes saw a deep valley with open mouths, and all who dwell on the earth and sea and islands shall bring to him gifts and presents and tokens of homage, but that deep valley shall not become full.* The very next vision shows the same deep valley, now open-mouthed for judgment, the continuation of the leveled mountains of chapter 52.$n$,$n$There mine eyes saw a deep valley with open mouths, and all who dwell on the earth and sea and islands shall bring to him gifts and presents and tokens of homage, but that deep valley shall not become full.$n$),
(19866,62,9,46,4,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* The named Son of Adam executes the very judgement on the kings and mighty for whom the instruments are prepared in 53:6.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(19885,61,8,61,8,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* Enoch repeats the very enthronement of 55:4 — the Father seats the Formed Son to judge.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(19917,53,4,53,3,$n$1 Enoch 53:3 — *For I saw all the angels of punishment abiding (there) and preparing all the instruments of Satan.* The same hosts of punishing angels Enoch saw being readied in ch53 now go forth bearing their scourges and chains in 56:1.$n$,$n$For I saw all the angels of punishment abiding (there) and preparing all the instruments of Satan.$n$),
(19941,60,11,60,11,$n$1 Enoch 60:11 — *And the other angel who went with me and showed me what was hidden told me what is first and last in the heaven in the height, and beneath the earth in the depth, and at the ends of the heaven, and on the foundation of the heaven.* The next chapter unfolds the same weighed order of winds and moon-lights Enoch glimpses here in their faithful orbit.$n$,$n$And the other angel who went with me and showed me what was hidden told me what is first and last in the heaven in the height, and beneath the earth in the depth, and at the ends of the heaven, and on the foundation of the heaven.$n$),
(19972,62,1,62,2,$n$1 Enoch 62:2 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.* The next chapter repeats the enthronement and adds what is poured out on him: the spirit of righteousness, and the word of his mouth that slays the sinners.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.$n$),
(21271,62,10,46,5,$n$1 Enoch 46:5 — *[And he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms] Because they do not extol and praise Him, Nor humbly acknowledge whence the kingdom was bestowed upon them.* The kings who perish for ever (63:9) are those put down for refusing to acknowledge the One from whom their kingdom was bestowed.$n$,$n$[And he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms] Because they do not extol and praise Him, Nor humbly acknowledge whence the kingdom was bestowed upon them.$n$),
(21272,62,9,46,4,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* The Son of Adam who drives the sinners from the earth (63:6) is the same One seen a chapter before breaking the teeth of the sinners.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(21304,10,20,10,20,$n$1 Enoch 10:20 — *And cleanse thou the earth from all oppression, and from all unrighteousness, and from all sin, and from all godlessness: and all the uncleanness that is wrought upon the earth destroy from off the earth.* Enoch's word to Noah in 65:12 repeats the cleansing he was earlier commanded to announce over the post-Flood earth.$n$,$n$And cleanse thou the earth from all oppression, and from all unrighteousness, and from all sin, and from all godlessness: and all the uncleanness that is wrought upon the earth destroy from off the earth.$n$),
(21397,39,6,61,4,$n$1 Enoch 61:4 — *The elect shall begin to dwell with the elect, And those are the measures which shall be given to faith And which shall strengthen righteousness.* The same gathering of the elect and righteous Enoch beheld earlier in the Parables, now seen dwelling in their heavenly place in 71:7.$n$,$n$The elect shall begin to dwell with the elect, And those are the measures which shall be given to faith And which shall strengthen righteousness.$n$),
(21407,70,1,71,1,$n$1 Enoch 71:1 — *And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* Chapter 71 reopens and re-seals the very ascent of 70:1 — the visionary repetition marking the climax of the Parables.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$),
(22500,82,5,82,4,$n$1 Enoch 82:4 — *Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.* To complete the years *with righteousness* (74:13) is to walk as the righteous of this blessing walk — not sinning as the sinners in the reckoning of their days.$n$,$n$Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.$n$),
(22503,82,3,82,5,$n$1 Enoch 82:5 — *Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.* Those who walk in the 364-day order of 74:13 are the righteous of 82:4; those who sin in the reckoning are the men of 82:5, at fault, not reckoning the four days. The order has two sides, and Enoch names both.$n$,$n$Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.$n$),
(22534,21,6,18,15,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* The Astronomical Book repeats word for word the earlier vision of the prison of the transgressing stars.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$),
(22549,74,11,74,11,$n$1 Enoch 74:11 — *And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.* The thirty days the moon falls behind the sun and stars in five years is the lunar shortfall 78:4–5 records; the solar order leads, the moon lags.$n$,$n$And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.$n$),
(22550,74,10,82,5,$n$1 Enoch 82:5 — *Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.* Enoch's own luminary book fixes the same solar reckoning Enoch 78:4 gives to the sun's revolution.$n$,$n$Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.$n$),
(22559,74,11,74,11,$n$1 Enoch 74:11 — *And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.* The same lag of the moon behind the sun Enoch already gave in the courses of the luminaries — the solar year is the primary order.$n$,$n$And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.$n$),
(22579,82,5,82,4,$n$1 Enoch 82:4 — *Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.* The blessing on those who keep the commandments (81:10) is given its calendar here: blessed are those who do not sin in the reckoning of their days. Keeping the commandments includes keeping the count.$n$,$n$Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.$n$),
(22580,82,7,82,7,$n$1 Enoch 82:7 — *And the account thereof is accurate and the recorded reckoning thereof exact; for the luminaries, and months and festivals, and years and days, has Uriel shown and revealed to me, to whom Yahuah (Lord) of the whole creation of the world hath subjected the host of heaven.* The charge to preserve and not alter (81:10) rests on this: the reckoning Uriel showed is accurate and exact, and the host of heaven is subject to Yahuah (Lord). What is exact is not to be amended.$n$,$n$And the account thereof is accurate and the recorded reckoning thereof exact; for the luminaries, and months and festivals, and years and days, has Uriel shown and revealed to me, to whom Yahuah (Lord) of the whole creation of the world hath subjected the host of heaven.$n$),
(23826,9,4,9,4,$n$1 Enoch 9:4 — *And they said to Yahuah (Lord) of the ages: ‘Lord of lords, Elohim (God) of gods, King of kings, and Elohim (God) of the ages, the throne of Thy glory (standeth) unto all the generations of the ages, and Thy name holy and glorious and blessed unto all the ages!* the angels' first cry against the Watchers names the same everlasting throne Enoch blesses here.$n$,$n$And they said to Yahuah (Lord) of the ages: ‘Lord of lords, Elohim (God) of gods, King of kings, and Elohim (God) of the ages, the throne of Thy glory (standeth) unto all the generations of the ages, and Thy name holy and glorious and blessed unto all the ages!$n$),
(25314,94,6,96,5,$n$1 Enoch 96:5 — *Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.* The very violence and oppression of Enoch's wicked path (93:6) is the woe the next chapter sentences.$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$),
(25412,104,9,104,7,$n$1 Enoch 104:7 — *And, although ye sinners say: “All our sins shall not be searched out and be written down,” nevertheless they shall write down all your sins every day.* What 98:7 warns — that every sin is seen in heaven — 104:7 confirms against the sinners' own denial: all of it is written down, every day.$n$,$n$And, although ye sinners say: “All our sins shall not be searched out and be written down,” nevertheless they shall write down all your sins every day.$n$),
(25419,94,7,97,8,$n$1 Enoch 97:8 — *Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.* Enoch's earlier woe names the same gold-and-silver pride that 98:2 dresses in royal purple.$n$,$n$Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.$n$),
(25490,108,3,108,3,$n$1 Enoch 108:3 — *And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* Enoch's own closing names what 103:8 promises the righteous will never suffer — the blotting falls only on the sinner.$n$,$n$And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.$n$),
(25507,108,3,108,3,$n$1 Enoch 108:3 — *And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* Enoch's own closing book confirms the asymmetry: the wicked are blotted out, while the righteous name of 104:8 endures.$n$,$n$And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.$n$),
(25549,104,6,103,5,$n$1 Enoch 103:5 — *Woe to you, ye sinners, when ye have died, If ye die in the wealth of your sins, And those who are like you say regarding you: “Blessed are the sinners: they have seen all their days.* Enoch's woe over the sinners who die in their sins is the woe the closing chapter (108) carries to its end.$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye sinners, when ye have died, If ye die in the wealth of your sins, And those who are like you say regarding you: “Blessed are the sinners: they have seen all their days.$n$),
(25566,81,1,81,1,$n$1 Enoch 81:1 — *And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’* The tables of the divisions Jubilees 1:29 describes are the same heavenly tablets Enoch was shown — the pre-written record of all the years.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’$n$),
(25593,72,1,72,1,$n$1 Enoch 72:1 — *The book of the courses of the luminaries of the heaven, the relations of each, according to their classes, their dominion and their seasons, according to their names and places of origin, and according to their months, which Uriel, the holy angel, who was with me, who is their guide, showed me; and he showed me all their laws exactly as they are, and how it is with regard to all the years of the world and unto eternity, till the new creation is accomplished which dureth till eternity.* The same luminaries Jubilees 2:9 makes the sign for seasons and feasts govern Enoch's calendar of the years.$n$,$n$The book of the courses of the luminaries of the heaven, the relations of each, according to their classes, their dominion and their seasons, according to their names and places of origin, and according to their months, which Uriel, the holy angel, who was with me, who is their guide, showed me; and he showed me all their laws exactly as they are, and how it is with regard to all the years of the world and unto eternity, till the new creation is accomplished which dureth till eternity.$n$),
(25597,60,14,41,4,$n$1 Enoch 41:4 — *And there I saw closed chambers out of which the winds are divided, the chamber of the hail and winds, the chamber of the mist, and of the clouds, and the cloud thereof hovers over the earth from the beginning of the world.* The chambers of hail and mist match Jubilees 2:2's angels of snow, hail and hoar frost.$n$,$n$And there I saw closed chambers out of which the winds are divided, the chamber of the hail and winds, the chamber of the mist, and of the clouds, and the cloud thereof hovers over the earth from the beginning of the world.$n$),
(25598,60,13,41,3,$n$1 Enoch 41:3 — *And there mine eyes saw the secrets of the lightning and of the thunder, and the secrets of the winds, how they are divided to blow over the earth, and the secrets of the clouds and dew, and there I saw from whence they proceed in that place and from whence they saturate the dusty earth.* The same governed winds, clouds, lightning and thunder that Jubilees 2:2 assigns to angelic spirits.$n$,$n$And there mine eyes saw the secrets of the lightning and of the thunder, and the secrets of the winds, how they are divided to blow over the earth, and the secrets of the clouds and dew, and there I saw from whence they proceed in that place and from whence they saturate the dusty earth.$n$),
(25627,6,6,6,6,$n$1 Enoch 6:6 — *And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* The 1 Enoch apparatus fixes the Watchers' descent to the same generation of Jared that Jubilees 4:15 names.$n$,$n$And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.$n$),
(25629,13,8,13,8,$n$1 Enoch 13:8 — *And behold a dream came to me, and visions fell down upon me, and I saw visions of chastisement, and a voice came bidding (me) I to tell it to the sons of heaven, and reprimand them.* The vision-and-witness commission of Jubilees 4:23 unfolds in the parallel Enoch apparatus.$n$,$n$And behold a dream came to me, and visions fell down upon me, and I saw visions of chastisement, and a voice came bidding (me) I to tell it to the sons of heaven, and reprimand them.$n$),
(25690,74,10,82,5,$n$1 Enoch 82:5 — *Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.* Enoch's luminary order names the exact 364-day reckoning Jubilees 6:32 commands Israel to observe.$n$,$n$Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.$n$),
(25691,74,13,74,12,$n$1 Enoch 74:12 — *And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.* The same 364-day order, completed *with perfect justice,* that Jubilees 6:32 says must not disturb its feasts.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$),
(25692,82,3,82,5,$n$1 Enoch 82:5 — *Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.* Jubilees 6:37 names the disturbing of the order outright — feasts confounded, the unclean day made holy. Enoch names its root: men at fault who do not reckon the four intercalary days, and so lose the year.$n$,$n$Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.$n$),
(25718,7,5,7,6,$n$1 Enoch 7:6 — *Then the earth laid accusation against the lawless ones.* the live Enoch testimony — the *seventh in his generation* whose commandment Jubilees 7:39 says Enoch handed to his sons' sons.$n$,$n$Then the earth laid accusation against the lawless ones.$n$),
(25721,26,1,26,1,$n$1 Enoch 26:1 — *And I went from thence to the middle of the earth, and I saw a blessed place in which there were trees with branches abiding and blooming [of a dismembered tree].* Enoch's vision of the middle of the earth — the holy mountain and Zion — is the same centre Jubilees 8:18 sets at the navel of the world.$n$,$n$And I went from thence to the middle of the earth, and I saw a blessed place in which there were trees with branches abiding and blooming [of a dismembered tree].$n$),
(25726,8,2,8,2,$n$1 Enoch 8:2 — *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* The Watchers' star-omens Kainam transcribes in Jubilees 8:3 are the very teaching 1 Enoch names by name.$n$,$n$And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.$n$),
(25927,15,10,15,12,$n$1 Enoch 15:12 — *And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.* Enoch foretold the very assault Noah's sons report in Jubilees 10:2 — the spirits rising up to lead astray and slay the sons of men.$n$,$n$And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.$n$),
(25953,19,1,19,1,$n$1 Enoch 19:1 — *And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* The evil spirits Abram prays to be delivered from in Jubilees 12:17 are the Watcher-spirits of the live 1 Enoch apparatus, who lead mankind astray into demon-worship.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$),
(25985,81,1,81,1,$n$1 Enoch 81:1 — *And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’* The four-hundred-year word of Jubilees 14:13 is read off the same heavenly tablets Enoch is shown — the history pre-written.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’$n$),
(29120,14,3,39,3,$n$1 Enoch 39:3 — *And in those days a whirlwind carried me off from the earth, And set me down at the end of the heavens.* The whirlwind that carried Enoch off from the earth is the whirlwind Jasher 3:36 gives for his ascent, told here by Enoch himself.$n$,$n$And in those days a whirlwind carried me off from the earth, And set me down at the end of the heavens.$n$),
(29122,70,1,71,1,$n$1 Enoch 71:1 — *And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* the heavenly translation Jasher 3:36 records, even the snow Jasher 3:38 finds at the place of his ascent.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$),
(29177,89,3,89,3,$n$1 Enoch 89:3 — *And I saw again, and behold fountains were opened on the surface of that great enclosure, and that water began to swell and rise upon the surface, and I saw that enclosure till all its surface was covered with water.* Enoch's Animal Apocalypse sees the same fountains opened that Jasher 6:14 names, the flood-vision live beside it.$n$,$n$And I saw again, and behold fountains were opened on the surface of that great enclosure, and that water began to swell and rise upon the surface, and I saw that enclosure till all its surface was covered with water.$n$),
(39145,103,4,103,4,$n$1 Enoch 103:4 — *And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.* The watcher-book and Wisdom of Solomon 3:1 speak one tongue: the righteous souls are kept, lit, and given peace in Yahuah's hand.$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$),
(39174,63,8,62,5,$n$1 Enoch 62:5 — *And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.* The fools who accounted his life madness (Wisdom of Solomon 5:4) are the kings whose faces fall when they at last behold him enthroned.$n$,$n$And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.$n$),
(39175,62,9,46,4,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* The mighty whom the Son of Adam casts down are the very ones who, in Wisdom of Solomon 5:3, repent and groan when they see the righteous exalted.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(43693,71,5,71,5,$n$1 Enoch 71:5 — *And he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens, And I saw there as it were a structure built of crystals, And between those crystals tongues of living fire.* Enoch's own book unfolds the translation Sirach 49:14 remembers, his spirit carried up to the heaven of heavens.$n$,$n$And he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens, And I saw there as it were a structure built of crystals, And between those crystals tongues of living fire.$n$),
(45458,14,15,14,18,$n$1 Enoch 14:18 — *And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* Adam's lost vision of the praising angels was a vision of this same throne-room that Enoch is shown.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(45459,14,11,18,4,$n$1 Enoch 18:4 — *I saw the winds of heaven which turn and bring the circumference of the sun and all the stars to their setting.* The sight of the angelic host that Adam lost outside the garden is exactly what Enoch, walking with Elohim, was caught up to behold.$n$,$n$I saw the winds of heaven which turn and bring the circumference of the sun and all the stars to their setting.$n$),
(45562,41,5,41,5,$n$*And I saw the chambers of the sun and moon, whence they proceed and whither they come again, and their glorious return, and how one is superior to the other, and their stately orbit, and how they do not leave their orbit, and they add nothing to their orbit and they take nothing from it, and they keep faith with each other, in accordance with the oath by which they are bound together.* (1 Enoch 41:5). 1 Enoch 41:5 --  Enoch shows the sun as an ordered servant kept under oath, not the god Adam dreaded in 16:3.$n$,$n$And I saw the chambers of the sun and moon, whence they proceed and whither they come again, and their glorious return, and how one is superior to the other, and their stately orbit, and how they do not leave their orbit, and they add nothing to their orbit and they take nothing from it, and they keep faith with each other, in accordance with the oath by which they are bound together.$n$),
(45738,40,9,40,9,$n$1 Enoch 40:9 — *And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’* The same three named angels who bear Adam's tokens in 1 Adam and Eve 31:5 stand named together among the four faces of the throne.$n$,$n$And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’$n$),
(45942,69,10,69,6,$n$1 Enoch 69:6 — *And the third was named Gâdreêl: he it is who showed the children of men all the blows of death, and he led astray Eve, and showed [the weapons of death to the sons of men] the shield and the coat of mail, and the sword for battle, and all the weapons of death to the children of men.* The same envy that now plots Adam's death in 1 Adam and Eve 47:7 first led Eve astray and brought the blows of death into the world.$n$,$n$And the third was named Gâdreêl: he it is who showed the children of men all the blows of death, and he led astray Eve, and showed [the weapons of death to the sons of men] the shield and the coat of mail, and the sword for battle, and all the weapons of death to the children of men.$n$),
(46048,32,4,24,4,$n$1 Enoch 24:4 — *And amongst them was a tree such as I had never yet smelt, neither was any amongst them nor were others like it: it had a fragrance beyond all fragrance, and its leaves and blooms and wood wither not for ever: and its fruit is beautiful, and its fruit resembles the dates of a palm.* The living tree behind the sword in 1 Adam and Eve 54:4 is this fragrant tree Enoch was shown — the tree no mortal may touch until the great judgement, when it is given to the righteous (1 Enoch 25:4–5).$n$,$n$And amongst them was a tree such as I had never yet smelt, neither was any amongst them nor were others like it: it had a fragrance beyond all fragrance, and its leaves and blooms and wood wither not for ever: and its fruit is beautiful, and its fruit resembles the dates of a palm.$n$),
(46116,69,6,8,2,$n$1 Enoch 8:2 — *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* The deceiver whose hollow promise is unmasked in 1-adam-eve 59:6 is the same liar whose deceit leads the whole earth astray into corruption.$n$,$n$And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.$n$),
(46438,19,1,19,1,$n$1 Enoch 19:1 — *And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* The many forms Satan takes to destroy Adam's soul in 2 Adam & Eve 3:15 are the same shape-shifting by which the fallen spirits defile mankind and are worshipped as gods.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$),
(46715,6,6,6,6,$n$1 Enoch 6:6 — *And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* The descent from the holy mountain into sin (22:10) is mirrored by the Watchers' own descent in the days of Jared in Enoch's book.$n$,$n$And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.$n$),
(48743,14,3,14,8,$n$1 Enoch 14:8 — *And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.* As Enoch was lifted by the winds and borne into heaven, so the angel bears Abraham up on the wings of the bird to be shown heaven and earth.$n$,$n$And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.$n$),
(48751,14,2,19,3,$n$1 Enoch 19:3 — *And I, Enoch, alone saw the vision, the ends of all things: and no man shall see as I have seen.* As Enoch alone saw the vision of the ends of all things, so Abraham is fed only by the angel's speech, sustained by the sight he is about to be given.$n$,$n$And I, Enoch, alone saw the vision, the ends of all things: and no man shall see as I have seen.$n$),
(48775,8,2,8,2,$n$1 Enoch 8:2 — *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* The Watchers' stolen lore of constellations and clouds is exactly the 'stars and clouds' Abraham binds to Azazel's portion in 14:4.$n$,$n$And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.$n$),
(48786,14,3,14,8,$n$1 Enoch 14:8 — *And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.* Abraham too is borne up as with many winds to the borders of the flaming fire (Apocalypse of Abraham 15:4); the wind-borne ascent is the shared pattern of the prophets caught up to heaven.$n$,$n$And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.$n$),
(48821,39,12,40,3,$n$1 Enoch 40:3 — *And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* Enoch likewise heard the four presences uttering praise before the throne of glory, the same song of peace Abraham hears taught by Yahoel.$n$,$n$And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.$n$),
(48824,14,3,14,8,$n$1 Enoch 14:8 — *And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.* Enoch too was lifted up by the winds and borne into heaven to behold the throne, the throne of fire Abraham sees in his own ascent.$n$,$n$And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.$n$),
(48830,39,11,40,2,$n$1 Enoch 40:2 — *And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.* Enoch too saw four presences encircling the throne of glory, the same fourfold company Abraham beholds round the throne of fire.$n$,$n$And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.$n$),
(48839,18,13,18,15,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* Abraham's powers of the stars under command match Enoch's host bound to their commandment and judged when they fail to keep it (Apocalypse of Abraham 19:9).$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$),
(48867,60,7,60,7,$n$1 Enoch 60:7 — *And on that day were two monsters parted, a female monster named Leviathan, to dwell in the abysses of the ocean over the fountains of the waters.* The Leviathan in his deep camping-ground that Abraham beholds is Enoch's Leviathan dwelling in the abysses of the waters.$n$,$n$And on that day were two monsters parted, a female monster named Leviathan, to dwell in the abysses of the ocean over the fountains of the waters.$n$),
(48977,1,9,1,9,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* The plagues prepared for the heathen in Apocalypse of Abraham 30:3 are this same judgment Enoch foresaw upon all the ungodly.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(49285,14,15,14,18,$n$1 Enoch 14:18 — *And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* Enoch's ascent to the lofty throne and the Glory none of flesh could behold is the elder pattern of Isaiah's angel from the seventh heaven (6:13) — it ain't new.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(49384,14,15,14,18,$n$1 Enoch 14:18 — *And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* Enoch too was brought before the lofty throne whose Glory none of flesh could behold — it ain't new.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(50233,15,10,15,12,$n$*And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.* (1 Enoch 15:12). The library names the very warfare Paul names: spirits that *rise up against the children of men.* This is why *we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers* (Ephesians 6:12) — the true adversary is the spirit-power, the unseen wickedness in high places, and the children of men stand against it not in the flesh but in the whole armour of Elohim (God).$n$,$n$And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.$n$),
(52064,108,3,108,3,$n$*And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* (1 Enoch 108:3). The library knows the dark side of the register: the names of the wicked *shall be blotted out of the book of life.* To be blotted out is the very judgement Yahuah (LORD) spoke at Sinai — *him will I blot out of my book* (Exodus 32:33). Paul writes the bright side: his fellowlabourers' *names are in the book of life* (Philippians 4:3), not blotted out but kept, enrolled among the holy ones whose names endure when sin has passed away.$n$,$n$And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.$n$),
(52065,104,2,104,1,$n$*I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.* (1 Enoch 104:1). *Whose names are in the book of life* (Philippians 4:3). Enoch swears to the righteous that their names are written before the glory of the Great One. Paul's fellow-labourers are written there; the writing was done in heaven, and the labour on earth reveals it.$n$,$n$I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.$n$),
(55120,70,1,71,1,$n$1 Enoch 71:1 — *And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* The uppermost dwellings this book promises Enoch will behold are the heavens the older Enoch book already says his spirit was translated into — a self-witness across the two books.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$),
(55165,72,3,72,3,$n$1 Enoch 72:3 — *And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.* The six gates of the sun Enoch measures here are the six portals his own Astronomical Book had already numbered.$n$,$n$And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.$n$),
(55168,72,5,72,6,$n$1 Enoch 72:6 — *In this way he rises in the first month in the great portal, which is the fourth [those six portals in the east].* The sun's gates that 2 Enoch 14:2 counts are the portals Enoch's own Astronomical Book numbers — the great portal, the fourth, where the sun rises in the first month.$n$,$n$In this way he rises in the first month in the great portal, which is the fourth [those six portals in the east].$n$),
(55177,74,11,74,11,$n$1 Enoch 74:11 — *And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.* The moon falling thirty days behind the sun in five years is the very deficiency Enoch's own Astronomical Book reckoned.$n$,$n$And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.$n$),
(55179,74,2,74,2,$n$1 Enoch 74:2 — *And all these Uriel, the holy angel who is the leader of them all, showed to me, and their positions, and I wrote down their positions as he showed them to me, and I wrote down their months as they were, and the appearance of their lights till fifteen days were accomplished.* The moon's reckoning through its gates, written down to the fifteenth day, is the lunar course Enoch's own Astronomical Book had already set down through the portals.$n$,$n$And all these Uriel, the holy angel who is the leader of them all, showed to me, and their positions, and I wrote down their positions as he showed them to me, and I wrote down their months as they were, and the appearance of their lights till fifteen days were accomplished.$n$),
(55189,6,6,6,6,$n$1 Enoch 6:6 — *And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* The descent to the place Ermon and the breaking of their vows on the hill is the very rebellion Enoch's own book names on Mount Hermon.$n$,$n$And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.$n$),
(55196,61,10,61,10,$n$1 Enoch 61:10 — *And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.* The cherubim, seraphim, and ordered powers of 2 Enoch 20:1 are the same summoned host the elder Enoch names before the throne of glory.$n$,$n$And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.$n$),
(55238,18,13,18,15,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* 1 Enoch's bound transgressor-host is the same rebellion in heaven 2 Enoch sees thrown down.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$),
(55244,69,20,69,16,$n$1 Enoch 69:16 — *And these are the secrets of this oath... And they are strong through his oath: And the heaven was suspended before the world was created, And for ever.* The hosts standing in their fiery order rest on the same created foundation 1 Enoch confesses, suspended by Him before the world was.$n$,$n$And these are the secrets of this oath... And they are strong through his oath: And the heaven was suspended before the world was created, And for ever.$n$),
(55283,81,3,81,6,$n$1 Enoch 81:6 — *One year we will leave thee with thy son, till thou givest thy (last) commands, that thou mayst teach thy children and record (it) for them, and testify to all thy children; and in the second year they shall take thee from their midst.* The year left to Enoch to teach his children and record it for them is the charge behind the books of Enoch's handwriting a later generation reads in 2 Enoch 35:2.$n$,$n$One year we will leave thee with thy son, till thou givest thy (last) commands, that thou mayst teach thy children and record (it) for them, and testify to all thy children; and in the second year they shall take thee from their midst.$n$),
(55302,81,2,81,2,$n$1 Enoch 81:2 — *And I observed the heavenly tablets, and read everything which was written (thereon) and understood everything, and read the book of all the deeds of mankind, and of all the children of flesh that shall be upon the earth to the remotest generations.* The works and sentences Enoch writes down in 2 Enoch 40:11 are the works of men he read on the heavenly tablets in his own book.$n$,$n$And I observed the heavenly tablets, and read everything which was written (thereon) and understood everything, and read the book of all the deeds of mankind, and of all the children of flesh that shall be upon the earth to the remotest generations.$n$),
(55362,98,7,98,7,$n$1 Enoch 98:7 — *And do not think in your spirit nor say in your heart that ye do not know and that ye do not see that every sin is every day recorded in heaven in the presence of the El Elyon (Most High).* The record kept so that none is hidden (2 Enoch 50:1) is the daily recording of every sin in heaven that Enoch's first book already warns of.$n$,$n$And do not think in your spirit nor say in your heart that ye do not know and that ye do not see that every sin is every day recorded in heaven in the presence of the El Elyon (Most High).$n$),
(55443,70,3,71,2,$n$1 Enoch 71:2 — *And I saw two streams of fire, And the light of that fire shone like hyacinth, And I fell on my face before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The taking of Enoch up to where Yahuah is in 2 Enoch 67:1 is the seizing and lifting up by Michael that Enoch's own earlier vision recounts.$n$,$n$And I saw two streams of fire, And the light of that fire shone like hyacinth, And I fell on my face before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(56509,5,7,5,4,$n$*But ye—ye have not been steadfast, nor done the commandments of Yahuah (Lord), But ye have turned away and spoken proud and hard words With your impure mouths against His greatness. Oh, ye hard-hearted, ye shall find no peace.* (1 Enoch 5:4). *Which delivered us from the wrath to come* (1 Thessalonians 1:10). Enoch names who the wrath is for: the hard-hearted who have not done the commandments of Yahuah (Lord) and shall find no peace. The Thessalonians are delivered from that, not because wrath is cancelled, but because they are not the hard-hearted; the next verse (1 Enoch 1:8) gives the righteous their peace.$n$,$n$But ye—ye have not been steadfast, nor done the commandments of Yahuah (Lord), But ye have turned away and spoken proud and hard words With your impure mouths against His greatness. Oh, ye hard-hearted, ye shall find no peace.$n$),
(56538,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). *At the coming of our Lord Yahusha HaMashiach (Lord Jesus Christ) with all his saints* (1 Thessalonians 3:13). Enoch carried the word long before Thessalonica: he comes with ten thousands of his holy ones to execute judgement upon all. It is the very prophecy Jude quotes by name as Enoch's; the day he comes with his holy ones is the day the ungodly are convicted.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(56544,51,1,51,1,$n$*And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* (1 Enoch 51:1). The library beholds the day of resurrection: *the earth shall give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received,* and *the Elect One shall arise.* This is the day Paul names — *Yahuah (Lord) himself shall descend from heaven with a shout... and the dead in Messiah (Christ) shall rise first* (1 Thessalonians 4:16). Sheol giving back what it received at the arising of the Elect One is the hope behind the rising of the dead in Messiah (Christ) — the righteous seed brought up out of Sheol at the descending of the King, the first resurrection, that the chosen should be saved.$n$,$n$And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.$n$),
(56570,58,3,58,3,$n$*And the righteous shall be in the light of the sun, And the elect in the light of eternal life: The days of their life shall be unending, And the days of the holy without number.* (1 Enoch 58:3). The Hebrew library sees the same destiny of the righteous: they *shall be in the light of the sun,* the elect *in the light of eternal life.* This is the lot of those Paul names *the children of light, and the children of the day... not of the night, nor of darkness* (1 Thessalonians 5:5) — the elect whose portion is light without end, set apart from the night that overtakes the sleeping.$n$,$n$And the righteous shall be in the light of the sun, And the elect in the light of eternal life: The days of their life shall be unending, And the days of the holy without number.$n$),
(56571,58,6,58,6,$n$*And there shall be a light that never endeth, And to a limit (lit. ‘number’) of days they shall not come, For the darkness shall first have been destroyed, [And the light established before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits] And the light of uprightness established for ever before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 58:6). *Ye are all the children of light, and the children of the day: we are not of the night, nor of darkness* (1 Thessalonians 5:5). Enoch saw the division made final: the darkness first destroyed, and a light that never ends established before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The children of the day inherit that light; the night they are not of is the darkness that is destroyed.$n$,$n$And there shall be a light that never endeth, And to a limit (lit. ‘number’) of days they shall not come, For the darkness shall first have been destroyed, [And the light established before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits] And the light of uprightness established for ever before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(56589,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). The Hebrew library beheld the very coming Paul proclaims: He *cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement... And to destroy all the ungodly.* Paul says *the Lord Yahusha (Lord Jesus) shall be revealed from heaven with his mighty angels, In flaming fire taking vengeance on them that know not Elohim (God)* (2 Thessalonians 1:7-8). The mighty angels attend him; the holy ones are another company — the seed of promise, gathered and coming with him into the land (Zechariah 14:5). The judgment to destroy the ungodly is the vengeance on them that obey not the gospel.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(56650,62,1,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Ask of me, and I shall give thee the heathen for thine inheritance* (Psalm 2:8). The King who asks is the Elect One Enoch saw placed on the throne of glory by Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The inheritance is given to the one who is seated.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(56651,62,9,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). The inheritance of *the heathen for thine inheritance* (Psalm 2:8) carries the judgment of the raging kings: the Son of Adam *shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats... And break the teeth of the sinners*. The kings who set themselves against the Anointed in Psalm 2:2 are put down before the enthroned Son of Adam; the nations given as inheritance are taken from the hand of the rebel kings.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(56652,48,8,63,1,$n$*In those days shall the mighty and the kings who possess the earth implore (Him) to grant them a little respite from His angels of punishment to whom they were delivered, that they might fall down and worship before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, and confess their sins before Him.* (1 Enoch 63:1). *Why do the heathen rage... The kings of the earth set themselves* (Psalm 2:1–2). Enoch saw where the raging ends: the mighty and the kings imploring for a little respite from the angels of punishment, that they might fall down and confess. He that sits in the heavens laughs (Psalm 2:4).$n$,$n$In those days shall the mighty and the kings who possess the earth implore (Him) to grant them a little respite from His angels of punishment to whom they were delivered, that they might fall down and worship before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, and confess their sins before Him.$n$),
(56797,19,1,19,1,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). The restored library already named the engine of the latter-time error: spirits *assuming many different forms* that *lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods.* Paul writes that *in the latter times some shall depart from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits, and doctrines of devils* (1 Timothy 4:1). The *seducing spirits* and *doctrines of devils* are these very deceiving spirits of Enoch's vision — not a new threat but the old work of the fallen, leading men to honour demons under a show of doctrine, until the day of the great judgement makes an end of them.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$),
(57163,61,8,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). The restored witness shows the same enthronement as *Sit thou at my right hand* (Psalm 110:1): the Head of Days (the Father) sets the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge — the chosen One seated by the Most High's own act, the Formed One given the seat of rule and judgement.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(57164,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). The restored witness names the enthroned One the *Son of Adam* — David's son after the flesh in the seed-of-Adam line — yet seated to judge by Yahuah (God) of Spirits, the very paradox of *Yahuah (LORD) said unto my Lord* (Psalm 110:1): the One of Adam's seed who is also the Lord enthroned at the right hand.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(57408,62,10,46,5,$n$*[And he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms] Because they do not extol and praise Him, Nor humbly acknowledge whence the kingdom was bestowed upon them.* (1 Enoch 46:5). The service of *all nations shall serve him* (Psalm 72:11) is refused by the proud kings, and so *he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms*. Those who will not fall down before the King and acknowledge His reign are cast from their seats; the nations that serve are blessed, the kings that withhold are abased.$n$,$n$[And he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms] Because they do not extol and praise Him, Nor humbly acknowledge whence the kingdom was bestowed upon them.$n$),
(57409,62,9,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). The falling-down of *all kings shall fall down before him* (Psalm 72:11) carries the abasing of the proud: the Son of Adam *Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats*. The kings who do not bow are pulled from their thrones before the enthroned Son of Adam — the universal dominion is no negotiation but the rule of the Chosen One.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(57410,62,6,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Yea, all kings shall fall down before him: all nations shall serve him* (Psalm 72:11). The King they fall before is the Elect One Enoch saw placed on the throne of glory to judge. The nations serve the one who is seated.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(59357,18,14,18,16,$n$*And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’* (1 Enoch 18:16). Enoch is shown the fallen host *bound... till the time when their guilt should be consummated* — held in a place of confinement until judgement. This is the *prison* Peter speaks of when the Messiah *went and preached unto the spirits in prison* (1 Peter 3:19): a real holding-place of bound spirits, kept against the appointed day, not annihilated but reserved.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$),
(59358,21,5,18,14,$n$*The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.* (1 Enoch 18:14). Enoch is brought to the place the angel names *a prison for the stars and the host of heaven* — the seven stars *which roll over the fire... which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (God).* It is the prison house of the angels; *this place is the prison of the angels, and here they will be imprisoned for ever* (1 Enoch 21:11). Peter names this same prison: *the spirits in prison* (1 Peter 3:19), the bound host of the days of Noah to whom the quickened Son proclaimed.$n$,$n$The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.$n$),
(59997,90,17,90,29,$n$1 Enoch 90:29 — *And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.* The house the Lord shall choose, named from the book of Enoch, is the new house Enoch saw the Lord gather His own into.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.$n$),
(60223,91,1,93,8,$n$*And after that in the sixth week all who live in it shall be blinded, And the hearts of all of them shall godlessly forsake wisdom. And in it a man shall ascend; And at its close the house of dominion shall be burnt with fire, And the whole race of the chosen root shall be dispersed.* (1 Enoch 93:8). 1 Enoch 91 —  — "I have read in the writing of Enoch that ye yourselves also shall depart from Yahuah" reaches for the very book of Enoch that foretells the generation of apostasy (self-link).$n$,$n$And after that in the sixth week all who live in it shall be blinded, And the hearts of all of them shall godlessly forsake wisdom. And in it a man shall ascend; And at its close the house of dominion shall be burnt with fire, And the whole race of the chosen root shall be dispersed.$n$),
(60447,21,10,21,10,$n$*And he said unto me: ‘This place is the prison of the angels, and here they will be imprisoned for ever.’* (1 Enoch 21:10). *Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness* (2 Peter 2:4). Enoch was shown the place and told what it is. The apostle points to the prison the library shows.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘This place is the prison of the angels, and here they will be imprisoned for ever.’$n$),
(62554,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). This is the very verse Jude quotes: *And Enoch also, the seventh from Adam, prophesied of these, saying, Behold, Yahuah (Lord) cometh with ten thousands of his saints, To execute judgment upon all, and to convince all that are ungodly among them of all their ungodly deeds which they have ungodly committed, and of all their hard speeches which ungodly sinners have spoken against him* (Jude 1:14-15). Word for word — *cometh with ten thousands,* *to execute judgment upon all,* *convict/convince all flesh... of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed,* *the hard things/hard speeches which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* An apostle, the brother of James, names *Enoch, the seventh from Adam* a true prophet and cites his book as prophecy. The library is one; it ain't new — the apostle reads the restored writing as the word it is.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(62589,21,6,18,15,$n$*And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* (1 Enoch 18:15). Enoch is shown the prison of *the stars... which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (God),* bound *till the time when their guilt should be consummated* (1 Enoch 21:7). These are Jude's *wandering stars, to whom is reserved the blackness of darkness for ever* (Jude 1:13) — the stars that would not keep their appointed course, the very image of the ungodly who keep not the faith once delivered.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$),
(66488,14,16,14,20,$n$*And the Great Glory sat thereon, and His raiment shone more brightly than the sun and was whiter than any snow.* (1 Enoch 14:20). *I saw Yahuah (the Lord) sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple* (Isaiah 6:1). Enoch saw the Great Glory seated, his raiment brighter than the sun and whiter than snow. The train that filled the temple is the raiment Enoch could not look upon.$n$,$n$And the Great Glory sat thereon, and His raiment shone more brightly than the sun and was whiter than any snow.$n$),
(66489,14,15,14,18,$n$*And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* (1 Enoch 14:18). *I saw Yahuah (the Lord) sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up* (Isaiah 6:1). Enoch saw the same lofty throne — crystal, wheels like the shining sun, cherubim — and the Glory none could approach (1 Enoch 14:20–21). The prophet and the patriarch stood before one throne.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(66492,39,13,40,4,$n$*The first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever.* (1 Enoch 40:4). *The whole earth is full of his glory* (Isaiah 6:3) is sung in heaven without ceasing: the first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever. One worship, in heaven and over all the earth.$n$,$n$The first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever.$n$),
(66493,39,12,40,3,$n$*And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* (1 Enoch 40:3). The seraphim who *cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy* (Isaiah 6:3) are the holy ones Enoch hears at the throne — the four presences who *uttered praises before Yahuah (God) of glory*. The restored witness shows the same ceaseless worship before the same throne of glory that filled Isaiah's temple.$n$,$n$And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.$n$),
(67773,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). The *righteous servant* who shall *justify many* (Isaiah 53:11) is the Son of Adam *born unto righteousness*, hidden from before the world and now revealed — the Elect One in whom righteousness dwells. The restored witness binds the suffering-and-justifying servant to the exalted Son of Adam before the Head of Days.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(67774,62,9,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). The servant who was *numbered with the transgressors* (Isaiah 53:12) — humbled, despised, slain — is the same Son of Adam exalted to judge the kings and the mighty. The pattern is one: rejected and cut off, then *divide him a portion with the great* (53:12); the suffering servant and the enthroned Elect One are the same Formed Son.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(69401,20,5,20,5,$n$1 Enoch 20:5 — *Michael, one of the holy angels, to wit, he that is set over the best part of mankind and over chaos.* Michael, named first to bury Adam, is the chief of the holy angels in the Watcher-tradition's own roster.$n$,$n$Michael, one of the holy angels, to wit, he that is set over the best part of mankind and over chaos.$n$),
(69749,45,4,45,4,$n$*Then will I cause Mine Elect One to dwell among them. And I will transform the heaven and make it an eternal blessing and light: And I will transform the earth and make it a blessing: And I will cause Mine elect ones to dwell upon it: But the sinners and evil-doers shall not set foot thereon.* (1 Enoch 45:4–5). *For, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth* (Isaiah 65:17). Enoch heard the same promise from the same mouth: the heaven transformed into an eternal blessing and light, the earth transformed into a blessing, the Elect One dwelling among his people. The prophet's new creation is the age of the Parables.$n$,$n$Then will I cause Mine Elect One to dwell among them. And I will transform the heaven and make it an eternal blessing and light:$n$),
(69782,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). *Yahuah (LORD) will come with fire, and with his chariots like a whirlwind, to render his anger with fury* (Isaiah 66:15); *by fire and by his sword will Yahuah (LORD) plead with all flesh* (66:16). 1 Enoch sees the same coming-in-judgement to *convict all flesh* — the verse Jude later quotes by name; the library's own witness to the fiery advent.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(69783,45,5,48,9,$n$*And I will give them over into the hands of Mine elect: As straw in the fire so shall they burn before the face of the holy: As lead in the water shall they sink before the face of the righteous, And no trace of them shall any more be found.* (1 Enoch 48:9). *By fire and by his sword will Yahuah (the LORD) plead with all flesh* (Isaiah 66:16); *neither shall their fire be quenched* (Isaiah 66:24). Enoch sees the sinners given into the hands of the elect, burning as straw before the face of the holy, sinking as lead before the face of the righteous. The fire that closes Isaiah is the fire of the Parables.$n$,$n$And I will give them over into the hands of Mine elect: As straw in the fire so shall they burn before the face of the holy: As lead in the water shall they sink before the face of the righteous, And no trace of them shall any more be found.$n$),
(69795,45,4,45,4,$n$*Then will I cause Mine Elect One to dwell among them. And I will transform the heaven and make it an eternal blessing and light: And I will transform the earth and make it a blessing: And I will cause Mine elect ones to dwell upon it: But the sinners and evil-doers shall not set foot thereon.* (1 Enoch 45:4–5). *As the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, shall remain before me* (Isaiah 66:22). Enoch heard Yahuah (Lord) promise to transform the heaven and the earth and set his elect upon it, the sinners shut out. The renewal in which the seed and the name remain is the renewal the Parables saw.$n$,$n$Then will I cause Mine Elect One to dwell among them. And I will transform the heaven and make it an eternal blessing and light:$n$),
(77220,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). *The chariots of Elohim (God) are twenty thousand, even thousands of angels: Yahuah (the Lord) is among them, as in Sinai* (Psalm 68:17): the psalm's thousands are angels, the chariotry of the coming One. Enoch's ten thousands of holy ones are another company — the seed of promise, gathered and coming with him into the land (Zechariah 14:5). The angels attend him; his saints come with him.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(80341,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). *Thou didst cause judgment to be heard from heaven; the earth feared, and was still* (Psalm 76:8): the restored apocalyptic sees the same judgment come down from above — He comes with His holy ones to execute judgment upon all, the earth made still before the One who arises to judge.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(86006,18,14,18,16,$n$*And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’* (1 Enoch 18:16). The *host of the high ones that are on high* whom Yahuah will *punish* (Isaiah 24:21) are the stars of heaven who transgressed — and Yahuah *bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated*. The punishment of the high host is their binding in the prison of the abyss.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$),
(86011,21,7,18,16,$n$*And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’* (1 Enoch 18:16). *They shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited* (Isaiah 24:22) — exactly the sentence Enoch sees: *bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated*. The host is shut in the pit *till the time* of visitation; the prophet and the witness see one judgment.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$),
(86012,21,6,18,15,$n$*And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* (1 Enoch 18:15). *Yahuah (LORD) shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high* (Isaiah 24:21) — the restored witness names that host: the stars that *transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (God)*, the rebel powers above who *did not come forth at their appointed times*. The high ones on high are the transgressing host bound for judgment.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$),
(90046,62,1,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Yahuah (The LORD) reigneth, he is clothed with majesty... the world also is stablished, that it cannot be moved* (Psalm 93:1). The restored witness shows the reign as the Father placing the Son on the throne of glory to judge; the One who reigns is the One who seats, and the One seated is the Formed.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(103259,41,5,41,5,$n$*And I saw the chambers of the sun and moon, whence they proceed and whither they come again, and their glorious return, and how one is superior to the other, and their stately orbit, and how they do not leave their orbit, and they add nothing to their orbit and they take nothing from it, and they keep faith with each other, in accordance with the oath by which they are bound together.* (1 Enoch 41:5). The sun and moon that *shall not smite thee by day... nor... by night* (Psalm 121:6) are not powers to dread but oath-bound servants of the Maker, keeping the courses he set. The Keeper rules the very lights, so they cannot harm the one he keeps.$n$,$n$And I saw the chambers of the sun and moon, whence they proceed and whither they come again, and their glorious return, and how one is superior to the other, and their stately orbit, and how they do not leave their orbit, and they add nothing to their orbit and they take nothing from it, and they keep faith with each other, in accordance with the oath by which they are bound together.$n$),
(114987,61,11,61,11,$n$*On that day shall raise one voice, and bless and glorify and exalt in the spirit of faith, and in the spirit of wisdom, and in the spirit of patience, and in the spirit of mercy, and in the spirit of judgement and of peace, and in the spirit of goodness, and shall all say with one voice: "Blessed is He, and may the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits be blessed for ever and ever."* (1 Enoch 61:11). The capstone's summons of *every thing that hath breath* is the host of heaven raising ONE voice — the same final, unanimous Hallelujah the Psalter ends on.$n$,$n$On that day shall raise one voice, and bless and glorify and exalt in the spirit of faith, and in the spirit of wisdom, and in the spirit of patience, and in the spirit of mercy, and in the spirit of judgement and of peace, and in the spirit of goodness, and shall all say with one voice: "Blessed is He, and may the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits be blessed for ever and ever."$n$),
(114988,39,12,40,3,$n$*And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* (1 Enoch 40:3). The praise the capstone commands below is already sounding above — the four presences before the throne uttering the praise *every thing that hath breath* is now gathered into.$n$,$n$And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.$n$),
(120191,14,15,14,18,$n$*And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* (1 Enoch 14:18). Enoch is carried up and sees the throne of the Most High, a vision twin to Daniel's — *his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire* (Daniel 7:9). The same heavenly throne-room of the Ancient of Days, seen by Enoch before Daniel.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(120469,104,2,104,2,$n$*Be hopeful; for aforetime ye were put to shame through ill and affliction; but now ye shall shine as the lights of heaven, ye shall shine and ye shall be seen, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to you.* (1 Enoch 104:2). *They that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament... as the stars for ever and ever* (Daniel 12:3). Enoch tells the righteous the same: they shall shine as the lights of heaven, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to them.$n$,$n$Be hopeful; for aforetime ye were put to shame through ill and affliction; but now ye shall shine as the lights of heaven, ye shall shine and ye shall be seen, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to you.$n$),
(120843,62,9,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). The pierced One *they shall look upon* (Zechariah 12:10) is the Son of Adam the restored witness sees revealed in the day — *this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen* — before whom the kings and the mighty are abased. The day of looking upon the pierced One is the day of the Son of Adam's appearing.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(120873,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). This is the very line Jude quotes, and it answers *Yahuah Elohai (the LORD my God) shall come, and all the saints with thee* (14:5). The holy ones who come with him are the seed of promise, gathered out of all nations and coming with him into the land while the ungodly are judged — not angels, and not souls come down from heaven.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$),
(121870,15,8,15,10,$n$*[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]* (1 Enoch 15:10). The library tells where these unclean spirits came from — the spirits of the giants, earth-bound, given over to the earth.$n$,$n$[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]$n$),
(121871,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). The very work of the demons in the tombs — afflicting, destroying — and they know their judgement is coming.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(121872,15,11,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). This is why they cry *art thou come hither to torment us before the time?* — they know the appointed day of the great judgement, and they tremble that He is here.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(122007,108,3,108,3,$n$*And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* (1 Enoch 108:3). Malachi's spared jewels — *I will spare them, as a man spareth his own son that serveth him* (Malachi 3:17) — stand against those whose *names shall be blotted out of the book of life*. The book of remembrance keeps the faithful; the wicked are blotted out.$n$,$n$And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.$n$),
(122747,15,11,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). The library tells where the unclean spirits came from — the souls of the dead giants, the offspring of the Watchers. These are the very devils the Son binds and casts out.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(124246,62,7,71,14,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). The library's own vision of the Son of Adam seated to judge — born unto righteousness, the Head of Days behind him, rewarding every man.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$),
(134196,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). The *unclean spirits* the twelve are given power over are named here — the spirits gone out from the slain giants, the offspring of the Watchers. The library tells you what they are; the Son gives His sent ones authority over them.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(134197,15,11,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). They destroy *until the day of the consummation* — but the Son, before that day, already hands their conquest to twelve men with nothing but a staff.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(134233,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). The library names the foul spirits the Son rebukes — the unclean spirits that *afflict* are the souls gone forth from the slain giants, born of the Watchers' rebellion.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(134234,15,11,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). These spirits *destroy until the day of the consummation* — but the Formed Son, with a word, charges this one to *come out of him, and enter no more*: a foretaste of the consummating judgement.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(135392,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). The library names what the *spirit* that *teareth* the child is — the afflicting spirits proceeding from the giants, the Watcher-rebellion's aftermath.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(135393,15,11,16,1,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). These spirits destroy until the judgment; the Son rebukes one here as a foretaste of the consummation that ends them.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$),
(135426,62,1,61,8,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *That ye may eat and drink at my table in my kingdom, and sit on thrones judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel)* (Luke 22:30). The Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge is the Son of Adam who shares that seat with the twelve.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$),
(135440,62,5,62,5,$n$*And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.* (1 Enoch 62:5). *Hereafter shall the Son of Adam sit on the right hand of the power of Elohim (God)* (Luke 22:69). Enoch saw the faces of those who see that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory — terror and pain. The council heard the claim; the vision shows them seeing it kept.$n$,$n$And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.$n$),
(135969,62,6,69,27,$n$*And he sat on the throne of his glory, And the sum of judgement was given unto the Son of Adam, And he caused the sinners to pass away and be destroyed from off the face of the earth, And those who have led the world astray.* (1 Enoch 69:27). *And hath given him authority to execute judgment also, because he is the Son of Adam* (John 5:27). Enoch saw the sum of judgement given to the Son of Adam on the throne of his glory. The authority is given — by the Father — and it is given to the Son of Adam by that name.$n$,$n$And he sat on the throne of his glory, And the sum of judgement was given unto the Son of Adam, And he caused the sinners to pass away and be destroyed from off the face of the earth, And those who have led the world astray.$n$),
(139484,1,4,1,4,$n$*And the eternal Elohim (God) will tread upon the earth, (even) on Mount Sinai, [And appear from His camp] And appear in the strength of His might from the heaven of heavens.* (1 Enoch 1:4). This is Micah's *tread upon the high places of the earth* (1:3) word for deed — *the eternal Elohim (God) will tread upon the earth*. The descending One who treads is the same in the prophet and the witness; he appears in the strength of his might.$n$,$n$And the eternal Elohim (God) will tread upon the earth, (even) on Mount Sinai, [And appear from His camp] And appear in the strength of His might from the heaven of heavens.$n$),
(140722,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). The afflicting spirit that seized the man is exactly what Enoch described — and it knows its Judge. When the Holy One of Elohim commands, the bound offspring of the Watchers must obey; the sentence already gone forth against them stands.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(140723,15,8,15,10,$n$*[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]* (1 Enoch 15:10). Enoch names the origin of the unclean spirits: they are the disembodied spirits of the giants, the offspring of the fallen Watchers, loosed upon the earth. This is the *unclean devil* the Son confronts.$n$,$n$[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]$n$),
(140747,15,9,15,11,$n$*And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.* (1 Enoch 15:11). The library names the unclean spirits Yahusha casts out — the disembodied spirits of the fallen Watchers' giant offspring, the very strong man's armoury now overcome.$n$,$n$And the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth, and cause trouble: they take no food, but nevertheless hunger and thirst, and cause offences.$n$),
(145066,96,1,96,5,$n$*Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.* (1 Enoch 96:5). Enoch's woe names Job's strong man — *He draweth also the mighty with his power: he riseth up, and no man is sure of life* (Job 24:22). The same trampling power that makes men despair of their lives is the very thing heaven marks for woe.$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$),
(145067,96,2,96,8,$n$*Woe to you, ye mighty, Who with might oppress the righteous; For the day of your destruction is coming. In those days many and good days shall come to the righteous—in the day of your judgement.* (1 Enoch 96:8). *They are exalted for a little while, but are gone and brought low* (Job 24:24). Enoch's woe to the mighty who oppress the righteous says the same: the day of their destruction is coming. The might does not keep.$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye mighty, Who with might oppress the righteous; For the day of your destruction is coming. In those days many and good days shall come to the righteous—in the day of your judgement.$n$),
(150619,18,1,18,1,$n$*I saw the treasuries of all the winds: I saw how He had furnished with them the whole creation and the firm foundations of the earth.* (1 Enoch 18:1). Enoch is shown the very *corner stone* of Job 38:6 — the world founded by Wisdom, the pillars on which the earth is set.$n$,$n$I saw the treasuries of all the winds: I saw how He had furnished with them the whole creation and the firm foundations of the earth.$n$),
(150625,69,22,69,17,$n$*And through it the earth was founded upon the water, And from the secret recesses of the mountains come beautiful waters, From the creation of the world and unto eternity.* (1 Enoch 69:17). The sea *shut up... with doors, when it brake forth, as if it had issued out of the womb* (Job 38:8) is bound by the same creating oath — the sand its appointed limit, which it dare not overpass.$n$,$n$And through it the earth was founded upon the water, And from the secret recesses of the mountains come beautiful waters, From the creation of the world and unto eternity.$n$),
(150635,18,13,18,15,$n$*And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* (1 Enoch 18:15). The *ordinances of heaven* (Job 38:33) are commandment: even the stars are judged by whether they come forth at their *appointed times* — the fixed order no man can set, which Yahuah alone governs.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$),
(151942,60,7,60,7,$n$*And on that day were two monsters parted, a female monster named Leviathan, to dwell in the abysses of the ocean over the fountains of the waters.* (1 Enoch 60:7). The restored witness names the same abyss-monster the LORD reserves:  (1 Enoch 60:7). Job's *Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook?* (Job 41:1) asks of a creature of the deep that man cannot reach — held in the abyss under Yahuah's (God's) hand alone.$n$,$n$And on that day were two monsters parted, a female monster named Leviathan, to dwell in the abysses of the ocean over the fountains of the waters.$n$),
(157298,14,15,14,18,$n$*And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* (1 Enoch 14:18). *I saw Yahuah (the LORD) sitting on his throne, and all the host of heaven standing by him* (1 Kings 22:19). Enoch saw the same throne — lofty, crystal, cherubim about it, ten thousand times ten thousand before him (1 Enoch 14:22). The restored witness joins the prophets: Yahuah (Lord) is enthroned in the heights, the host attending.$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$),
(165944,99,7,99,7,$n$*And they who worship stones, and grave images of gold and silver and wood and stone and clay, and those who worship impure spirits and demons, and all kinds of idols not according to knowledge, shall get no manner of help from them.* (1 Enoch 99:7). Enoch puts idol-worship and demon-worship in one breath, just as the Song does — *to gods whom they knew not, to new gods that came newly up* (Deuteronomy 32:17) — *whom your fathers feared not*.$n$,$n$And they who worship stones, and grave images of gold and silver and wood and stone and clay, and those who worship impure spirits and demons, and all kinds of idols not according to knowledge, shall get no manner of help from them.$n$),
(165963,1,9,1,9,$n$*And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* (1 Enoch 1:9). *He came with ten thousands of saints* (Deuteronomy 33:2). Enoch's ten thousands of holy ones are the same accompanying host — the verse Jude later quotes by name. The Formed One comes attended by the holy ones.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$);
INSERT INTO _s459m VALUES
(39,4292,$n$1 Enoch 14:18 — the Throne-room the open heaven gives access to. Sapphire, fire, the Father on the Throne; the cosmological room into which Matt 3:16's opened heaven gives access.$n$),
(41,4298,$n$1 Enoch 40:5 — *the voice of the Holy One ... in the heaven, and the voice of the Elect One ... from the throne of glory.* The doubled Father / Son voice the Hebrew library promises; Matt 3:17 enacts the Father side publicly.$n$),
(41,4299,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — the direct Father-voice naming the Son of Adam: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* The construction Matt 3:17 enacts at the Yarden (Jordan).$n$),
(48,4323,$n$*But with the righteous He will make peace. And will protect the elect, And mercy shall be upon them. And they shall all belong to Elohim (God), And they shall be prospered, And they shall all be blessed. And He will help them all, And light shall appear unto them, And He will make peace with them.* (1 Enoch 1:8). *Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 5:3). The blessing is not an entry fee; it is the Father's own word over those who are already his. Enoch heard the same word before the Beatitudes were spoken: peace, protection, mercy, belonging — pronounced over the elect, not offered to applicants.$n$),
(49,4328,$n$*And the righteous shall be in the light of the sun, And the elect in the light of eternal life: The days of their life shall be unending, And the days of the holy without number.* (1 Enoch 58:3). *Ye are the light of the world* (Matthew 5:14) — not *become*; *are.* Enoch says why: the righteous are set in the light of the sun and the elect in the light of eternal life. The light the disciples carry is the light they were placed in.$n$),
(49,4330,$n$*And when the Righteous One shall appear before the eyes of the righteous, Whose elect works hang upon Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And light shall appear to the righteous and the elect who dwell on the earth, Where then will be the dwelling of the sinners, And where the resting-place of those who have denied Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits? It had been good for them if they had not been born.* (1 Enoch 38:2). *Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 5:16). Enoch saw the day the light appears on the righteous and the elect who dwell on the earth — and the question that day asks of the sinners. The shining is the Father's doing; the glory goes to him.$n$),
(51,4334,$n$*Be not godless in your hearts, and lie not and alter not the words of uprightness, nor charge with lying the words of the Holy Great One, nor take account of your idols; for all your lying and all your godlessness issue not in righteousness but in great sin.* (1 Enoch 104:9). Enoch's charge to his children is the charge Matthew 5:19 makes to every teacher: do not alter the words of uprightness. *Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so, he shall be called the least in the kingdom of heaven.* To alter the words and to teach men so are one act; both are named here before the gospel names them.$n$),
(51,4335,$n$*And now I know this mystery, that sinners will alter and pervert the words of righteousness in many ways, and will speak wicked words, and lie, and practise great deceits, and write books concerning their words.* (1 Enoch 104:10). Enoch knew the mystery before the pulpit practised it: sinners will alter and pervert the words of righteousness, and write books about it. *Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so* (Matthew 5:19) — the teaching is the perverting; the books are the sermons. The kingdom-status of such teachers was fixed long before the sermon was preached.$n$),
(61,4365,$n$*And they said to Yahuah (Lord) of the ages: ‘Lord of lords, Elohim (God) of gods, King of kings, and Elohim (God) of the ages, the throne of Thy glory (standeth) unto all the generations of the ages, and Thy name holy and glorious and blessed unto all the ages!* (1 Enoch 9:4). Enoch's angels pray what the disciples are taught to pray: the holy and blessed name, the throne of glory that stands to all generations, the King of kings. *Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom come* (Matthew 6:9–10) is the same prayer in the mouth of the children.$n$),
(61,4366,$n$*‘Blessed be Thou, O Yahuah (Lord), King, Great and mighty in Thy greatness, Yahuah (Lord) of the whole creation of the heaven, King of kings and Elohim (God) of the whole world. And Thy power and kingship and greatness abide for ever and ever, And throughout all generations Thy dominion; And all the heavens are Thy throne for ever, And the whole earth Thy footstool for ever and ever.* (1 Enoch 84:2). *Hallowed be thy name* (Matthew 6:9). Enoch's own prayer blesses the King whose dominion is through all generations and whose throne is the heavens. The disciples are taught to pray what the patriarch prayed.$n$),
(61,4367,$n$*Thou hast made all things, and power over all things hast Thou: and all things are naked and open in Thy sight, and Thou seest all things, and nothing can hide itself from Thee.* (1 Enoch 9:5). The One whose kingdom the disciples pray to come is the One who made all things and holds power over all things, from whom nothing hides. *Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven* (Matthew 6:10) asks nothing new; it asks that what is already true in heaven be seen on earth.$n$),
(69,4386,$n$*And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.* (1 Enoch 90:33). *Many shall come from the east and west, and shall sit down with Avraham (Abraham), and Yitschaq (Isaac), and Ya'aqov (Jacob), in the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 8:11). Enoch saw the sitting-down: all that had been destroyed and dispersed assembled in the house, and the Lord of the sheep rejoicing because they had returned. The many from east and west are the dispersed of the house coming home — the scattered sheep, not a new flock.$n$),
(71,4391,$n$*And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?* (1 Enoch 46:2). Enoch asks who *that Son of Adam* is — a figure named by title, standing beside the Head of Days. When Yahusha (Jesus) says *the Son of Adam hath not where to lay his head* (Matthew 8:20) he takes that title for himself: the named one of the Parables, now with no bed on the earth he came to.$n$),
(73,4395,$n$1 Enoch 15:11 — *the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth.* The spirits-from-the-giants demon-origin architecture; Matt 8:28's demoniacs walk the same.$n$),
(96,4411,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — *this is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him.* The Son of Adam's righteousness-abides-eternally architecture; Matt 9:6's authority to forgive sins is the present-tense exercise of the righteousness that abides over him.$n$),
(102,4424,$n$*And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.* (1 Enoch 90:25). The shepherds who were set over the sheep and destroyed more than they were bidden end here, judged and cast into the fiery abyss. When Yahusha (Jesus) saw the multitudes *as sheep having no shepherd* (Matthew 9:36), he was looking at the flock those shepherds had left; the vision had already recorded their sentence.$n$),
(102,4425,$n$*And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.* (1 Enoch 90:29). The shepherdless sheep of Matthew 9:36 are not left shepherdless. Enoch saw the Lord of the sheep bring a new house, greater and loftier than the first, with all the sheep within it. The compassion that moved him at the sight of the scattered flock is the compassion that builds the house.$n$),
(102,4426,$n$*And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.* (1 Enoch 90:33). *When he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad* (Matthew 9:36). Enoch saw where the scattering ends: all that had been destroyed and dispersed assembled in the house, and the Lord of the sheep rejoicing because they had returned.$n$),
(114,4453,$n$*I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.* (1 Enoch 104:1). *Whosoever therefore shall confess me before men, him will I confess also before my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 10:32). Enoch swears to the righteous that their names are already written before the glory of the Great One. The Son confesses before the Father the ones whose names were written before they ever confessed.$n$),
(114,4454,$n$*And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.* (1 Enoch 103:4). *But whosoever shall deny me before men, him will I also deny before my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 10:33). Enoch's word to the righteous who die in righteousness is that their memorial does not perish before the Great One. The warning of Matthew 10:33 is the other side of that promise: a memorial can be kept, and a name can be blotted out (1 Enoch 108:3). The denier is not a tare who never had a name; he is wheat that did not endure.$n$),
(118,4461,$n$*But with the righteous He will make peace. And will protect the elect, And mercy shall be upon them. And they shall all belong to Elohim (God), And they shall be prospered, And they shall all be blessed. And He will help them all, And light shall appear unto them, And He will make peace with them.* (1 Enoch 1:8). The answer sent to Yochanan (John) — *the blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, and the dead are raised up, and the poor have the gospel preached to them* (Matthew 11:5) — is the peace, protection, mercy, and light Enoch saw promised to the righteous, now arriving in flesh.$n$),
(118,4462,$n$*And then shall all the righteous escape, And shall live till they beget thousands of children, And all the days of their youth and their old age Shall they complete in peace.* (1 Enoch 10:17). Enoch saw the days when the righteous escape and complete their years in peace, the earth tilled in righteousness and cleansed of oppression (1 Enoch 10:17–22). The works Yahusha (Jesus) lists for Yochanan (John) at Matthew 11:5 are the first fruits of those days — the age Enoch saw, beginning.$n$),
(185,4501,$n$*Woe to you, sinners, for ye persecute the righteous; For ye shall be delivered up and persecuted because of injustice, And heavy shall its yoke be upon you.* (1 Enoch 95:7). *Then the Pharisees went out, and held a council against him, how they might destroy him* (Matthew 12:14). Enoch's woe already names them: sinners who persecute the righteous, and the heavy yoke that waits for them. The council against the Righteous One is the act the woe was written for.$n$),
(186,4504,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.* (1 Enoch 62:2). *Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him, and he shall shew judgment to the Gentiles* (Matthew 12:18). Enoch saw the same: the spirit of righteousness poured out on the Elect One seated on the throne, and the word of his mouth bringing judgment. The servant of Isaiah and the Elect One of the Parables are one figure, and the Spirit upon him is the same Spirit.$n$),
(189,4512,$n$*And these—they have no place of repentance for ever, because they have shown them what was hidden, and they are the damned: but as for thee, my son, Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits knows that thou art pure, and guiltless of this reproach concerning the secrets.* (1 Enoch 65:11). *But the blasphemy against the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Ghost) shall not be forgiven unto men* (Matthew 12:32). Enoch heard the sentence on those who showed what was hidden and became the damned: no place of repentance for ever. There is a sin that closes the door from the inside; the Pharisees who called the Spirit's work the work of Beelzebub stood at that door.$n$),
(194,4526,$n$*And the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath revealed him to the holy and righteous; For he hath preserved the lot of the righteous, Because they have hated and despised this world of unrighteousness, And have hated all its works and ways in the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits: For in his name they are saved, And according to his good pleasure hath it been in regard to their life.* (1 Enoch 48:7). *Because it is given unto you to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to them it is not given* (Matthew 13:11). Enoch says who the *you* are: the holy and righteous to whom the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits reveals him, who have hated this world of unrighteousness. The revealing follows the belonging; it does not create it.$n$),
(195,4531,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). *Then cometh the wicked one, and catcheth away that which was sown in his heart* (Matthew 13:19). Enoch names the spirits of the Watchers assuming many forms, leading mankind astray — the actor behind the catching-away. He is not a figure of speech; the restored library records his origin and his end.$n$),
(197,4536,$n$*And to Gabriel said Yahuah (Lord): ‘Proceed against the bastards and the reprobates, and against the children of fornication: and destroy [the children of fornication and] the children of the Watchers from amongst men [and cause them to go forth]: send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle: for length of days shall they not have.* (1 Enoch 10:9). *The tares are the children of the wicked one* (Matthew 13:38). Enoch names them before the parable does: the children of the Watchers, a seed with a father of its own, distinguished from the line of Adam and marked for destruction. The tares are not bad wheat; they are another seed.$n$),
(198,4540,$n$*In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.* (1 Enoch 10:13). *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth* (Matthew 13:42). Enoch saw the abyss of fire and the prison appointed for the Watchers — the furnace the parable names, already mapped.$n$),
(198,4541,$n$*And Michael, and Gabriel, and Raphael, and Phanuel shall take hold of them on that great day, and cast them on that day into the burning furnace, that Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits may take vengeance on them for their unrighteousness in becoming subject to Satan and leading astray those who dwell on the earth.’* (1 Enoch 54:6). *The reapers are the angels* (Matthew 13:39), and here they are by name: Michael, Gabriel, Raphael and Phanuel, casting the hosts of Azazel into the burning furnace on the great day. The furnace of Matthew 13:42 has its angels, its day, and its reason — vengeance for leading astray those who dwell on the earth.$n$),
(200,4545,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *All these things spake Yahusha (Jesus) unto the multitude in parables* (Matthew 13:34). Enoch had named the Son of Adam as the one who reveals all the treasures of that which is hidden. The parables are that revealing — hidden things opened, by the one chosen to open them.$n$),
(203,4557,$n$*And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’* (1 Enoch 22:7). *The good seed are the children of the kingdom; but the tares are the children of the wicked one* (Matthew 13:38). The seed war is older than the parable. Enoch is shown the spirit of Hevel (Abel), the first righteous blood, making its suit against the seed of Qayin (Cain) until that seed is gone from among the seed of men. Two seeds, from Genesis 4 to the harvest.$n$),
(224,4597,$n$*And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?* (1 Enoch 46:2). *Whom do men say that I the Son of Adam am?* (Matthew 16:13). The question uses the title Enoch asked about — *that Son of Adam,* the one who went with the Head of Days. The King asks whether men have recognized the figure the Parables named.$n$),
(224,4598,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *Thou art the Messiah (Christ), the Son of the living Elohim (God)* (Matthew 16:16). Kefa (Peter) confesses what Enoch was told: the Son of Adam who has righteousness, whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits has chosen, whose lot has the pre-eminence for ever. The confession at Caesarea Philippi is the angel's answer at 1 Enoch 46:3, spoken on earth.$n$),
(225,4602,$n$*For he is mighty in all the secrets of righteousness, And unrighteousness shall disappear as a shadow, And have no continuance; Because the Elect One standeth before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his glory is for ever and ever, And his might unto all generations.* (1 Enoch 49:2). *I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 16:19). The secrets of righteousness belong to the Elect One who stands before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits; the keys Kefa (Peter) receives are stewardship of what is his. The one who holds the secrets delegates their opening.$n$),
(225,4603,$n$*And the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne, And his mouth shall pour forth all the secrets of wisdom and counsel: For Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath given (them) to him and hath glorified him.* (1 Enoch 51:3). *I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 16:19). Enoch saw the Elect One seated on the Father's throne, his mouth pouring out the secrets of wisdom and counsel. The keys are given by the one who sits on that throne; the house of David's key (Isaiah 22:22) is on his shoulder before it is in Kefa's (Peter's) hand.$n$),
(225,4604,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *Flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 16:17). The Father's naming of the Son of Adam at 1 Enoch 71:14 is the same revealing — the Head of Days declaring who he is. Kefa (Peter) receives on earth what Enoch heard in heaven, and the keys follow the revealing.$n$),
(225,4605,$n$*And he sat on the throne of his glory, And the sum of judgement was given unto the Son of Adam, And he caused the sinners to pass away and be destroyed from off the face of the earth, And those who have led the world astray.* (1 Enoch 69:27). *Whatsoever thou shalt bind on earth shall be bound in heaven* (Matthew 16:19). The sum of judgement was given to the Son of Adam on the throne of his glory; what the apostles bind and loose is bound and loosed under that judgement, not beside it.$n$),
(371,4677,$n$*And Azâzêl taught men to make swords, and knives, and shields, and breastplates, and made known to them the metals of the earth and the art of working them, and bracelets, and ornaments, and the use of antimony, and the beautifying of the eyelids, and all kinds of costly stones, and all colouring tinctures.* (1 Enoch 8:1). *Whoso shall offend one of these little ones which believe in me, it were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck* (Matthew 18:6). The stumbling-blocks laid across the way of the little ones have a history: Azazel taught men the arts that became the snares. The millstone is the King's answer to the teacher of the snare.$n$),
(371,4680,$n$*Here their spirits shall be set apart in this great pain till the great day of judgement and punishment and torment of those who curse for ever and retribution for their spirits. There He shall bind them for ever.* (1 Enoch 22:11). *It were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and that he were drowned in the depth of the sea* (Matthew 18:6). Better than what? Than the place Enoch was shown — spirits set apart in great pain until the great day of judgement, and bound there. The sea is the lesser end.$n$),
(372,4686,$n$*And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’* (1 Enoch 40:9). *In heaven their angels do always behold the face of my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 18:10). Enoch is given the names of the four who stand before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits — mercy, healing, power, and repentance unto hope. The little ones are watched over from the throne itself.$n$),
(372,4682,$n$*And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep came unto them and took in His hand the staff of His wrath, and smote the earth, and the earth clave asunder, and all the beasts and all the birds of the heaven fell from among those sheep, and were swallowed up in the earth and it covered them.* (1 Enoch 90:18). *For the Son of Adam is come to save that which was lost* (Matthew 18:11). The Lord of the sheep comes to the flock in person, staff in hand, and the beasts and birds that devoured them are swallowed by the earth. The saving of the lost is the Lord of the sheep arriving.$n$),
(372,4683,$n$*And after that I saw that when they forsook the house of Yahuah (Lord) and His tower they fell away entirely, and their eyes were blinded; and I saw Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep how He wrought much slaughter amongst them in their herds until those sheep invited that slaughter and betrayed His place.* (1 Enoch 89:54). *If a man have an hundred sheep, and one of them be gone astray, doth he not leave the ninety and nine, and goeth into the mountains, and seeketh that which is gone astray?* (Matthew 18:12). Enoch's vision names the owner of the flock: Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep, whose house and tower the sheep forsook. The shepherd of the parable is not a hired man; he is the Lord of the sheep seeking his own.$n$),
(372,4685,$n$*And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.* (1 Enoch 90:33). *He rejoiceth more of that sheep, than of the ninety and nine which went not astray* (Matthew 18:13). Enoch saw that joy at the end: the Lord of the sheep rejoicing with great joy because all that had been dispersed had returned to his house. The parable's one sheep is the vision's whole flock.$n$),
(379,4711,$n$*Woe to you, ye rich, for ye have trusted in your riches, And from your riches shall ye depart, Because ye have not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of your riches.* (1 Enoch 94:8). *A rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 19:23). Enoch's woe says why: those who trust in riches depart from them, having not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of their wealth. The difficulty is not the money; it is the trust.$n$),
(379,4712,$n$*Woe to you, ye sinners, who live on the mid ocean and on the dry land, Whose remembrance is evil against you.* (1 Enoch 97:7). *A rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven* (Matthew 19:23). The young ruler's confidence — *all these things have I kept from my youth up* — is the sinner's confidence Enoch names: a remembrance that is evil against him, however secure the holdings look.$n$),
(379,4713,$n$*And now let us do what we purposed: For we have gathered silver, And many are the husbandmen in our houses.’ And our granaries are (brim) full as with water,* (1 Enoch 97:9). *It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of Elohim (God)* (Matthew 19:24). Enoch gives the rich man's own speech — silver gathered, granaries full, *let us do what we purposed.* That speech is the needle's eye closing.$n$),
(379,4715,$n$*And (then) the children of the earth shall see the wise in security, And shall understand all the words of this book, And recognize that their riches shall not be able to save them In the overthrow of their sins.* (1 Enoch 100:6). *With men this is impossible; but with Elohim (God) all things are possible* (Matthew 19:26). Enoch saw the day the children of the earth understand that riches cannot save them. What riches cannot do, Elohim (God) does — that is the whole of the disciples' hope, and the whole of the rich man's.$n$),
(382,4726,$n$*And the congregation of the elect and holy shall be sown. And all the elect shall stand before him on that day.* (1 Enoch 62:8). *So the last shall be first, and the first last: for many be called, but few chosen* (Matthew 20:16). Enoch saw the chosen gathered: the congregation of the elect and holy sown, and all the elect standing before him on that day. The few are not fewer because they tried harder; they are the elect, and the elect are revealed by their standing.$n$),
(384,4736,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). *The Son of Adam came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many* (Matthew 20:28). The same Son of Adam, Enoch saw, raises the kings and the mighty from their seats and breaks the teeth of the sinners. The one who serves is the one who judges; the ransom and the reckoning belong to the same hands.$n$),
(388,4753,$n$*But He remained unmoved, though He saw it, and rejoiced that they were devoured and swallowed and robbed, and left them to be devoured in the hand of all the beasts.* (1 Enoch 89:58). *Let no fruit grow on thee henceforward for ever. And presently the fig tree withered away* (Matthew 21:19). Enoch saw the Lord of the sheep do the same to a flock that had abandoned him: unmoved, leaving them to be devoured. The withered tree is the leadership that bore no fruit, left to its own harvest.$n$),
(390,4761,$n$*And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.* (1 Enoch 90:25). *He will miserably destroy those wicked men, and will let out his vineyard unto other husbandmen* (Matthew 21:41). The husbandmen answer their own parable; Enoch's vision records the sentence they pronounced — the seventy shepherds judged, found guilty, and cast into the fiery abyss.$n$),
(395,4782,$n$*And the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne, And his mouth shall pour forth all the secrets of wisdom and counsel: For Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath given (them) to him and hath glorified him.* (1 Enoch 51:3). *Yahuah (The LORD) said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand* (Matthew 22:44; Psalm 110:1). Enoch heard the same seating spoken by the Father: *the Elect One shall in those days sit on My throne.* The Pharisees could not say how David's son is David's Lord; the Parables had already seated him.$n$),
(395,4783,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool* (Matthew 22:44). The Head of Days placing the Elect One on the throne of glory is Psalm 110:1 seen from the throne room — the Father seating the Son, the Son judging. The Formless seats the Formed; the One who is seated is Elohim (God) and has a Father.$n$),
(395,4784,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *If David then call him Lord, how is he his son?* (Matthew 22:45). The Father answers at 1 Enoch 71:14: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* Born — David's son after the flesh; named by the Head of Days — David's Lord. The question the Pharisees could not answer, the Parables had answered.$n$),
(400,4801,$n$*And he said unto me: ‘This place is the prison of the angels, and here they will be imprisoned for ever.’* (1 Enoch 21:10). *Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of Gehinnom (hell)?* (Matthew 23:33). Enoch was shown the prison of the angels and told it holds them for ever. The judgment the serpents cannot escape is the judgment their fathers, the Watchers, are already held for; the seed goes where the seed came from.$n$),
(400,4802,$n$*And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’* (1 Enoch 22:7). *That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Hevel (Abel)* (Matthew 23:35). Enoch saw the spirit of Hevel (Abel) making its suit against the seed of Qayin (Cain) until that seed is destroyed. The blood that cries from the ground (Genesis 4:10) is still crying in Enoch's vision, and the King hands the sum of it to the generation standing in front of him.$n$),
(401,4807,$n$*And He said unto me: “Because of their unrighteousness their judgement has been determined upon and shall not be withheld by Me for ever. Because of the sorceries which they have searched out and learnt, the earth and those who dwell upon it shall be destroyed.”* (1 Enoch 65:10). *As in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noach (Noah) entered into the ark* (Matthew 24:38). Enoch heard the sentence pronounced over those days: judgement determined, not to be withheld, the earth and its dwellers to be destroyed for the sorceries they had learned. The eating and drinking went on under a sentence already passed.$n$),
(401,4808,$n$*In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.* (1 Enoch 10:13). *And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be* (Matthew 24:39). The flood took the wicked away; it did not carry the righteous off. Enoch's word for the Watchers is the same taking: led off to the abyss of fire, to the prison. The ones taken at the coming are the ones taken at the flood — the judged.$n$),
(402,4814,$n$*And it looked at them [and their eyes opened], and it cried to the sheep, and the rams saw it and all ran to it.* (1 Enoch 90:10). *And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds* (Matthew 24:31). Enoch saw the gathering as a flock: the great horn cried to the sheep, their eyes opened, and the rams all ran to it. The gathering is the sheep running to the horn that called them.$n$),
(410,4845,$n$*And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.* (1 Enoch 62:5). *When the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory* (Matthew 25:31). Enoch saw that seat and the faces of those who see it — terror, pain, downcast countenance, when they see that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory. The sheep-and-goats judgment opens on the throne the Parables had already set.$n$),
(410,4846,$n$*And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.* (1 Enoch 61:10). *And all the holy angels with him* (Matthew 25:31). Enoch gives the roll: the host of the heavens, the holy ones above, Cherubim, Seraphim and Ophannim, the angels of power and of principalities — and the Elect One among them. The company of the coming was mustered in the Parables before the gospel named it.$n$),
(410,4847,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). *And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another* (Matthew 25:32). The Son of Adam who separates is the Son of Adam Enoch saw raise the kings and the mighty from their seats and break the teeth of the sinners. The separation is a reversal; the mighty do not keep their seats at it.$n$),
(410,4848,$n$*And he shall put down the countenance of the strong, And shall fill them with shame. And darkness shall be their dwelling, And worms shall be their bed, And they shall have no hope of rising from their beds, Because they do not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 46:6). *Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels* (Matthew 25:41). Enoch saw what that departure is for the strong: countenance put down, shame, darkness for a dwelling, worms for a bed, no hope of rising — because they did not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$),
(410,4849,$n$*And in the day of our suffering and tribulation He saves us not, And we find no respite for confession That our Lord is true in all His works, and in His judgements and His justice, And His judgements have no respect of persons.* (1 Enoch 63:8). *Depart from me, ye cursed* (Matthew 25:41) is answered in Enoch by the mouths of the kings and the mighty themselves: in the day of their tribulation he saves them not, and their confession comes too late to be anything but true. *Lord, when saw we thee an hungred?* (Matthew 25:44) is the same late confession.$n$),
(411,4850,$n$*And I asked the angel who went with me and showed me all the hidden things, concerning that Son of Adam, who he was, and whence he was, (and) why he went with the Head of Days?* (1 Enoch 46:2). *Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Matthew 26:64). The bound man before the council names himself with Enoch's title — *that Son of Adam* who went with the Head of Days. The council thought it was judging him; he was telling them who would judge.$n$),
(411,4854,$n$*And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.* (1 Enoch 62:9). *Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power* (Matthew 26:64). Enoch saw what the council will see: all the kings and the mighty falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, petitioning him for mercy. The men who condemned him will kneel to him.$n$),
(418,4877,$n$*And there shall stand up in that day all the kings and the mighty, And the exalted and those who hold the earth, And they shall see and recognize How he sits on the throne of his glory, And righteousness is judged before him, And no lying word is spoken before him.* (1 Enoch 62:3). *When the morning was come, all the chief priests and elders of the people took counsel against Yahusha (Jesus) to put him to death* (Matthew 27:1). Enoch saw the other morning: all the kings and the mighty standing up in that day to see and recognize how he sits on the throne of his glory, where no lying word is spoken. The council that condemned him stands at his bar.$n$),
(418,4878,$n$*And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.* (1 Enoch 61:10). *If he be the King of Yashar'el (Israel), let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him* (Matthew 27:42). The mockers set the wrong test. Enoch saw the King's credential: the whole host of heaven summoned, and the Elect One among them. He did not come down from the cross; he is the one for whom the heavens are mustered.$n$),
(418,4879,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). *He trusted in Elohim (God); let him deliver him now, if he will have him* (Matthew 27:43). The Head of Days had already said it: *the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.* The cross was not the Father's forsaking of the Son; it was the Son of Adam, born unto righteousness, doing what righteousness does.$n$),
(418,4880,$n$*And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.* (1 Enoch 62:9). *Let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him* (Matthew 27:42). Enoch saw the mockers' end: the kings and the mighty and those who rule the earth falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, worshipping and petitioning. *Every knee should bow* (Philippians 2:10) — the mockers included.$n$),
(423,4902,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch saw the placing — Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits setting the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge and to weigh deeds in the balance. The Father is the giver; the Son is seated; the power is the power to judge.$n$),
(423,4900,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.* (1 Enoch 62:2). *All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch saw the giving: the Elect One seated on the throne of glory, the spirit of righteousness poured out on him, the word of his mouth slaying the sinners. The power was given by the Father; the Son wields it.$n$),
(423,4901,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). *All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Enoch's Son of Adam raises the kings and the mighty from their seats and breaks the teeth of the sinners. That is what all power looks like when it is used.$n$),
(618,7846,$n$1 Enoch 15:8-7 — *the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth.* The unclean spirit at Mark 1:24 is one of the watchers' bound offspring; it recognizes the Holy One because it was there at the rebellion.$n$),
(618,7845,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). 1 Enoch 16:1 names the unclean spirit's origin and its appointed end: the spirits gone forth from the giants destroy until the day of the great judgement. The demon's own question at Mark 1:24 — *art thou come to destroy us?* — names that it knows its judgement-day is fixed; the watchers' offspring recognize that the Holy One of Elohim is the one who holds the day of their consummation.$n$),
(618,7844,$n$1 Enoch 16:4, 4 — *Say to them therefore: "You have no peace."* The demon's *Let us alone* (Mark 1:24) is the no-peace condition speaking; the Holy One's coming is the disturbance of a peace never granted.$n$),
(618,7843,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). 1 Enoch 19:1 names the watcher-spirits and their appointed standing-place of judgement. At Mark 3:11 the unclean spirits *fell down before him, and cried, saying, Thou art the Son of Elohim (God)* — the watcher-administration recognizing the Judge before whom it must one day stand, falling down before the Formed one whose great-judgement-day is named in the Enochic library.$n$),
(621,7858,$n$1 Enoch 15:10 — *as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.* The earth-bound multitude the Hebrew library locates; *Legion: for we are many* (Mark 5:9) is the gospel's word for the same class.$n$),
(621,7857,$n$1 Enoch 15:11 — *the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth.* The torment of the man among the tombs — crying, cutting himself with stones — is the work the Hebrew library attributes to the spirits of the giants.$n$),
(621,7856,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). *And the unclean spirits went out, and entered into the swine: and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the sea* (Mark 5:13). The spirits of the giants afflict and destroy, Enoch says, and they do not eat yet hunger. The sea was not their judgement; that waits for the day of the consummation. It was the King displacing them.$n$),
(621,7855,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). *For he said unto him, Come out of the man, thou unclean spirit.* 1 Enoch 16:1 names the spirits the command addresses by their origin in the slain giants:  The unclean spirit is not a faceless force; the Hebrew library had recorded its lineage and its sentence — *Say to them therefore: "You have no peace."* (1 Enoch 16:4) — long before the King commanded it out of the man.$n$),
(621,7852,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). *And see him that was possessed with the devil, and had the legion, sitting, and clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid* (Mark 5:15). The man restored is the reversal, in one life, of what Enoch says these spirits do — defile mankind and lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods. Their day of judgement is fixed; the Gadarene was given his back early.$n$),
(624,7868,$n$*And there I saw a holy mountain, and underneath the mountain to the east there was a stream and it flowed towards the south.* (1 Enoch 26:2). 1 Enoch 27:1-3 places the accursed valley — the Hinnom-shaped place of punishment for the godless — beside the holy mountain, the very Ge-Hinnom topography the gospel's *hell* (Gehenna) draws its name from. The King's *cut it off ... than having two hands to go into hell* (Mark 9:43) walks the same place-of-judgment architecture 1 Enoch maps at the middle of the earth: the accursed valley appointed for the day of judgment.$n$),
(624,7869,$n$*Here their spirits shall be set apart in this great pain till the great day of judgement and punishment and torment of those who curse for ever and retribution for their spirits. There He shall bind them for ever.* (1 Enoch 22:11). *Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched* (Mark 9:48). Enoch was shown where the sinners' spirits are set apart in great pain until the great day of judgement — a holding until the judgement comes, and then the binding for ever. The place Mark warns of is the place Enoch had mapped; the fire that is not quenched is the judgement the holding waits for.$n$),
(629,7876,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Sitting on the right hand of power* (Mark 14:62). Enoch saw the placing: Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits set the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge. The bound man names his seat before the court that thinks it is judging him.$n$),
(629,7875,$n$*And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* (1 Enoch 71:14). 1 Enoch 71:14 names the Son of Adam born unto righteousness, over whom the righteousness of the Head of Days never fails. Mark 14:62's self-identification — *I am: and ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power* — names the same figure the Parables named: the righteous one whom the Head of Days does not forsake, enthroned at the right hand. The title-naming of the Parables and the direct attribution of the King land on one figure.$n$),
(629,7874,$n$*And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.* (1 Enoch 62:9). *Ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Mark 14:62). Enoch saw the seeing: the kings and the mighty falling on their faces before that Son of Adam, petitioning for mercy. The court that condemned him will see him, exactly as he said.$n$),
(633,7892,$n$*And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 40:1). *Suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly host praising Elohim (God)* (Luke 2:13). Enoch saw that host where it stands — thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. At the birth of the Son the host that stands before the throne came down to the fields.$n$),
(633,7893,$n$1 Enoch 40:3 — *I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (God) of glory.* The praise before the throne; Luke 2:14's *Glory to Elohim (God) in the highest* is the same heavenly-praise register sounded on earth.$n$),
(633,7894,$n$1 Enoch 40:4 — *the first voice blesses Yahuah (God) of Spirits for ever and ever.* The host blessing the Most High for ever; Luke 2:14's glory-in-the-highest is the same blessing, now over Bethlehem.$n$),
(635,7899,$n$*Before I took thy mother Edna, I saw in a vision on my bed, and behold a bull came forth from the earth, and that bull was white; and after it came forth a heifer, and along with this (latter) came forth two bulls, one of them black and the other red.* (1 Enoch 85:3). 1 Enoch 85:3 opens the Animal Apocalypse with the white bull (Adam) coming forth from the earth, the heifer (Chavah/Eve), and the two young bulls — the black (Cain) and the red (Hevel/Abel). This is the Adamic toledot in vision-form, the same opening of the seed-line Luke 3:38 closes its backward genealogy on: *the son of Adam, which was the son of Elohim (God).* The Hebrew library sees the first man as the white bull from the earth whom Yahuah created; the gospel names the same Adam as the son of Elohim at the head of the seed-line.$n$),
(635,7900,$n$1 Enoch 85:9 — *another white bull... from Him proceeded many white bulls, and they resembled him... one following the other.* The Sethite seed-line as the white bulls one-following-another; Luke 3:36-38 traces that same line backward to Adam.$n$),
(638,7908,$n$1 Enoch 15:10 — *as for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.* The earth-dwelling demon-origin; Luke 8:29's unclean spirit that drove the man into the wilderness is an earthbound spirit of the order 1 Enoch names.$n$),
(638,7906,$n$*From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."* (1 Enoch 16:1). *What have I to do with thee, Yahusha (Jesus), thou Son of Elohim (God) most high? I beseech thee, torment me not* (Luke 8:28). The spirits know the day of the consummation is appointed for them; Enoch records that they destroy only until it. The demoniac's cry is the fear of a sentence already written.$n$),
(638,7907,$n$1 Enoch 16:1 — *thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated.* The appointed-consummation the spirits dread; Luke 8:31's Legion *besought him that he would not command them to go out into the deep* — the confinement appointed against the day of judgment.$n$),
(641,7924,$n$*And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* (1 Enoch 6:6). *I beheld Satan as lightning fall from heaven* (Luke 10:18). Enoch records the first fall — two hundred who descended on Hermon in the days of Jared and bound themselves by oath. The seventy returning with the devils subject to them (Luke 10:17) were undoing, territory by territory, what began on that mountain.$n$),
(648,7948,$n$*And he answered me and said unto me: ‘These three have been made that the spirits of the dead might be separated. And such a division has been made for the spirits of the righteous, in which there is the bright spring of water.* (1 Enoch 22:9). Enoch is shown the holding-places of the dead — distinct compartments hewn in the great mountain. Luke 16:22's carrying of Lazaros *by the angels into Avraham's (Abraham's) bosom* while the rich man is *buried* and lifts his eyes in another place walks the same architecture the Hebrew library named: the dead are held in separated compartments pending the judgment, not annihilated into nothing and not dispatched to a final eternal destination.$n$),
(648,7947,$n$*And such has been made for sinners when they die and are buried in the earth and judgement has not been executed on them in their lifetime.* (1 Enoch 22:10). The conscious-souls-of-the-dead-assembled register against the inherited soul-sleep misread. Luke 16:23's rich man *in hell (hadēs) lift up his eyes, being in torments, and seeth Avraham (Abraham) afar off, and Lazaros in his bosom* assumes exactly this architecture — the spirits of the dead are gathered, aware, and identifiable, held in the hollow places the Hebrew library named.$n$),
(648,7946,$n$*And these places have been made to receive them till the day of their judgement and till their appointed period [till the period appointed], till the great judgement (comes) upon them.’* (1 Enoch 22:4). *Between us and you there is a great gulf fixed* (Luke 16:26). Enoch saw the fixing: the hollow places made to receive the dead until the day of their judgement, divided one from another. Sheol is real and the dead are aware in it — and it is a holding until the appointed period, not the final destination.$n$),
(650,7938,$n$*And it looked at them [and their eyes opened], and it cried to the sheep, and the rams saw it and all ran to it.* (1 Enoch 90:10). *For the Son of Adam is come to seek and to save that which was lost* (Luke 19:10). Enoch saw the seeking as a horn crying to the sheep, their eyes opening, and all of them running to it. The lost are the house of Yashar'el (Israel) scattered among the nations; the seeking is the call that brings the sheep running home — not a new flock gathered from the nations.$n$),
(652,7959,$n$*And there I saw another vision, the dwelling-places of the holy, And the resting-places of the righteous.* (1 Enoch 39:4). The Hebrew library names the dwellings of the righteous WITH the holy angels — the resting-places of the elect among the holy ones of heaven. *They are equal unto the angels; and are the children of Elohim (God), being the children of the resurrection* (Luke 20:36): the equal-unto-the-angels register the King names against the Sadducees' deny-the-resurrection is the same dwelling-with-the-righteous-angels Enoch saw — the children of the resurrection sharing the resting-places of the holy ones, no longer dying, no longer given in marriage, equal unto the angels.$n$),
(652,7958,$n$*Here mine eyes saw their dwellings with His righteous angels, And their resting-places with the holy. And they petitioned and interceded and prayed for the children of men, And righteousness flowed before them as water, And mercy like dew upon the earth: Thus it is amongst them for ever and ever.* (1 Enoch 39:5). *Equal unto the angels; and are the children of Elohim (God), being the children of the resurrection* (Luke 20:36). Enoch saw their dwellings with the righteous angels and their resting-places with the holy. The children of the resurrection dwell where Enoch saw them dwell.$n$),
(652,7957,$n$*Be hopeful, and cast not away your hope; for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.* (1 Enoch 104:4). *Neither can they die any more: for they are equal unto the angels* (Luke 20:36). Enoch tells the righteous to hope, *for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.* The equality with angels is joy without end, promised before the Sadducees asked their question.$n$),
(653,7956,$n$*And he answered me and said unto me: ‘These three have been made that the spirits of the dead might be separated. And such a division has been made for the spirits of the righteous, in which there is the bright spring of water.* (1 Enoch 22:9). *To day shalt thou be with me in paradise* (Luke 23:43). Enoch was shown the hollow places where the spirits of the dead are received — deep, wide, divided. The paradise promised to the thief that day is the righteous division of those places, where the bright spring of water is, until the day of judgement.$n$),
(653,7955,$n$*And these places have been made to receive them till the day of their judgement and till their appointed period [till the period appointed], till the great judgement (comes) upon them.’* (1 Enoch 22:4). *To day shalt thou be with me in paradise* (Luke 23:43). Enoch was shown the places made to receive the dead until the day of their judgement. The paradise promised to the thief that day is the righteous division of those places, held until the great judgement — not the final state, but the keeping until it.$n$),
(657,7969,$n$*Wisdom went forth to make her dwelling among the children of men, And found no dwelling-place: Wisdom returned to her place, And took her seat among the angels.* (1 Enoch 42:2). *He came unto his own, and his own received him not* (John 1:11). Enoch saw Wisdom go out to make her dwelling among the children of men and find no place. The Word came to his own and found no room; the rejection was foreseen before the Word was made flesh.$n$),
(663,7998,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *And hath given him authority to execute judgment also, because he is the Son of Adam* (John 5:27). Enoch saw the giving: the Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge and to weigh deeds in the balance. The authority John names is the seat Enoch saw filled.$n$),
(663,7997,$n$*And when he shall lift up his countenance To judge their secret ways according to the word of the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And their path according to the way of the righteous judgement of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, Then shall they all with one voice speak and bless, And glorify and extol and sanctify the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 61:9). *And hath given him authority to execute judgment also, because he is the Son of Adam* (John 5:27). Enoch saw him lift up his countenance to judge their secret ways, and the whole host bless the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for it. The authority is given by the Father; the judging is the Son's; the praise returns to the Father.$n$),
(670,8002,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness ... the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.* The named Son of Adam declared by Yahuah (God) of Spirits; John 12:23's *the hour is come, that the Son of Adam should be glorified* names the hour that Son of Adam is glorified.$n$),
(670,8001,$n$1 Enoch 61:9 — *then shall they all ... bless and glorify and extol and laud the name of Yahuah (God) of Spirits.* The glorifying-of-the-name at the Son of Adam's enthronement; John 12:28's *Father, glorify thy name ... I have both glorified it, and will glorify it again* walks the same — the hour of the Son of Adam is the hour the name is glorified.$n$),
(1017,9875,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all* the coming Jude quoted — the One taken up returns, and the holy ones with him are the seed of promise gathered to him.$n$),
(1022,9899,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Yahuah (The LORD) said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand* (Acts 2:34). Enoch saw the seating: Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placing the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge. The right hand of Psalm 110 is the throne of glory of the Parables.$n$),
(1022,9900,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness* the named Son of Adam — the Yahusha made Lord and Messiah.$n$),
(1867,12616,$n$*And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* (1 Enoch 71:1). *By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death... because Elohim (God) had translated him* (Hebrews 11:5). The Torah says only that Elohim (God) took him; Enoch tells the taking from the inside — *my spirit was translated and it ascended into the heavens.* The man who pleased Elohim (God) was brought up among the holy sons of Elohim (God), translated rather than buried.$n$),
(1917,12820,$n$*And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* (1 Enoch 14:18). The throne Enoch saw — crystal, wheels like the sun, cherubim, fire streaming from beneath it (1 Enoch 14:18–22) — is the throne-and-fire presence John is brought into when he sees the Formed One whose *eyes were as a flame of fire* and whose *feet like unto fine brass, as if they burned in a furnace* (Revelation 1:14–15). John falls as dead, as Enoch fell on his face.$n$),
(1917,12822,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness... the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not* seated on the throne of glory; the slain-yet-living One *alive for evermore... have the keys of hell and of death* (Revelation 1:18).$n$),
(1918,12826,$n$*Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.* (1 Enoch 25:5). The restored library says plainly what the letter promises: the fruit of the tree *shall be for food to the elect,* and the tree transplanted to the holy place. *To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of Elohim (God)* (Revelation 2:7). The same elect, the same tree, the same gift.$n$),
(1951,12942,$n$*And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* (1 Enoch 14:18). *And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone* (Revelation 4:3). Enoch saw the lofty throne of crystal with wheels like the shining sun and the cherubim about it, and the Great Glory seated on it (1 Enoch 14:20). The throne of precious stone was seen before the door in heaven opened to John.$n$),
(1951,15006,$n$1 Enoch 18:12 — *I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above* the lofty throne-room Enoch reached in his ascent, the heaven into which a door opens and John is caught up (Revelation 4:1-2).$n$),
(1951,15005,$n$*And I saw angels who could not be counted, A thousand thousands, and ten thousand times ten thousand, Encircling that house. And Michael, and Raphael, and Gabriel, and Phanuel, And the holy angels who are above the heavens, Go in and out of that house.* (1 Enoch 71:8). *Him that liveth for ever and ever* (Revelation 4:9) sits in a house Enoch saw: a structure built of crystals with tongues of living fire between them (1 Enoch 71:5), encircled by angels beyond counting. It is the throne-room John enters.$n$),
(1953,12952,$n$1 Enoch 40:3 — *the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (God) of glory* the four about the throne of glory whose ceaseless praise Enoch heard (Revelation 4:8).$n$),
(1953,12953,$n$*The first voice blesses Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits for ever and ever.* (1 Enoch 40:4). The praise Enoch heard rises *for ever and ever* — the very note John's four living creatures sound, who *rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy* (Revelation 4:8). One worship before one throne.$n$),
(1953,15003,$n$*And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.* (1 Enoch 40:2). Enoch saw the four John sees: four presences on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, whose praises he heard (1 Enoch 40:3). John's *four beasts* who *rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy* (Revelation 4:8) are the same four about the same throne.$n$),
(1954,15004,$n$*And he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens, And I saw there as it were a structure built of crystals, And between those crystals tongues of living fire.* (1 Enoch 71:5). Enoch saw the throne-room floored and walled with crystal — *a structure built of crystals* — the same clear, shining expanse John names *a sea of glass like unto crystal* (Revelation 4:6). The crystal pavement of the throne-house the seers of Yashar'el (Israel) beheld is the crystal sea before the throne, the clear floor of the heavenly sanctuary.$n$),
(1955,12956,$n$*And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 40:1). *The four and twenty elders fall down before him that sat on the throne* (Revelation 4:10). Enoch saw the multitude beyond number standing before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The elders who cast their crowns belong to that numberless worship.$n$),
(1961,12979,$n$*And after that I saw thousands of thousands and ten thousand times ten thousand, I saw a multitude beyond number and reckoning, who stood before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 40:1). *Ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands* (Revelation 5:11) — John's count is Enoch's count, word for word. Enoch heard that host bless Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits and bless the Elect One beside him (1 Enoch 40:4–5); John hears them cry *Worthy is the Lamb that was slain* (Revelation 5:12). The Father and the Lamb, praised together by the myriads.$n$),
(1961,12980,$n$1 Enoch 18:16 — *bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years* the ten-thousand reckonings of Enoch's throne-vision, the world Revelation 5's myriad-numbered host stands in (Revelation 5:11).$n$),
(1962,15014,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *this Son of Adam... Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats* the enthroned Elect One before whom the mighty fall, the worshipped Son distinct from Yahuah (God) of Spirits who seated him (Revelation 5:13).$n$),
(1962,15015,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing* (Revelation 5:12). The dignity the Lamb receives is the seat Enoch saw given: the Elect One placed on the throne of glory by Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, to judge. The Lamb receives; the Father gives.$n$),
(2008,13160,$n$*In those days make ready, ye righteous, to raise your prayers as a memorial, And place them as a testimony before the angels, That they may place the sin of the sinners for a memorial before the El Elyon (Most High).* (1 Enoch 99:3). Enoch bids the righteous *raise your prayers as a memorial... before the angels* — and in Revelation an angel does exactly that, offering the incense *with the prayers of all saints* so that they *ascended up before Elohim (God)* (Revelation 8:4). The prayers are a memorial laid before the Most High, and the same fire-bearing angel who carries them up then casts the fire of the altar to the earth (8:5): the memorial of the righteous becomes the judgment on the sinners.$n$),
(2063,13370,$n$1 Enoch 18:14 — *this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven* the Hebrew library names the prison-pit of the fallen stars the seer sees opened (Revelation 9:1).$n$),
(2063,13371,$n$1 Enoch 18:16 — *He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated* the binding Enoch saw and the loosing John sees are two ends of one story (Revelation 9:1).$n$),
(2063,13372,$n$1 Enoch 21:7 — *the place was cleft as far as the abyss, being full of great descending columns of fire* the furnace-place from which the smoke of the pit rises (Revelation 9:2).$n$),
(2063,15033,$n$1 Enoch 18:12 — *a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it... a waste and horrible place* the waste abyss at the end of heaven and earth, the pit the fallen star unlocks (Revelation 9:1).$n$),
(2063,15034,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (God)* the transgressing stars bound for breaking the commandment; the fallen star is one of them (Revelation 9:1).$n$),
(2063,15035,$n$*And I saw a deep abyss, with columns of heavenly fire, and among them I saw columns of fire fall, which were beyond measure alike towards the height and towards the depth.* (1 Enoch 18:11). *There arose a smoke out of the pit, as the smoke of a great furnace* (Revelation 9:2). Enoch saw the abyss with its columns of heavenly fire beyond measure. The smoke rises from a fire that was seen before the pit was opened.$n$),
(2063,15036,$n$*These are of the number of the stars of heaven, which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord), and are bound here till ten thousand years, the time entailed by their sins, are consummated.’* (1 Enoch 21:6). *I saw a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit* (Revelation 9:1). Enoch was told who is bound in that place: stars of heaven that transgressed the commandment, bound till their ten thousand years are consummated. The pit has prisoners before it has a key.$n$),
(2073,13414,$n$*And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’* (1 Enoch 81:1). *The mystery of Elohim (God) should be finished, as he hath declared to his servants the prophets* (Revelation 10:7). Enoch is set before the heavenly tablets and told to read what is written there and mark every fact. The mystery is what stands written in heaven; the prophets read it and declare it, and the seventh trumpet brings it to pass.$n$),
(2073,13415,$n$*And I observed the heavenly tablets, and read everything which was written (thereon) and understood everything, and read the book of all the deeds of mankind, and of all the children of flesh that shall be upon the earth to the remotest generations.* (1 Enoch 81:2). *The mystery of Elohim (God) should be finished, as he hath declared to his servants the prophets* (Revelation 10:7). Enoch read the heavenly tablets and the book of all the deeds of mankind to the remotest generations. The prophet does not invent the mystery; he reads it where it is already written.$n$),
(2076,13433,$n$*And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.* (1 Enoch 90:29). The restored library saw the end of the measuring — not the old house propped up but *a new house... greater and loftier than the first*, into which the Lord of the sheep gathers all his flock. So the angel's reed to *measure the temple of Elohim (God), and the altar, and them that worship therein* (Revelation 11:1) marks off the house being built for the regathered: the worshippers numbered now are the sheep brought home into the greater house, the restoration of all Yashar'el (Israel).$n$),
(2163,13799,$n$*And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.* (1 Enoch 90:20). *Whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world* (Revelation 13:8). Enoch saw the books opened before the Lord of the sheep on his throne, and elsewhere *the books of the living were opened before Him* (1 Enoch 47:3). The worshippers of the beast are not in that book; the names in it were written before the beast rose.$n$),
(2163,15091,$n$*And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* (1 Enoch 108:3). *Whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb* (Revelation 13:8). Enoch knows the book and the blotting: *their names shall be blotted out of the book of life.* The names were written before the foundation of the world; the beast's worshippers are not among them, and the wheat that falls away is blotted out. No name is added after.$n$),
(2165,13805,$n$*And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep came unto them and took in His hand the staff of His wrath, and smote the earth, and the earth clave asunder, and all the beasts and all the birds of the heaven fell from among those sheep, and were swallowed up in the earth and it covered them.* (1 Enoch 90:18). *As many as would not worship the image of the beast should be killed* (Revelation 13:15). Enoch saw the end of every beast and bird that devoured the sheep: the Lord of the sheep came with the staff of his wrath and the earth swallowed them. The beast and the false prophet go into the fire (Revelation 19:20); the beasts of the vision go into the earth. The fire the false prophet calls down is not the fire that has the last word.$n$),
(2172,13836,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him* named by Yahuah (God) of Spirits; the enthroned Son of Adam revealed for judgment (Revelation 14:14).$n$),
(2417,15167,$n$1 Enoch 18:16 — *He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated* a fixed term of binding, the dragon shut up till the thousand years be fulfilled (Revelation 20:3).$n$),
(2423,14898,$n$*And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.* (1 Enoch 90:20). *The books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life* (Revelation 20:12). Enoch saw the sealed books taken and opened before the Lord of the sheep on his throne, and in the Parables *the books of the living were opened before Him* (1 Enoch 47:3). The books of deeds and the book of the living, opened together for judgment, are the books of the great white throne.$n$),
(2434,14941,$n$*Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.* (1 Enoch 25:5). Enoch was shown the tree of life transplanted to the holy place, its fruit for food to the elect. John sees the transplanting done — the tree *in the midst of the street* of the city, *and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations* (Revelation 22:2). The fruit reserved for the elect is theirs; the leaves reach the nations through them.$n$),
(2676,16012,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* Enoch frames his prophecy with this advent twice over, and it is 1:9 that Jude quotes by name.$n$),
(2750,16298,$n$1 Enoch 14:1 — *The book of the words of righteousness, and of the reprimand of the eternal Watchers in accordance with the command of the Holy Great One in that vision.* The heading of the very document Enoch writes out and reads before Elohim (God) in 13:6 and 13:10 — a book of reprimand, not of pardon.$n$),
(2847,16669,$n$1 Enoch 18:16 — *And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.* Enoch revisits the same prison of the stars later in the journey, repeating the binding-till-judgement of 1 Enoch 17:21 word for word.$n$),
(2854,16706,$n$1 Enoch 15:10 — *[As for the spirits of heaven, in heaven shall be their dwelling, but as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling.]* Enoch's own earlier vision identifies the form-shifting spirits of 19:1 as the earth-bound evil spirits sprung from the dead giants.$n$),
(2854,16705,$n$1 Enoch 15:12 — *And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.* This is the defiling and leading-astray of mankind that Uriel shows Enoch in 19:1, the same spirits at work.$n$),
(2855,16701,$n$1 Enoch 16:3 — *“You have been in heaven, but all the mysteries had not yet been revealed to you, and you knew worthless ones, and these in the hardness of your hearts you have made known to the women, and through these mysteries women and men work much evil on earth."* Enoch's own word explains why the women of 19:2 become agents of destruction: the Watchers taught them the forbidden mysteries.$n$),
(2857,16721,$n$1 Enoch 40:9 — *And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’* Enoch names Michael first again among the archangels, the same honoured prince of 1 Enoch 20:5.$n$),
(2859,16716,$n$1 Enoch 18:14 — *The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.* Raguel's vengeance on the world of the luminaries in 1 Enoch 20:4 is the binding of the transgressing stars Enoch sees imprisoned one chapter later.$n$),
(2859,16715,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* The luminaries Raguel takes vengeance on in 1 Enoch 20:4 are these stars that broke their appointed order.$n$),
(2860,16739,$n$1 Enoch 18:13–14 — *I saw there seven stars like great burning mountains, and to me, when I inquired regarding them, The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.* Enoch's earlier journey shows the very same seven bound stars and the same prison-of-the-host that he revisits in 21:4-5.$n$),
(2862,16731,$n$1 Enoch 19:1 — *And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* The same Uriel who guides Enoch names the term of this prison: the fallen angels stand here till the great judgement.$n$),
(2863,16751,$n$1 Enoch 18:14 — *The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.* The chapter-21 cell Enoch toured is the same prison of the angels named in Enoch 22:7.$n$),
(2870,16775,$n$1 Enoch 18:8 — *But the middle one reached to heaven like the throne of Elohim (God), of alabaster, and the summit of the throne was of sapphire.* Enoch had already seen this central throne-mountain among the seven on his earlier journey, the same height-excelling middle peak resembling the seat of a throne (24:3).$n$),
(2970,17136,$n$1 Enoch 15:7 — *And therefore I have not appointed wives for you; for as for the spiritual ones of the heaven, in heaven is their dwelling.* Chapter 25 in this parse is a verbatim duplicate of chapter 15; the same word on the origin of evil spirits stands in both places.$n$),
(2992,17235,$n$1 Enoch 72:3 — *And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.* The Astronomical Book opens by repeating this very vision, confirming the twelve portals Enoch first glimpses here in chapter 33.$n$),
(2996,17245,$n$1 Enoch 76:1 — *And at the ends of the earth I saw twelve portals open to all the quarters (of the heaven), from which the winds go forth and blow over the earth.* Enoch's own Luminaries section widens chapter 34's three-per-quarter gates into the twelve portals of the winds.$n$),
(2999,17258,$n$1 Enoch 34:2 — *And here I saw three portals of heaven open in the heaven: through each of them proceed north winds: when they blow there is cold, hail, frost, snow, dew, and rain.* The journey of chapter 34 already met the west portals; chapter 35:1 returns to describe them, marking them small such as he had seen in the east.$n$),
(3002,17270,$n$1 Enoch 77:1 — *And the first quarter is called the east, because it is the first: and the second, the south, because the El Elyon (Most High) will descend there, yea, there in quite a special sense will He who is blessed for ever descend.* Enoch's own Luminaries book names the same four quarters he surveys here, confirming one consistent cosmology across the books.$n$),
(3025,17356,$n$*This is the spirit which went forth from Abel ... he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed* (1 Enoch 22:7) — the cry of Genesis 4:10 given a seed-war shape, running till the wicked seed is cut off.$n$),
(3032,17390,$n$*as for the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling* (1 Enoch 15:10) — the residue of the *men of renown* (Genesis 6:4): the giants' spirits left dwelling on the earth.$n$),
(3032,17391,$n$*the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy... and cause trouble* (1 Enoch 15:11) — the demonic legacy of the Nephilim, the seed-war's cosmic front continuing after the flesh has fallen.$n$),
(3170,17913,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* Enoch's first parable already declared the 'judgement upon all' that chapter 37 reopens (1 Enoch 37:9).$n$),
(3173,17936,$n$1 Enoch 45:3 — *On that day Mine Elect One shall sit on the throne of glory And shall try their works, And their places of rest shall be innumerable. And their souls shall grow strong within them when they see Mine elect ones, And those who have called upon My glorious name:* Enoch's own parables name the same enthronement, the Elect One on the throne of glory trying works, that 38:10 declares.$n$),
(3175,17929,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* Enoch's parables name the Son of Adam as the One who unseats the kings and mighty that 38:6 sees cast down from their thrones.$n$),
(3178,17953,$n$1 Enoch 45:3 — *On that day Mine Elect One shall sit on the throne of glory And shall try their works, And their places of rest shall be innumerable. And their souls shall grow strong within them when they see Mine elect ones, And those who have called upon My glorious name:* The same Elect One on the same throne of glory; what He speaks from it in 1 Enoch 39:5 He executes here as judgement of works.$n$),
(3188,17995,$n$1 Enoch 60:11 — *And the other angel who went with me and showed me what was hidden told me what is first and last in the heaven in the height, and beneath the earth in the depth, and at the ends of the heaven, and on the foundation of the heaven.* Enoch's own Parables expand the balance of 41:1, showing the weighing reckoned spirit by spirit beside the chambers of the winds.$n$),
(3203,18047,$n$1 Enoch 72:1 — *The book of the courses of the luminaries of the heaven, the relations of each, according to their classes, their dominion and their seasons, according to their names and places of origin, and according to their months, which Uriel, the holy angel, who was with me, who is their guide, showed me; and he showed me all their laws exactly as they are, and how it is with regard to all the years of the world and unto eternity, till the new creation is accomplished which dureth till eternity.* — the Luminaries book unfolds in detail the chambers Enoch only glimpses in 44:1.$n$),
(3430,18922,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* The Father places the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge and weigh deeds — the same throne-of-glory judgement 45:3 announces.$n$),
(3437,18955,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — *And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’* Parables restates 46:3 — the same Son of Adam over whom righteousness abides, never forsaken by the Head of Days.$n$),
(3446,18995,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* The Son of Adam named in 48:2 is the Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge.$n$),
(3452,19007,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* The office of judging the secret things named in 49:4 is the throne-of-glory judgement given here.$n$),
(3453,19003,$n$1 Enoch 51:1 — *And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* Enoch's own ch51 makes the Elect One the agent of resurrection — the rising of the righteous who fell asleep in Him.$n$),
(3457,19023,$n$1 Enoch 108:3 — *And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* Enoch's own books show the inverse of 50:4's verdict: the unrepentant blotted out, while the elect's names stand.$n$),
(3458,19019,$n$1 Enoch 51:1 — *And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* Enoch's own next chapter sets the righteous judgement of 50:4 after the resurrection, when the Elect One arises to judge.$n$),
(3461,19054,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* Enoch's own parallel: the Father places the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge, the same enthronement as 51:3.$n$),
(3674,19847,$n$1 Enoch 53:1 — *There mine eyes saw a deep valley with open mouths, and all who dwell on the earth and sea and islands shall bring to him gifts and presents and tokens of homage, but that deep valley shall not become full.* The very next vision shows the same deep valley, now open-mouthed for judgment, the continuation of the leveled mountains of chapter 52.$n$),
(3676,19866,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* The named Son of Adam executes the very judgement on the kings and mighty for whom the instruments are prepared in 53:6.$n$),
(3684,19885,$n$1 Enoch 61:8 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* Enoch repeats the very enthronement of 55:4 — the Father seats the Formed Son to judge.$n$),
(3685,19917,$n$1 Enoch 53:3 — *For I saw all the angels of punishment abiding (there) and preparing all the instruments of Satan.* The same hosts of punishing angels Enoch saw being readied in ch53 now go forth bearing their scourges and chains in 56:1.$n$),
(3699,19941,$n$1 Enoch 60:11 — *And the other angel who went with me and showed me what was hidden told me what is first and last in the heaven in the height, and beneath the earth in the depth, and at the ends of the heaven, and on the foundation of the heaven.* The next chapter unfolds the same weighed order of winds and moon-lights Enoch glimpses here in their faithful orbit.$n$),
(3706,19972,$n$1 Enoch 62:2 — *And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.* The next chapter repeats the enthronement and adds what is poured out on him: the spirit of righteousness, and the word of his mouth that slays the sinners.$n$),
(4033,21272,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* The Son of Adam who drives the sinners from the earth (63:6) is the same One seen a chapter before breaking the teeth of the sinners.$n$),
(4033,21271,$n$1 Enoch 46:5 — *[And he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms] Because they do not extol and praise Him, Nor humbly acknowledge whence the kingdom was bestowed upon them.* The kings who perish for ever (63:9) are those put down for refusing to acknowledge the One from whom their kingdom was bestowed.$n$),
(4040,21304,$n$1 Enoch 10:20 — *And cleanse thou the earth from all oppression, and from all unrighteousness, and from all sin, and from all godlessness: and all the uncleanness that is wrought upon the earth destroy from off the earth.* Enoch's word to Noah in 65:12 repeats the cleansing he was earlier commanded to announce over the post-Flood earth.$n$),
(4061,21407,$n$1 Enoch 71:1 — *And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* Chapter 71 reopens and re-seals the very ascent of 70:1 — the visionary repetition marking the climax of the Parables.$n$),
(4064,21397,$n$1 Enoch 61:4 — *The elect shall begin to dwell with the elect, And those are the measures which shall be given to faith And which shall strengthen righteousness.* The same gathering of the elect and righteous Enoch beheld earlier in the Parables, now seen dwelling in their heavenly place in 71:7.$n$),
(4359,22503,$n$1 Enoch 82:5 — *Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.* Those who walk in the 364-day order of 74:13 are the righteous of 82:4; those who sin in the reckoning are the men of 82:5, at fault, not reckoning the four days. The order has two sides, and Enoch names both.$n$),
(4359,22500,$n$1 Enoch 82:4 — *Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.* To complete the years *with righteousness* (74:13) is to walk as the righteous of this blessing walk — not sinning as the sinners in the reckoning of their days.$n$),
(4368,22534,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* The Astronomical Book repeats word for word the earlier vision of the prison of the transgressing stars.$n$),
(4370,22550,$n$1 Enoch 82:5 — *Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.* Enoch's own luminary book fixes the same solar reckoning Enoch 78:4 gives to the sun's revolution.$n$),
(4370,22549,$n$1 Enoch 74:11 — *And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.* The thirty days the moon falls behind the sun and stars in five years is the lunar shortfall 78:4–5 records; the solar order leads, the moon lags.$n$),
(4375,22559,$n$1 Enoch 74:11 — *And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.* The same lag of the moon behind the sun Enoch already gave in the courses of the luminaries — the solar year is the primary order.$n$),
(4384,22580,$n$1 Enoch 82:7 — *And the account thereof is accurate and the recorded reckoning thereof exact; for the luminaries, and months and festivals, and years and days, has Uriel shown and revealed to me, to whom Yahuah (Lord) of the whole creation of the world hath subjected the host of heaven.* The charge to preserve and not alter (81:10) rests on this: the reckoning Uriel showed is accurate and exact, and the host of heaven is subject to Yahuah (Lord). What is exact is not to be amended.$n$),
(4384,22579,$n$1 Enoch 82:4 — *Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.* The blessing on those who keep the commandments (81:10) is given its calendar here: blessed are those who do not sin in the reckoning of their days. Keeping the commandments includes keeping the count.$n$),
(4716,23826,$n$1 Enoch 9:4 — *And they said to Yahuah (Lord) of the ages: ‘Lord of lords, Elohim (God) of gods, King of kings, and Elohim (God) of the ages, the throne of Thy glory (standeth) unto all the generations of the ages, and Thy name holy and glorious and blessed unto all the ages!* the angels' first cry against the Watchers names the same everlasting throne Enoch blesses here.$n$),
(5109,25314,$n$1 Enoch 96:5 — *Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.* The very violence and oppression of Enoch's wicked path (93:6) is the woe the next chapter sentences.$n$),
(5127,25419,$n$1 Enoch 97:8 — *Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.* Enoch's earlier woe names the same gold-and-silver pride that 98:2 dresses in royal purple.$n$),
(5129,25412,$n$1 Enoch 104:7 — *And, although ye sinners say: “All our sins shall not be searched out and be written down,” nevertheless they shall write down all your sins every day.* What 98:7 warns — that every sin is seen in heaven — 104:7 confirms against the sinners' own denial: all of it is written down, every day.$n$),
(5147,25490,$n$1 Enoch 108:3 — *And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* Enoch's own closing names what 103:8 promises the righteous will never suffer — the blotting falls only on the sinner.$n$),
(5152,25507,$n$1 Enoch 108:3 — *And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* Enoch's own closing book confirms the asymmetry: the wicked are blotted out, while the righteous name of 104:8 endures.$n$),
(5166,25549,$n$1 Enoch 103:5 — *Woe to you, ye sinners, when ye have died, If ye die in the wealth of your sins, And those who are like you say regarding you: “Blessed are the sinners: they have seen all their days.* Enoch's woe over the sinners who die in their sins is the woe the closing chapter (108) carries to its end.$n$),
(5172,25566,$n$1 Enoch 81:1 — *And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’* The tables of the divisions Jubilees 1:29 describes are the same heavenly tablets Enoch was shown — the pre-written record of all the years.$n$),
(5174,25598,$n$1 Enoch 41:3 — *And there mine eyes saw the secrets of the lightning and of the thunder, and the secrets of the winds, how they are divided to blow over the earth, and the secrets of the clouds and dew, and there I saw from whence they proceed in that place and from whence they saturate the dusty earth.* The same governed winds, clouds, lightning and thunder that Jubilees 2:2 assigns to angelic spirits.$n$),
(5174,25597,$n$1 Enoch 41:4 — *And there I saw closed chambers out of which the winds are divided, the chamber of the hail and winds, the chamber of the mist, and of the clouds, and the cloud thereof hovers over the earth from the beginning of the world.* The chambers of hail and mist match Jubilees 2:2's angels of snow, hail and hoar frost.$n$),
(5175,25593,$n$1 Enoch 72:1 — *The book of the courses of the luminaries of the heaven, the relations of each, according to their classes, their dominion and their seasons, according to their names and places of origin, and according to their months, which Uriel, the holy angel, who was with me, who is their guide, showed me; and he showed me all their laws exactly as they are, and how it is with regard to all the years of the world and unto eternity, till the new creation is accomplished which dureth till eternity.* The same luminaries Jubilees 2:9 makes the sign for seasons and feasts govern Enoch's calendar of the years.$n$),
(5188,25629,$n$1 Enoch 13:8 — *And behold a dream came to me, and visions fell down upon me, and I saw visions of chastisement, and a voice came bidding (me) I to tell it to the sons of heaven, and reprimand them.* The vision-and-witness commission of Jubilees 4:23 unfolds in the parallel Enoch apparatus.$n$),
(5189,25627,$n$1 Enoch 6:6 — *And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* The 1 Enoch apparatus fixes the Watchers' descent to the same generation of Jared that Jubilees 4:15 names.$n$),
(5201,25690,$n$1 Enoch 82:5 — *Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.* Enoch's luminary order names the exact 364-day reckoning Jubilees 6:32 commands Israel to observe.$n$),
(5201,25691,$n$1 Enoch 74:12 — *And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.* The same 364-day order, completed *with perfect justice,* that Jubilees 6:32 says must not disturb its feasts.$n$),
(5201,25692,$n$1 Enoch 82:5 — *Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.* Jubilees 6:37 names the disturbing of the order outright — feasts confounded, the unclean day made holy. Enoch names its root: men at fault who do not reckon the four intercalary days, and so lose the year.$n$),
(5208,25718,$n$1 Enoch 7:6 — *Then the earth laid accusation against the lawless ones.* the live Enoch testimony — the *seventh in his generation* whose commandment Jubilees 7:39 says Enoch handed to his sons' sons.$n$),
(5210,25726,$n$1 Enoch 8:2 — *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* The Watchers' star-omens Kainam transcribes in Jubilees 8:3 are the very teaching 1 Enoch names by name.$n$),
(5212,25721,$n$1 Enoch 26:1 — *And I went from thence to the middle of the earth, and I saw a blessed place in which there were trees with branches abiding and blooming [of a dismembered tree].* Enoch's vision of the middle of the earth — the holy mountain and Zion — is the same centre Jubilees 8:18 sets at the navel of the world.$n$),
(5264,25927,$n$1 Enoch 15:12 — *And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.* Enoch foretold the very assault Noah's sons report in Jubilees 10:2 — the spirits rising up to lead astray and slay the sons of men.$n$),
(5276,25953,$n$1 Enoch 19:1 — *And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* The evil spirits Abram prays to be delivered from in Jubilees 12:17 are the Watcher-spirits of the live 1 Enoch apparatus, who lead mankind astray into demon-worship.$n$),
(5287,25985,$n$1 Enoch 81:1 — *And he said unto me: ‘Observe, Enoch, these heavenly tablets, And read what is written thereon, And mark every individual fact.’* The four-hundred-year word of Jubilees 14:13 is read off the same heavenly tablets Enoch is shown — the history pre-written.$n$),
(6179,29120,$n$1 Enoch 39:3 — *And in those days a whirlwind carried me off from the earth, And set me down at the end of the heavens.* The whirlwind that carried Enoch off from the earth is the whirlwind Jasher 3:36 gives for his ascent, told here by Enoch himself.$n$),
(6179,29122,$n$1 Enoch 71:1 — *And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* the heavenly translation Jasher 3:36 records, even the snow Jasher 3:38 finds at the place of his ascent.$n$),
(6194,29177,$n$1 Enoch 89:3 — *And I saw again, and behold fountains were opened on the surface of that great enclosure, and that water began to swell and rise upon the surface, and I saw that enclosure till all its surface was covered with water.* Enoch's Animal Apocalypse sees the same fountains opened that Jasher 6:14 names, the flood-vision live beside it.$n$),
(9014,39145,$n$1 Enoch 103:4 — *And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.* The watcher-book and Wisdom of Solomon 3:1 speak one tongue: the righteous souls are kept, lit, and given peace in Yahuah's hand.$n$),
(9024,39175,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* The mighty whom the Son of Adam casts down are the very ones who, in Wisdom of Solomon 5:3, repent and groan when they see the righteous exalted.$n$),
(9024,39174,$n$1 Enoch 62:5 — *And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.* The fools who accounted his life madness (Wisdom of Solomon 5:4) are the kings whose faces fall when they at last behold him enthroned.$n$),
(10306,43693,$n$1 Enoch 71:5 — *And he translated my spirit into the heaven of heavens, And I saw there as it were a structure built of crystals, And between those crystals tongues of living fire.* Enoch's own book unfolds the translation Sirach 49:14 remembers, his spirit carried up to the heaven of heavens.$n$),
(10874,45459,$n$1 Enoch 18:4 — *I saw the winds of heaven which turn and bring the circumference of the sun and all the stars to their setting.* The sight of the angelic host that Adam lost outside the garden is exactly what Enoch, walking with Elohim, was caught up to behold.$n$),
(10874,45458,$n$1 Enoch 14:18 — *And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* Adam's lost vision of the praising angels was a vision of this same throne-room that Enoch is shown.$n$),
(10904,45562,$n$*And I saw the chambers of the sun and moon, whence they proceed and whither they come again, and their glorious return, and how one is superior to the other, and their stately orbit, and how they do not leave their orbit, and they add nothing to their orbit and they take nothing from it, and they keep faith with each other, in accordance with the oath by which they are bound together.* (1 Enoch 41:5). 1 Enoch 41:5 --  Enoch shows the sun as an ordered servant kept under oath, not the god Adam dreaded in 16:3.$n$),
(10962,45738,$n$1 Enoch 40:9 — *And he said to me: ‘This first is Michael, the merciful and long- suffering: and the second, who is set over all the diseases and all the wounds of the children of men, is Raphael: and the third, who is set over all the powers, is Gabriel: and the fourth, who is set over the repentance unto hope of those who inherit eternal life, is named Phanuel.’* The same three named angels who bear Adam's tokens in 1 Adam and Eve 31:5 stand named together among the four faces of the throne.$n$),
(11024,45942,$n$1 Enoch 69:6 — *And the third was named Gâdreêl: he it is who showed the children of men all the blows of death, and he led astray Eve, and showed [the weapons of death to the sons of men] the shield and the coat of mail, and the sword for battle, and all the weapons of death to the children of men.* The same envy that now plots Adam's death in 1 Adam and Eve 47:7 first led Eve astray and brought the blows of death into the world.$n$),
(11049,46048,$n$1 Enoch 24:4 — *And amongst them was a tree such as I had never yet smelt, neither was any amongst them nor were others like it: it had a fragrance beyond all fragrance, and its leaves and blooms and wood wither not for ever: and its fruit is beautiful, and its fruit resembles the dates of a palm.* The living tree behind the sword in 1 Adam and Eve 54:4 is this fragrant tree Enoch was shown — the tree no mortal may touch until the great judgement, when it is given to the righteous (1 Enoch 25:4–5).$n$),
(11071,46116,$n$1 Enoch 8:2 — *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* The deceiver whose hollow promise is unmasked in 1-adam-eve 59:6 is the same liar whose deceit leads the whole earth astray into corruption.$n$),
(11162,46438,$n$1 Enoch 19:1 — *And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* The many forms Satan takes to destroy Adam's soul in 2 Adam & Eve 3:15 are the same shape-shifting by which the fallen spirits defile mankind and are worshipped as gods.$n$),
(11242,46715,$n$1 Enoch 6:6 — *And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* The descent from the holy mountain into sin (22:10) is mirrored by the Watchers' own descent in the days of Jared in Enoch's book.$n$),
(11788,48751,$n$1 Enoch 19:3 — *And I, Enoch, alone saw the vision, the ends of all things: and no man shall see as I have seen.* As Enoch alone saw the vision of the ends of all things, so Abraham is fed only by the angel's speech, sustained by the sight he is about to be given.$n$),
(11792,48743,$n$1 Enoch 14:8 — *And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.* As Enoch was lifted by the winds and borne into heaven, so the angel bears Abraham up on the wings of the bird to be shown heaven and earth.$n$),
(11799,48775,$n$1 Enoch 8:2 — *And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.* The Watchers' stolen lore of constellations and clouds is exactly the 'stars and clouds' Abraham binds to Azazel's portion in 14:4.$n$),
(11804,48786,$n$1 Enoch 14:8 — *And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.* Abraham too is borne up as with many winds to the borders of the flaming fire (Apocalypse of Abraham 15:4); the wind-borne ascent is the shared pattern of the prophets caught up to heaven.$n$),
(11815,48830,$n$1 Enoch 40:2 — *And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.* Enoch too saw four presences encircling the throne of glory, the same fourfold company Abraham beholds round the throne of fire.$n$),
(11817,48824,$n$1 Enoch 14:8 — *And the vision was shown to me thus: Behold, in the vision clouds invited me and a mist summoned me, and the course of the stars and the lightnings sped and hastened me, and the winds in the vision caused me to fly and lifted me upward, and bore me into heaven.* Enoch too was lifted up by the winds and borne into heaven to behold the throne, the throne of fire Abraham sees in his own ascent.$n$),
(11818,48821,$n$1 Enoch 40:3 — *And I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (Lord) of glory.* Enoch likewise heard the four presences uttering praise before the throne of glory, the same song of peace Abraham hears taught by Yahoel.$n$),
(11822,48839,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* Abraham's powers of the stars under command match Enoch's host bound to their commandment and judged when they fail to keep it (Apocalypse of Abraham 19:9).$n$),
(11828,48867,$n$1 Enoch 60:7 — *And on that day were two monsters parted, a female monster named Leviathan, to dwell in the abysses of the ocean over the fountains of the waters.* The Leviathan in his deep camping-ground that Abraham beholds is Enoch's Leviathan dwelling in the abysses of the waters.$n$),
(11865,48977,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.* The plagues prepared for the heathen in Apocalypse of Abraham 30:3 are this same judgment Enoch foresaw upon all the ungodly.$n$),
(11957,49285,$n$1 Enoch 14:18 — *And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* Enoch's ascent to the lofty throne and the Glory none of flesh could behold is the elder pattern of Isaiah's angel from the seventh heaven (6:13) — it ain't new.$n$),
(11986,49384,$n$1 Enoch 14:18 — *And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.* Enoch too was brought before the lofty throne whose Glory none of flesh could behold — it ain't new.$n$),
(12181,50233,$n$1 Enoch 15:12 — *these spirits shall rise up against the children of men* the very spirit-war Paul names; *against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places* (Ephesians 6:12).$n$),
(12607,52065,$n$*I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.* (1 Enoch 104:1). *Whose names are in the book of life* (Philippians 4:3). Enoch swears to the righteous that their names are written before the glory of the Great One. Paul's fellow-labourers are written there; the writing was done in heaven, and the labour on earth reveals it.$n$),
(13335,55120,$n$1 Enoch 71:1 — *And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.* The uppermost dwellings this book promises Enoch will behold are the heavens the older Enoch book already says his spirit was translated into — a self-witness across the two books.$n$),
(13352,55165,$n$1 Enoch 72:3 — *And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.* The six gates of the sun Enoch measures here are the six portals his own Astronomical Book had already numbered.$n$),
(13353,55168,$n$1 Enoch 72:6 — *In this way he rises in the first month in the great portal, which is the fourth [those six portals in the east].* The sun's gates that 2 Enoch 14:2 counts are the portals Enoch's own Astronomical Book numbers — the great portal, the fourth, where the sun rises in the first month.$n$),
(13356,55179,$n$1 Enoch 74:2 — *And all these Uriel, the holy angel who is the leader of them all, showed to me, and their positions, and I wrote down their positions as he showed them to me, and I wrote down their months as they were, and the appearance of their lights till fifteen days were accomplished.* The moon's reckoning through its gates, written down to the fifteenth day, is the lunar course Enoch's own Astronomical Book had already set down through the portals.$n$),
(13357,55177,$n$1 Enoch 74:11 — *And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.* The moon falling thirty days behind the sun in five years is the very deficiency Enoch's own Astronomical Book reckoned.$n$),
(13359,55189,$n$1 Enoch 6:6 — *And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* The descent to the place Ermon and the breaking of their vows on the hill is the very rebellion Enoch's own book names on Mount Hermon.$n$),
(13362,55196,$n$1 Enoch 61:10 — *And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, and the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubin, Seraphin and Ophannin, and all the angels of power, and all the angels of principalities, and the Elect One, and the other powers on the earth (and) over the water.* The cherubim, seraphim, and ordered powers of 2 Enoch 20:1 are the same summoned host the elder Enoch names before the throne of glory.$n$),
(13374,55244,$n$1 Enoch 69:16 — *And these are the secrets of this oath... And they are strong through his oath: And the heaven was suspended before the world was created, And for ever.* The hosts standing in their fiery order rest on the same created foundation 1 Enoch confesses, suspended by Him before the world was.$n$),
(13375,55238,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.* 1 Enoch's bound transgressor-host is the same rebellion in heaven 2 Enoch sees thrown down.$n$),
(13387,55283,$n$1 Enoch 81:6 — *One year we will leave thee with thy son, till thou givest thy (last) commands, that thou mayst teach thy children and record (it) for them, and testify to all thy children; and in the second year they shall take thee from their midst.* The year left to Enoch to teach his children and record it for them is the charge behind the books of Enoch's handwriting a later generation reads in 2 Enoch 35:2.$n$),
(13395,55302,$n$1 Enoch 81:2 — *And I observed the heavenly tablets, and read everything which was written (thereon) and understood everything, and read the book of all the deeds of mankind, and of all the children of flesh that shall be upon the earth to the remotest generations.* The works and sentences Enoch writes down in 2 Enoch 40:11 are the works of men he read on the heavenly tablets in his own book.$n$),
(13412,55362,$n$1 Enoch 98:7 — *And do not think in your spirit nor say in your heart that ye do not know and that ye do not see that every sin is every day recorded in heaven in the presence of the El Elyon (Most High).* The record kept so that none is hidden (2 Enoch 50:1) is the daily recording of every sin in heaven that Enoch's first book already warns of.$n$),
(13442,55443,$n$1 Enoch 71:2 — *And I saw two streams of fire, And the light of that fire shone like hyacinth, And I fell on my face before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The taking of Enoch up to where Yahuah is in 2 Enoch 67:1 is the seizing and lifting up by Michael that Enoch's own earlier vision recounts.$n$),
(13694,56509,$n$*But ye—ye have not been steadfast, nor done the commandments of Yahuah (Lord), But ye have turned away and spoken proud and hard words With your impure mouths against His greatness. Oh, ye hard-hearted, ye shall find no peace.* (1 Enoch 5:4). *Which delivered us from the wrath to come* (1 Thessalonians 1:10). Enoch names who the wrath is for: the hard-hearted who have not done the commandments of Yahuah (Lord) and shall find no peace. The Thessalonians are delivered from that, not because wrath is cancelled, but because they are not the hard-hearted; the next verse (1 Enoch 1:8) gives the righteous their peace.$n$),
(13699,56538,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all* the library's coming-with-the-saints prophecy, the word behind hearts stablished *at the coming of our Lord... with all his saints* (1 Thessalonians 3:13).$n$),
(13706,56571,$n$*And there shall be a light that never endeth, And to a limit (lit. ‘number’) of days they shall not come, For the darkness shall first have been destroyed, [And the light established before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits] And the light of uprightness established for ever before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 58:6). *Ye are all the children of light, and the children of the day: we are not of the night, nor of darkness* (1 Thessalonians 5:5). Enoch saw the division made final: the darkness first destroyed, and a light that never ends established before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The children of the day inherit that light; the night they are not of is the darkness that is destroyed.$n$),
(13709,56589,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly* the library's same coming; the mighty angels attend him, the holy ones are the seed of promise coming with him, and the judgment is the vengeance of 2 Thessalonians 1:7-8.$n$),
(13730,56650,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *Ask of me, and I shall give thee the heathen for thine inheritance* (Psalm 2:8). The King who asks is the Elect One Enoch saw placed on the throne of glory by Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. The inheritance is given to the one who is seated.$n$),
(13730,56651,$n$*this Son of Adam... Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats... And break the teeth of the sinners* (1 Enoch 46:4) — the inheritance of 2:8 carries the judgment of the raging kings (2:2) before the enthroned Son of Adam.$n$),
(13730,56652,$n$*In those days shall the mighty and the kings who possess the earth implore (Him) to grant them a little respite from His angels of punishment to whom they were delivered, that they might fall down and worship before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, and confess their sins before Him.* (1 Enoch 63:1). *Why do the heathen rage... The kings of the earth set themselves* (Psalm 2:1–2). Enoch saw where the raging ends: the mighty and the kings imploring for a little respite from the angels of punishment, that they might fall down and confess. He that sits in the heavens laughs (Psalm 2:4).$n$),
(13867,57163,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). The restored witness shows the same enthronement as *Sit thou at my right hand* (Psalm 110:1): the Head of Days (the Father) sets the Elect One on the throne of glory to judge — the chosen One seated by the Most High's own act, the Formed One given the seat of rule and judgement.$n$),
(13867,57164,$n$*This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him* (1 Enoch 71:14) — the enthroned One named the Son of Adam: of Adam's seed yet seated to judge, the paradox of 110:1.$n$),
(13944,57410,$n$*Yahuah (God) of Spirits seated the Elect One on the throne of His glory... he is the Chosen One before Yahuah (God) of Spirits* (1 Enoch 61:8) — the King to whom *all nations shall serve* (72:11) is the Elect One enthroned to judge.$n$),
(13944,57409,$n$*this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats... And break the teeth of the sinners* (1 Enoch 46:4) — the *all kings shall fall down* (72:11) carries the abasing of the proud before the Son of Adam.$n$),
(13944,57408,$n$*he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms Because they do not extol and praise Him* (1 Enoch 46:5) — those who will not *fall down before him... serve him* (72:11) are cast from their seats; the nations that serve are blessed.$n$),
(14531,59357,$n$*He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated* (1 Enoch 18:16) — the fallen host bound until judgement, the prison Peter names (1 Peter 3:19).$n$),
(14531,59358,$n$*this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven* (1 Enoch 18:14) — the prison house of the transgressing angels, the spirits in prison (1 Peter 3:19).$n$),
(14723,59997,$n$1 Enoch 90:29 — *And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.* The house the Lord shall choose, named from the book of Enoch, is the new house Enoch saw the Lord gather His own into.$n$),
(14802,60223,$n$*And after that in the sixth week all who live in it shall be blinded, And the hearts of all of them shall godlessly forsake wisdom. And in it a man shall ascend; And at its close the house of dominion shall be burnt with fire, And the whole race of the chosen root shall be dispersed.* (1 Enoch 93:8). 1 Enoch 91 —  — "I have read in the writing of Enoch that ye yourselves also shall depart from Yahuah" reaches for the very book of Enoch that foretells the generation of apostasy (self-link).$n$),
(15478,62554,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 — *And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all... And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed* the very verse Jude quotes by name (Jude 1:14-15). SELF-LINK into the live 1 Enoch ch1 thread.$n$),
(15484,62589,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — *the stars which... have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (God)... because they did not come forth at their appointed times* bound in the prison; the wandering stars (Jude 1:13).$n$),
(16568,66493,$n$★ *I heard the voices of those four presences as they uttered praises before Yahuah (God) of glory* (1 Enoch 40:3) — the holy ones crying *Holy, holy, holy* (Isaiah 6:3) seen at the throne of glory in the restored witness.$n$),
(16568,66492,$n$*the first voice blesses Yahuah (God) of Spirits for ever and ever* (1 Enoch 40:4) — the whole earth *full of his glory* (Isaiah 6:3) is the unending blessing the holy ones pour before the throne.$n$),
(16569,66489,$n$*the middle one reached to heaven, like the throne of Yahuah (God)... the top of the throne was of sapphire* (1 Enoch 14:18) — the throne *high and lifted up* (Isaiah 6:1) framed in Enoch's own throne-vision.$n$),
(16569,66488,$n$*And I saw a flaming fire... a mountain whose summit reached to heaven* (1 Enoch 14:20) — the Glory whose *train filled the temple* (Isaiah 6:1) is the same fire-wrapped Presence none could look upon.$n$),
(16936,67773,$n$★★ *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him* (1 Enoch 71:14) — the *righteous servant* who shall *justify many* (Isaiah 53:11), the Elect One revealed.$n$),
(16936,67774,$n$★★ *And this Son of Adam... Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats... And break the teeth of the sinners* (1 Enoch 46:4) — the servant *numbered with the transgressors* (Isaiah 53:12) exalted to judge; suffering servant and enthroned Elect One are one Formed Son.$n$),
(17361,69401,$n$1 Enoch 20:5 — *Michael, one of the holy angels, to wit, he that is set over the best part of mankind and over chaos.* Michael, named first to bury Adam, is the chief of the holy angels in the Watcher-tradition's own roster.$n$),
(17463,69782,$n$★ *He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all... to convict all flesh* (1 Enoch 1:9) — *by fire... will Yahuah (LORD) plead with all flesh* (Isaiah 66:16); the library's witness to the fiery advent (the verse Jude quotes by name).$n$),
(17463,69783,$n$*And I will give them over into the hands of Mine elect: As straw in the fire so shall they burn before the face of the holy: As lead in the water shall they sink before the face of the righteous, And no trace of them shall any more be found.* (1 Enoch 48:9). *By fire and by his sword will Yahuah (the LORD) plead with all flesh* (Isaiah 66:16); *neither shall their fire be quenched* (Isaiah 66:24). Enoch sees the sinners given into the hands of the elect, burning as straw before the face of the holy, sinking as lead before the face of the righteous. The fire that closes Isaiah is the fire of the Parables.$n$),
(19369,77220,$n$★★ *He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones* (1 Enoch 1:9) — 68:17's thousands are angels, the chariotry of the coming One; Enoch's holy ones are another company, the seed of promise gathered and coming with him (Zechariah 14:5).$n$),
(20119,80341,$n$★ *He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all* (1 Enoch 1:9) — the judgment heard from heaven (76:8) seen coming down upon all the ungodly.$n$),
(21573,86012,$n$★★★ *the stars which... have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (God)... because they did not come forth at their appointed times* (1 Enoch 18:15) — the *host of the high ones that are on high* (Isaiah 24:21) named: the rebel stars that broke command.$n$),
(21573,86011,$n$★★★ *He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated* (1 Enoch 18:16) — exactly *shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited* (Isaiah 24:22); bound till the day of visitation.$n$),
(21573,86006,$n$★ *He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated* (1 Enoch 18:16) — the *punish*-ing of the high host (Isaiah 24:21) is their binding in the abyss till judgment.$n$),
(22618,90046,$n$★ *Yahuah (God) of Spirits... seated him on the throne of His glory* (1 Enoch 61:8) — the Father seats the Formed Son; the One reigning in 93:1 is enthroned BY the Most High.$n$),
(28854,114988,$n$1 Enoch 40:3 — the four presences *uttered praises before Yahuah (God) of glory* — the praise already sounding above.$n$),
(30058,120191,$n$★★ *the throne... of stibium, and the top of the throne was of sapphire... a flaming fire* (1 Enoch 14:18-16) — Enoch sees the fiery throne of the Most High, twin to *his throne was like the fiery flame* (Daniel 7:9).$n$),
(30207,120843,$n$★ *this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats* (1 Enoch 46:4) — the pierced One they look upon is the Son of Adam beheld in the day of His appearing.$n$),
(30215,120873,$n$★ *He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all* (1 Enoch 1:9) — the restored witness Jude quotes; the same day-of-Yahuah coming with the holy ones of Zechariah 14:5.$n$),
(30427,121870,$n$1 Enoch 15:10 — *the spirits of the earth which were born upon the earth, on the earth shall be their dwelling* — where the unclean spirits belong.$n$),
(30427,121871,$n$1 Enoch 15:11 — *the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy... and work destruction on the earth* — their very trade in the tombs.$n$),
(30427,121872,$n$1 Enoch 16:1 — *until the day of the consummation, the great judgement* — why they cry *art thou come... before the time?*$n$),
(30457,122007,$n$*And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.* (1 Enoch 108:3). Malachi's spared jewels — *I will spare them, as a man spareth his own son that serveth him* (Malachi 3:17) — stand against those whose *names shall be blotted out of the book of life*. The book of remembrance keeps the faithful; the wicked are blotted out.$n$),
(30607,122747,$n$1 Enoch 16:1 — the unclean spirits are the souls of the dead giants, offspring of the Watchers — the very devils the Son binds.$n$),
(30917,124246,$n$1 Enoch 71:14 — the Son of Adam born unto righteousness, the Head of Days behind him.$n$),
(33633,134196,$n$1 Enoch 15:11 — *the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy* — the library names the unclean spirits: the offspring of the Watchers.$n$),
(33633,134197,$n$1 Enoch 16:1 — they destroy *until the day of the consummation* — yet the Son hands their conquest to twelve men with a staff before that day.$n$),
(33640,134233,$n$1 Enoch 15:11 — *the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy, attack, do battle, and work destruction on the earth.* The library names the foul spirits the Son rebukes — souls gone forth from the slain giants.$n$),
(33640,134234,$n$1 Enoch 16:1 — *...thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement.* They roam until the consummation; the Son's *enter no more into him* is a foretaste of that judgement.$n$),
(33881,135392,$n$1 Enoch 15:11 — *the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy... and cause trouble.* The library names what the spirit that teareth the child is.$n$),
(33881,135393,$n$1 Enoch 16:1 — *thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation... over the Watchers.* The Son rebukes one as a foretaste of the judgment that ends them.$n$),
(33888,135426,$n$*And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.* (1 Enoch 61:8). *That ye may eat and drink at my table in my kingdom, and sit on thrones judging the twelve tribes of Yashar'el (Israel)* (Luke 22:30). The Elect One placed on the throne of glory to judge is the Son of Adam who shares that seat with the twelve.$n$),
(33891,135440,$n$*And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.* (1 Enoch 62:5). *Hereafter shall the Son of Adam sit on the right hand of the power of Elohim (God)* (Luke 22:69). Enoch saw the faces of those who see that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory — terror and pain. The council heard the claim; the vision shows them seeing it kept.$n$),
(33996,135969,$n$1 Enoch 69:27-7 — *Yahuah (God) of Spirits seated the Elect One on the throne of His glory, And he shall judge... This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness.* The Father seats the Son of Adam to judge — exactly John 5:27.$n$),
(34937,140723,$n$1 Enoch 15:10 — the spirits of the earth dwell on the earth. The origin of the *unclean devil*: the disembodied spirits of the giants, offspring of the fallen Watchers.$n$),
(34937,140722,$n$1 Enoch 15:11 — *the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy...* The afflicting spirit Enoch named; it knows its Judge and must obey the Holy One.$n$),
(34942,140747,$n$1 Enoch 15:11 — *the spirits of the giants afflict, oppress, destroy... and work destruction on the earth.* The library names the unclean spirits — the strong man's armoury, now overcome.$n$),
(35907,145066,$n$*Woe to you who devour the might of others... And tread upon the righteous with your might* (1 Enoch 96:5) — heaven marks for woe the trampling power of Job's mighty man (24:22).$n$),
(35907,145067,$n$*Woe to you, ye mighty, Who with might oppress the righteous; For the day of your destruction is coming. In those days many and good days shall come to the righteous—in the day of your judgement.* (1 Enoch 96:8). *They are exalted for a little while, but are gone and brought low* (Job 24:24). Enoch's woe to the mighty who oppress the righteous says the same: the day of their destruction is coming. The might does not keep.$n$),
(37172,150625,$n$1 Enoch 69:17 — through the creating oath the sea was made and the sand set as its bound, which it dare not pass.$n$),
(37175,150635,$n$1 Enoch 18:15 — even the stars are judged for not coming forth at their appointed times; the ordinances are commandment.$n$),
(37459,151942,$n$*And on that day were two monsters parted, a female monster named Leviathan, to dwell in the abysses of the ocean over the fountains of the waters.* (1 Enoch 60:7). The restored witness names the same abyss-monster the LORD reserves:  (1 Enoch 60:7). Job's *Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook?* (Job 41:1) asks of a creature of the deep that man cannot reach — held in the abyss under Yahuah's (God's) hand alone.$n$),
(38640,157298,$n$*reached to heaven, like the throne of Yahuah... the top of the throne was of sapphire* (1 Enoch 14:18) — the restored witness shown the same enthroned Most High Micaiah beheld in the council.$n$),
(40676,165963,$n$1 Enoch 1:9 (extras) — *He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones*: the ten thousands of saints, the verse Jude later quotes by name.$n$);
